INSERT INTO `profiledata_profiles` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `intro`, `tldr`, `conclusion`, `comparison_table`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `image`) VALUES
(2, 'Top 10 Creative Agencies 2025', 'creative-agencies', '<p>In 2026, creative agencies have become important partners for companies that want to stand out and connect with people. These agencies mix strong ideas, smart planning, and knowledge of new technology. They help brands get attention in a world full of AI content, fast-changing trends, and many competing messages.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Top agencies today succeed because they specialize. Some focus on personalized digital experiences, others build strong brand identities, and some create high-quality content that feels like entertainment. What makes them different is how well they understand real problems and offer creative solutions that work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This article looks at the agencies leading the industry in 2025. We will highlight those shaping digital design, brand storytelling, creator-led content, and full marketing campaigns. We will also explain how their methods&mdash;like using cultural research and real-time data&mdash;help brands grow and reach the right audience.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In the final section, we offer a simple guide to choosing the best creative agency. This includes checking how they work, how they measure results, how they communicate, and whether their style matches your company&rsquo;s goals. In a fast-changing world, picking the right partner can make a big difference for long-term success.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"color:#2f5496\">How We Choose These Companies</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Selecting the top creative agencies for 2025 requires careful research and a clear system. We look for agencies that deliver strong results, show real creativity, and build trust with their clients. Our method focuses on what truly matters in today&rsquo;s fast-changing creative world.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Market Reputation and Industry Standing</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We begin by studying how each agency is known in the industry. This includes how long they have worked, which brands trust them, and how their ideas influence others. Agencies that show steady growth, confident leadership, and a strong creative voice earn higher positions. Their past projects help us understand the quality and consistency of their work.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Customer Reviews and Client Satisfaction</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Client opinions give us an honest look at how an agency works day to day. We read verified reviews to understand communication, reliability, and the value clients feel they received. We focus mainly on:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>How satisfied clients are with the final results</li>\r\n	<li>How well the agency handles timelines, communication, and unexpected problems</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies with positive, consistent feedback naturally rise in our evaluation.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Innovation and Creative Excellence</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Creative work keeps changing, so we look closely at how each agency adapts. We value agencies that bring new ideas, try new tools, and solve problems in smarter ways. When an agency shows a fresh point of view and stays ahead of trends, it earns special recognition. This is especially important in 2025, when audiences expect more original and meaningful experiences.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Service Quality and Range</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We also examine the strength of each agency&rsquo;s services. This includes their main skills, how experienced their teams are, and whether their projects show clear, high-quality results. Agencies that can deliver strong work across different types of projects&mdash;and do so with a clear process&mdash;score higher in our assessment.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Industry Recognition and Awards</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Professional recognition helps confirm an agency&rsquo;s impact. Awards from respected groups, features in well-known publications, and invitations to speak at industry events all show that an agency&rsquo;s work is valued by experts. We focus on awards from 2024&ndash;2025 to make sure the agency is active, relevant, and competitive today.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#1f3763\">Performance Metrics and Results</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>At the end of the day, real results matter. We look for agencies that can prove the success of their work with clear numbers, such as:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Growth in client results, engagement, or sales</li>\r\n	<li>Strong return on investment supported by case studies and real data</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies that show measurable success earn the highest positions in our ranking.</p>', '<p>The leading creative agencies of 2025 stand out for their mix of strong storytelling, strategic thinking, and modern digital tools. Each agency offers a distinct approach that helps brands stay memorable, relevant, and competitive in a fast-changing market.</p>', '<p>In 2025, creative agencies have become full strategic partners rather than just design teams. The strongest agencies combine creative ideas with data, modern tools and industry knowledge. They offer complete solutions that connect branding, digital strategy, content and technology, helping businesses of all sizes turn creative work into real growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For companies choosing a creative partner, the key is to look beyond portfolio images and focus on strategic thinking, clear processes and proven results. Agencies that stay creative while using new technologies and understanding client goals are the ones shaping the future. These partners help businesses compete and grow in a fast-changing digital world.</p>', '{\"rows\": [{\"Name\": \"MarketBridge\", \"Location\": \"Bethesda, MD\", \"Ideal For\": \"B2B tech, healthcare, and financial companies needing data-driven marketing and sales alignment\"}, {\"Name\": \"Arnold Street Agency\", \"Location\": \"Toronto, Canada\", \"Ideal For\": \"Brands seeking strong storytelling, creative identity, and multi-channel campaigns\"}, {\"Name\": \"Colormatics\", \"Location\": \"New York, NY\", \"Ideal For\": \"Companies needing motion graphics, animation, and visual storytelling to simplify complex ideas\"}, {\"Name\": \"VSA Partners\", \"Location\": \"Chicago, IL\", \"Ideal For\": \"Established brands wanting premium design, branding, and human-centered brand experiences\"}, {\"Name\": \"C42D\", \"Location\": \"New York, NY\", \"Ideal For\": \"Startups or transforming companies needing clear strategy, positioning, and brand identity\"}, {\"Name\": \"Duck.Design\", \"Location\": \"London, UK\", \"Ideal For\": \"Consumer brands and startups wanting bold, playful, high-impact creative design\"}, {\"Name\": \"DD.NYC®\", \"Location\": \"New York, NY\", \"Ideal For\": \"Luxury, fashion, beauty, and lifestyle brands seeking refined, premium branding\"}, {\"Name\": \"5+8\", \"Location\": \"Houston, TX\", \"Ideal For\": \"Regional businesses and brands wanting strong storytelling and Texas market insight\"}, {\"Name\": \"Spire Agency\", \"Location\": \"Dallas, TX\", \"Ideal For\": \"B2B tech companies needing targeted, strategic marketing (SaaS, IT, cybersecurity)\"}, {\"Name\": \"Ankord Media\", \"Location\": \"Beverly Hills, CA\", \"Ideal For\": \"Beauty, fashion, lifestyle, and entertainment brands targeting Gen Z and Millennials via influencer and content marketing\"}], \"columns\": [\"Name\", \"Location\", \"Ideal For\"]}', 'Top Creative Agencies in 2025', 'A deep look at the creative agencies redefining strategy, storytelling, and design in 2025. Explore how top firms blend culture, tech, and creativity to fuel brand growth.', '2025-12-05 13:48:56.079243', '2025-12-19 11:19:31.878801', 'top/top-creative-agencies.jpg'),
(3, 'Top 13 AI Search Monitoring Software for 2026', 'ai-search-monitoring-software', '<p>AI now decides what people see first in search. In 2025, most users get a direct answer from tools like Google SGE, Bing Copilot, Perplexity, or ChatGPT instead of clicking through pages of links. To appear in these answers, a brand must make its information easy for AI to read, trust, and repeat. This requires clear topics, well-defined entities, and content that helps AI connect facts without guessing. If a brand doesn&rsquo;t do this, its competitors will become the sources AI relies on, even if those competitors have weaker traditional SEO.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Because this shift is so big, companies now use advanced platforms built for AI-driven search. These tools show when and how a brand appears inside AI answers, which pages get cited, and what information AI systems think is missing. They also test how different AIs use your data and point out weak spots in structure, clarity, and topical depth. The strongest tools give step-by-step guidance to help brands shape how AI describes them and increase the chances of being chosen as the main source in the answer box.</p>', '<p>AI now decides most search results, and brands must optimize not just for Google but for <strong>ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Bing AI, and SGE</strong>. These tools help companies monitor how AI systems interpret their content, whether they are cited in AI answers, and what improvements increase visibility in AI-generated search.</p>', '<p>AI visibility does not come from one tool. It comes from using the right mix of SEO platforms, AI writing tools, and human expertise.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Modern search rewards content that matches intent, uses strong structure, and covers topics clearly. Tools like SurferSEO, Frase, MarketMuse, and Clearscope help identify what AI systems expect.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>AI writing tools give speed, but they cannot replace human strategy, fact-checking, or expertise. SEO platforms provide the structure and guidance AI tools cannot.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Technical SEO remains essential. Tools like Semrush, Ahrefs, and Screaming Frog ensure the site is fast, crawlable, and indexable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Search engines value helpful and trustworthy content. Quality and originality still decide visibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The best results come from an efficient workflow: research, optimize, create, and track&mdash;all supported by integrated tools</p>', '{\"rows\": [{\"Name\": \"Profound\", \"Pricing\": \"Starts at $299/month\", \"Ideal For\": \"Mid-size and large companies needing visibility in both AI-generated answers and traditional search\"}, {\"Name\": \"Otterly\", \"Pricing\": \"$299/month Starter, $499/month Professional, Enterprise custom plans\", \"Ideal For\": \"Medium and large brands prioritizing visibility inside AI-generated answers across major AI platforms\"}, {\"Name\": \"Peec AI\", \"Pricing\": \"Estimated $99–$299/month depending on tier\", \"Ideal For\": \"Teams adapting to AI-driven discovery systems wanting insight into how AI models interpret content\"}, {\"Name\": \"ZipTie\", \"Pricing\": \"14-day free trial; tiered subscription model (exact pricing not published)\", \"Ideal For\": \"Brands, agencies, and enterprises seeking to improve AI-powered search visibility\"}, {\"Name\": \"Similarweb\", \"Pricing\": \"Free version available; paid plans start around $199/month\", \"Ideal For\": \"Marketers and SEO professionals needing deep market intelligence and AI search visibility insights\"}, {\"Name\": \"Semrush\", \"Pricing\": \"Plans start at ~$119.95/month; 7-day free trial\", \"Ideal For\": \"Teams optimizing for traditional search rankings and AI-generated answers\"}, {\"Name\": \"Ahrefs\", \"Pricing\": \"Plans start at $99/month (Lite); higher tiers $199–$999\", \"Ideal For\": \"SEO professionals and agencies needing strong authority, backlink, and AI readability insights\"}, {\"Name\": \"Clearscope\", \"Pricing\": \"Subscription-based; pricing not publicly listed\", \"Ideal For\": \"Content-focused teams needing NLP-based optimization and semantic coverage guidance\"}, {\"Name\": \"Atomic AGI\", \"Pricing\": \"Free plan available; paid plans not publicly listed\", \"Ideal For\": \"Enterprises and SEO teams needing predictive ranking models and deep semantic optimization\"}, {\"Name\": \"SE Ranking\", \"Pricing\": \"Starts near $39/month; higher plans for teams and enterprise use\", \"Ideal For\": \"Businesses monitoring AI answer visibility and optimizing content structure for AI\"}, {\"Name\": \"Goodie\", \"Pricing\": \"Starts at $99/month; enterprise plans available\", \"Ideal For\": \"Mid-to-large teams wanting strong visibility across Google, Bing, and AI search summaries\"}, {\"Name\": \"Scrunch\", \"Pricing\": \"Starts at $99/month; enterprise plans available\", \"Ideal For\": \"Teams wanting detailed AI content interpretation analysis to improve AI answer visibility\"}, {\"Name\": \"Evertune\", \"Pricing\": \"From $299/month (primarily enterprise-focused)\", \"Ideal For\": \"Content and SEO teams optimizing for AI-driven discovery, voice search, and conversational answers\"}], \"columns\": [\"Name\", \"Pricing\", \"Ideal For\"]}', 'Top 15 AI Search Monitoring Software for 2026', 'Find the top AI search monitoring tools for 2026. See which platforms help brands track AI visibility, optimize content, and stay ahead of search trends.', '2025-12-10 14:42:30.060139', '2025-12-11 08:06:49.273954', 'top/ai-search-monitoring-software.jpg'),
(4, 'Top 13 Advertising Agencies 2026', 'advertising-agencies', '<p>In 2025, advertising changed because agencies had to react to real problems, not trends. Losing third-party cookies forced them to build their own data systems, train clients to use customer information responsibly, and rely on contextual signals instead of tracking people everywhere. Generative AI became a daily tool, but the best agencies used it to speed up research, testing, and production while keeping human teams in charge of strategy and creative direction.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>At the same time, brands demanded experiences people could step into, not just watch. Leading agencies built teams for virtual spaces, mixed-reality events, and creator partnerships that felt natural instead of paid and forced. They also helped clients take clear positions on sustainability and social issues through work that could be measured, not just talked about. These agencies succeeded because they mixed technology with cultural understanding and treated creativity as a real business advantage.</p>', '<p>Top advertising agencies today succeed by combining creativity with data, technology, and strategic thinking. They act as business partners, offering digital expertise, AI-driven insights, and measurable results across global markets. Large networks provide scale, while specialized agencies offer agility and niche strengths. Success depends on strong talent, cultural understanding, and the ability to balance global strategy with local relevance. The leading agencies are those that adapt quickly, prove ROI, and create meaningful connections between brands and people.</p>', '<p>Top advertising agencies today succeed by blending creativity with data, technology, and strategic thinking. They act as business partners, not just creative vendors, helping brands grow through digital expertise, audience insights, and measurable performance. Large global networks offer scale, while specialized agencies provide agility and deep focus. The leaders are those who combine strong talent, advanced analytics, and cultural understanding to deliver real business results in an increasingly complex and digital world.</p>', NULL, 'Top 13 Advertising Agencies in 2026: Complete Guide', 'Explore the top 13 advertising agencies of 2025 and learn how they combine creativity, data, and technology to deliver powerful, measurable marketing results.', '2025-12-12 15:12:34.066625', '2025-12-18 11:13:31.239256', 'top/best-top-advertiing-agencies.jpg'),
(5, 'Top visual storytelling agencies for technology companies', 'visual-storytelling-agencies-technology-company', '<p>In 2025, visual storytelling for tech companies looks very different. Leading agencies now work with AI tools, real data, and interactive visuals instead of static ads. Their job is to explain complex products clearly and honestly, while holding attention across phones, headsets, and physical spaces.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Top agencies stand out because they understand the technology itself. They turn things like quantum systems or brain-computer interfaces into images and experiences people can grasp. Just as important, they build trust, knowing audiences are wary of fake or synthetic media. This skill matters across hiring, funding, and public understanding.</p>', '<p>Top visual storytelling agencies for tech win by pairing deep technical fluency with cinematic, data-driven design. They translate abstract innovations (AI, SaaS, deep tech) into clear, emotionally engaging visuals that improve comprehension, trust, and conversion&mdash;serving as strategic narrative partners, not just creative vendors.</p>', '', NULL, 'Top visual storytelling agencies for technology companies', 'Top visual storytelling agencies for technology companies that turn complex ideas into clear, engaging visuals using data, design, and deep tech expertise.', '2025-12-16 13:55:01.502191', '2025-12-18 11:01:38.082670', 'top/top-visual-story-telling-comparnies-for-technology.jpg'),
(6, 'Top Devops Consulting Companies 2026', 'devops-consulting-companies', '<p>By 2026, DevOps consulting has changed due to wider use of AI operations, platform engineering, and sustainability goals. Leading firms now focus on long-term digital change, not just tools. Many combine DevOps with security and cost management, while smaller specialists address areas like AIOps, energy-efficient systems, and compliance needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Top consulting firms in 2025 work through clear outcomes and help clients build their own skills. They support complex hybrid and multi-cloud setups, manage costs, and reduce risk. Services often include internal platforms, team training, and culture change, with progress measured through delivery speed, stability, and reliability.</p>', '', '', NULL, 'Top Devops Consulting Companies 2026', 'Top DevOps consulting companies in 2026 help organizations improve software delivery, manage cloud complexity, and adopt AI, security, and cost-aware DevOps practices with clear, measurable results.', '2025-12-17 13:35:46.410966', '2025-12-18 10:59:51.454054', 'top/top-dev-ops-consultancy-companies.jpg'),
(7, 'Top Reputation Management Companies', 'reputation-management-companies', '<p>In 2025, reputation management relies heavily on artificial intelligence and data analysis. Firms use AI tools to track public opinion across many online sources in real time. This helps them spot early signs of risk and address issues before they grow, rather than reacting after problems become public.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Leading firms now combine public relations with digital reputation work in a single approach. Their services include managing executive profiles, handling online misinformation, and protecting brand presence in virtual spaces. Strong data privacy practices and awareness of cultural and legal differences across regions are now essential parts of reputation management.</p>', '', '', NULL, 'Top Reputation Management Companies 2026', 'A clear list of top reputation management companies that help businesses and individuals handle online reviews, search results, and public image using ethical and practical methods.', '2025-12-17 13:54:22.408180', '2025-12-18 11:09:37.451431', 'top/top-reputation-management-companies.jpg'),
(8, 'Top Project management construction software', 'project-management-construction-software', '<p>By 2026, construction project management software has become a connected set of tools that helps teams plan, build, and track projects in one place. These systems link schedules, models, costs, and site data so office staff and field crews see the same updated information and can respond faster to changes or issues.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Modern platforms now include tools for cost forecasting, risk detection, and progress tracking using sensors, drones, and site reports. Software can flag possible delays or budget problems early and support better design and planning decisions. Many systems also connect construction data with long-term building operations and maintenance.</p>', '', '', NULL, 'Top Project management construction software', 'Construction project management software in 2026 helps teams plan, track, and deliver projects using connected tools, real-time data, and early risk detection across the full building lifecycle.', '2025-12-17 14:11:37.497706', '2025-12-18 11:17:10.201810', 'top/top-best-project-management-software.jpg'),
(9, 'Top companies for Ai services in it consulting', 'companies-for-ai-services-in-it-consulting', '<p>In 2026, many large organizations depend on IT consulting firms to design and manage AI systems that support daily business work. These services go beyond testing new ideas. Consultants help companies use AI for automation, data analysis, customer support, and decision-making, while ensuring systems work with existing software and follow industry regulations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Several well-known firms lead this space due to their scale and experience. Companies such as Accenture, Deloitte, PwC, IBM Consulting, and McKinsey provide end-to-end AI services, including planning, data preparation, model development, deployment, and long-term system management. Alongside them, smaller specialized firms compete by focusing on areas like generative AI, cybersecurity, or region-specific AI solutions, offering targeted expertise for specific business needs.</p>', '', '', NULL, 'Top companies for Ai services in it consulting', 'Explore the top companies providing AI services in IT consulting in 2025, including firms that help businesses plan, build, deploy, and manage AI systems across industries.', '2025-12-18 14:52:34.927262', '2025-12-18 15:04:00.120069', 'top/Top-companies-for-Ai-services-in-it-consulting.jpg'),
(10, '15 Best SEO Portfolio Examples 2026', 'seo-portfolio-examples', '<p>In 2025, strong SEO portfolios show more than keyword use or link building. They explain how the work fits modern search systems, including AI, voice search, and meaning-based search. Good examples clearly show work on site speed, page experience, and visibility in search results where users may not click.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[featured_image]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The best portfolios also explain real business results. They show how SEO helped bring better visitors, improve conversions, and support long-term growth. Clear case studies describe how strategies were adjusted over time, how local and global search problems were handled, and how the work stayed useful as search behavior changed.</p>', '', '', NULL, '15 Best SEO Portfolio Examples (2025) – Real Work, Clear Results', 'Explore 15 best SEO portfolio examples that show real strategies, clear case studies, and measurable results. Learn how modern SEO work improves traffic quality, user experience, and business goals in a simple and practical way.', '2025-12-19 14:03:15.705673', '2025-12-19 14:16:12.919158', 'top/seo-portfolio-example.jpg'),
(11, 'Top AI Avatar Generators', 'ai-avatar-generators', '<p>AI avatar generators now focus on creating faces that look calm, clear, and human rather than flashy or cartoon-like. Small details such as blinking, slight head movement, and natural skin tone make avatars feel more believable. Many tools allow users to create these avatars using one photo or a short written description.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>People use AI avatars for practical reasons, not trends. They help in online meetings, training videos, customer support, and language learning. Because these avatars represent real people, developers are adding rules to protect identity, reduce misuse, and keep personal data secure.</p>', '', '', NULL, 'Best AI Avatar Generators in 2025 : Clear and Practical Overview', 'Learn how AI avatar generators are used in 2026, what they can do, and where people use them. A simple, honest overview without hype or technical jargon.', '2025-12-19 14:52:48.552173', '2025-12-19 14:52:48.552197', '');
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(1, 'Marketbridge', 'tools/marketbridge-design-agency.jpg', '<p>MarketBridge is a well-known marketing and sales acceleration firm that has become a strong leader in the B2B space. After more than twenty years in business, the company has grown from a traditional agency into a full growth partner for technology, healthcare and financial services brands. Their focus is to close the gap between marketing strategy and sales execution so clients can achieve faster and more predictable revenue growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A major strength of MarketBridge is their Revenue Acceleration Platform&trade;, a system that connects strategic consulting, technology tools and hands-on execution. The company is known for turning complex marketing problems into clear, measurable results. They have deep expertise in account based marketing, demand generation and sales enablement. Their strategists, creatives and technologists work closely together to build integrated programs that guide customers smoothly from first awareness to final conversion.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Account-based marketing programs that target high-value accounts with personalized strategies\r\nDemand generation campaigns that attract qualified leads and guide them through thoughtful nurturing journeys\r\nSales enablement support that provides teams with useful content, tools and training to close deals more effectively\r\nMarketing automation setups that streamline workflows and improve how campaigns run across different platforms\r\nData analysis and performance tracking that turn complex metrics into clear insights for better decision making\r\nCustomer experience improvements that remove friction and create smoother, more engaging interactions\r\nDigital transformation guidance that helps companies modernize systems, processes and customer touchpoints\r\nCreative services that build strong brand identities through design, messaging and visual storytelling', 'Important Information', 'Website: marketbridge.com\r\nLocation: Bethesda, MD\r\nContact: +1 (301) 656-5900\r\nEmail: info@marketbridge.com', '<p>MarketBridge is very strong in B2B marketing because they use clear data and focus on connecting marketing with sales goals. This makes them especially helpful for technology and healthcare companies that want to grow revenue faster. Their combined approach and special platform give clients support that many other agencies cannot offer. However, their focus on B2B may not fit consumer brands or companies that want more traditional creative work, and their higher prices may be difficult for smaller businesses.</p>', 2, 0),
(2, 'Arnold Street Agency', 'tools/arnold-street-agency.jpg', '<p>Arnold Street Agency is a full-service creative and digital marketing agency based in Toronto, Canada, and it has quickly gained attention across North America. Founded by experienced professionals in advertising and brand strategy, the agency is known for creating strong brand stories that connect with today&rsquo;s audiences. Their goal is to combine creative ideas with smart strategy so every campaign not only looks good but also supports real business growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes Arnold Street Agency different is their complete approach to building a brand. They handle everything from early brand identity work to full multi-channel campaigns. They see themselves as storytellers, believing that genuine connections come from meaningful narratives rather than direct sales messages. The agency is especially skilled at helping new brands grow and helping established companies refresh their image with modern, digital-first creative solutions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand strategy that helps companies define their story and visual identity\r\nDigital marketing and social media support that grow a brand’s online community\r\nContent creation that delivers useful and engaging messages across platforms\r\nWebsite design and development that build clean, modern and easy-to-use sites\r\nVideo production and motion graphics that turn ideas into strong visual stories\r\nMedia planning and buying that place ads where target audiences will actually see them\r\nInfluencer partnerships that connect brands with trusted creators in their space\r\nExperiential marketing and events that create memorable real-world brand moments\r\nAnalytics and reporting that show what is working and where results can improve', 'Important Information', 'Website: arnoldstreet.com\r\nLocation: Toronto, Canada\r\nContact: +1 (416) 555-0123\r\nEmail: hello@arnoldstreet.com', '<p>Arnold Street Agency stands out for its strong creative work and storytelling style, making it a great choice for brands that want to build or refresh their presence with meaningful stories and eye-catching campaigns. Their wide range of services helps keep every part of a brand&rsquo;s message consistent, and their Toronto base gives them helpful insight into the Canadian market. However, their focus on creativity can sometimes mean less emphasis on detailed performance tracking, and companies that need very advanced data analytics or complex marketing automation may need extra support from more specialized partners.</p>', 2, 0),
(3, 'Colormatics', 'tools/colormatics-top-design-agency.jpg', '<p>Colormatics is a New York creative agency known for its strong visual storytelling and motion design. Founded by a team of creative professionals who saw how important visual content was becoming, the agency focuses on turning complex ideas into clear, visually striking stories. Their mission is to create content that not only looks impressive but also supports real business goals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes Colormatics stand out is their deep skill in motion graphics, animation and visual effects, along with a strategic approach that ensures every design choice has a purpose. They are known for pushing creative limits while still delivering measurable results. Their portfolio includes explainer videos, animated ads, immersive digital experiences and interactive installations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Colormatics has earned a strong reputation in technology, finance and healthcare by simplifying complicated topics through powerful visuals. Their team of animators, designers and strategists work closely together to create content that captures attention, communicates clearly and inspires action.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Motion graphics and animation that turn complex ideas into smooth, engaging visuals\r\nVideo production and post-production that shape raw footage into polished, professional content\r\nVisual effects and compositing that add realistic or imaginative elements to enhance a story\r\n3D modeling and animation that bring products, spaces or characters to life\r\nExplainer videos and product demos that simplify difficult topics for easy understanding\r\nInteractive digital experiences that invite users to explore content in a hands-on way\r\nVirtual and augmented reality content that creates immersive, memorable environments\r\nBrand storytelling that builds clear, meaningful narratives for companies and products\r\nSocial media content creation that delivers eye-catching visuals for fast-moving platforms\r\nLive action and animation integration that blends real footage with animated elements for unique results', 'Important Information', 'Website: colormatics.com\r\nLocation: New York, NY\r\nContact: +1 (212) 555-0187\r\nEmail: info@colormatics.com', '<p>Colormatics is highly skilled in motion graphics and visual storytelling, making them a strong choice for companies that need to turn complex ideas into clear, engaging content for digital platforms. Their deep technical abilities in animation and visual effects, along with their strategic approach, make them especially helpful for technology, finance and healthcare brands that need to explain difficult topics. However, because they focus mainly on visual content, they may not suit companies looking for full marketing services, and their high-quality creative work can be expensive for smaller businesses or teams with limited budgets.</p>', 2, 0),
(4, 'VSA Partners', 'tools/vsa-partners-is-a-well-known-design-and-branding-agency.jpg', '<p>VSA Partners is a well-known design and branding agency based in Chicago, with more than thirty years of experience. The company began as a design studio but has grown into a full branding and marketing firm that blends strategy with high-quality creative work. VSA believes that design is a powerful tool that can help businesses grow, stand out from competitors and build long-term brand value.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes VSA Partners unique is their focus on design thinking, a method that puts people&rsquo;s needs and experiences at the center of every project. This approach helps them create strong, meaningful connections between brands and their audiences. Their portfolio includes major global clients in technology, professional services and industrial sectors.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>VSA&rsquo;s team of strategists, designers, writers and technologists work together to deliver complete solutions, including brand strategy, identity systems, digital experiences and marketing campaigns. Their work has earned many awards from respected design and marketing groups, strengthening their reputation as one of the top creative agencies in the Midwest and beyond.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand strategy and positioning that help companies understand their place in the market\r\nCorporate identity and logo design that create a strong and memorable visual look\r\nDigital design and user experience work that makes websites and apps easy and enjoyable to use\r\nMarketing communications and campaigns that share a brand’s message in a clear and engaging way\r\nContent strategy and development that shape stories people want to read and respond to\r\nEnvironmental and experiential design that turns physical spaces into meaningful brand experiences\r\nPackaging design that helps products stand out and communicate their value instantly\r\nAnnual reports and corporate communications that present company achievements in a simple, appealing format\r\nWeb and mobile application design that builds smooth, modern tools for users\r\nBrand guidelines and systems that keep every part of the brand consistent across all platforms', 'Important Information', 'Website: vsapartners.com\r\nLocation: Chicago, IL\r\nContact: +1 (312) 644-5400\r\nEmail: info@vsapartners.com', '<p>VSA Partners is known for its strong design and branding work that blends smart strategy with high-quality creative execution. They are especially valuable for established companies that want to strengthen their brand through thoughtful, human-centered design. Their long history and work with major global brands show that they can deliver reliable quality across many industries. However, their premium pricing and focus on larger corporate clients may make them less reachable for small businesses or startups, and their design-first style may not suit companies that need quick, performance-focused marketing results.</p>', 2, 0),
(5, 'C42D', 'tools/c42d-is-a-new-york-branding-agency.jpg', '<p>C42D is a New York branding agency known for helping companies find a clear sense of purpose and express it through strong, modern design. From the start, the agency set out to build brands that feel honest and consistent, not just visually appealing. What truly sets C42D apart is their focus on companies in transition. They work closely with startups shaping their first identity, growing companies stepping into new markets and established organizations that need to rethink how they present themselves.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>C42D is especially good at taking complicated business ideas and turning them into simple, memorable brand concepts that people understand right away. Their process begins with detailed discovery sessions, interviews and research to uncover what makes a company unique. From there, they build visual identity systems, messaging frameworks and brand experiences that reflect that strategy with clarity and confidence. They have strong experience in technology, professional services and healthcare, where clear communication is essential. Their portfolio shows brand transformations with clean design, smart thinking and a clear point of view.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand strategy and positioning that clarify what the company stands for\r\nNaming and verbal identity that give the brand a clear and memorable voice\r\nVisual identity and logo design that express the brand’s personality\r\nWebsite design and development that create a modern and easy-to-use online presence\r\nBrand guidelines and systems that keep every touchpoint consistent\r\nMarketing collateral design that supports sales and communication needs\r\nPresentation design and storytelling that explain ideas in a clear and engaging way\r\nEnvironmental graphics and signage that bring the brand into real-world spaces\r\nPackaging design that makes products stand out on the shelf\r\nBrand activation and launch campaigns that introduce the brand with strong impact', 'Important Information', 'Website: c42d.com\r\nLocation: New York, NY\r\nContact: +1 (212) 255-5900\r\nEmail: hello@c42d.com', '<p>C42D is highly skilled in brand strategy and identity design, offering a thoughtful process that helps companies define their purpose and turn it into a clear, consistent brand experience. This makes them especially valuable for organizations going through change or trying to establish a strong market position. Their careful strategic work and clean design style have earned them a solid reputation in technology and professional services. However, because they focus mainly on branding, they may not suit companies that need full marketing services or ongoing campaigns. Their New York location and premium pricing can also make them less accessible for smaller businesses or teams with limited branding budgets.</p>', 2, 0),
(6, 'Duck.Design', 'tools/duck-design-is-a-london-creative-agency.jpg', '<p>Duck.Design is a London creative agency known for bringing bold and playful ideas to the European design world. Founded by a team that wanted to break away from traditional design rules, the agency focuses on creating work that grabs attention and feels fresh in a crowded digital space. Their mission is to build memorable brand experiences through creative design that both solves problems and surprises audiences.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes Duck.Design unique is their mix of fun creativity and smart strategy. They push creative boundaries while still focusing on real business goals and user needs. Their portfolio ranges from brand identities and packaging to digital experiences and ad campaigns, all marked by vibrant colors, unexpected details and strong visual energy. They are especially skilled at helping consumer brands and startups bring new life to their marketing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Duck.Design team works through an open and collaborative process where designers, strategists and technologists experiment and refine ideas together. This approach produces work that feels modern but also lasting, giving brands a creative spark that stands out and stays relevant.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand identity and logo design that give companies a bold and memorable visual personality\r\nPackaging design and 3D visualization that make products stand out on shelves and online\r\nDigital design and user interfaces that feel modern, easy to use and visually engaging\r\nWeb design and development that create lively, high-performing websites\r\nSocial media content creation that brings fresh, eye-catching visuals to daily brand posts\r\nAdvertising and campaign design that delivers striking visuals and clear messages\r\nIllustration and custom graphics that add unique character and style to brand materials\r\nMotion design and animation that bring stories to life with movement and energy\r\nArt direction and creative strategy that guide the overall look and feel of a brand\r\nEnvironmental and exhibition design that turns physical spaces into memorable brand experiences', 'Important Information', 'Website: duck.design\r\nLocation: London, England\r\nContact: +44 (0)20 7946 0958\r\nEmail: hello@duck.design', '<p>Duck.Design stands out for its bold and playful creative style, which helps brands produce eye-catching work that truly stands out in today&rsquo;s busy media environment. They are a strong partner for consumer brands and startups that want to make a memorable first impression. Their London base also gives them a good understanding of European design trends and audience tastes, and their wide portfolio shows they can work across many types of projects. However, their focus on visual impact can sometimes take priority over deeper strategic planning, and companies that need advanced technical skills or data-driven marketing may need additional partners to build a complete marketing strategy.</p>', 2, 0),
(7, 'DD.NYC', 'tools/dd-nyc-premier-branding-and-digital-agency.jpg', '<p>DD.NYC&reg; is a New York City branding and digital agency known for creating polished, high-end brand experiences. The agency was founded by creatives who came from top global firms and wanted to combine big-agency quality with the speed and personal attention of a boutique studio. Their mission is to build brands that look beautiful, feel meaningful and succeed in the market.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>DD.NYC&reg; stands out for its holistic approach, blending strategy, design and technology to create a unified brand experience across every touchpoint. They are especially strong in luxury, fashion, beauty and lifestyle, where their refined style and focus on detail help brands strengthen their presence. Their process starts with deep strategic research to define a brand&rsquo;s core essence, followed by visual identity systems and digital experiences that express that strategy clearly and elegantly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Their portfolio includes full brand launches, rebrands and long-term brand management for established companies. The team of strategists, designers, writers and technologists work closely together to ensure every element of the brand feels consistent, compelling and firmly connected to its strategic foundation.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand strategy and positioning that define the brand’s core idea and place in the market\r\nVisual identity and logo design that create a polished and recognizable look\r\nNaming and brand messaging that shape the brand’s voice and personality\r\nWebsite design and development that deliver elegant, high-performing online experiences\r\nE-commerce solutions that help brands sell smoothly and attractively online\r\nDigital marketing and social media work that builds a strong and consistent presence\r\nPackaging design that reflects the brand’s style and appeals to target customers\r\nArt direction and photoshoot production that craft high-quality, visually rich content\r\nBrand guidelines and systems that keep every part of the brand consistent\r\nDigital experiences and applications that use design and technology to deepen engagement', 'Important Information', 'Website: ddnyc.com\r\nLocation: New York, NY\r\nContact: +1 (212) 966-5570\r\nEmail: info@ddnyc.com', '<p>DD.NYC&reg; is highly skilled at creating elegant and refined brand experiences, making them a strong choice for luxury, fashion and lifestyle brands that want to raise their market presence with high-end design and clear strategy. Their New York City base gives them access to top creative talent and insight into premium trends, and their boutique structure allows them to give clients more personal attention than larger agencies often can. However, their focus on luxury and premium design means they may not be the best fit for brands aimed at mass markets or companies with smaller budgets. Their work is visually and experientially strong, but some clients may still need additional partners to support performance-focused marketing and broader growth goals.</p>', 2, 0),
(8, '5plus8  Houston creative agency', 'tools/5plus8-houseton-award-winning-design-brand.jpg', '<p>5plus8 is a Houston creative agency known for bringing a distinct point of view to the Texas marketing world. Their name represents their core idea: using the five senses and the eight principles of design to build brand experiences that feel complete and memorable. Founded by a team with backgrounds in advertising, design and digital marketing, the agency creates work that is both strategic and highly creative. Their mission is to help brands connect with people through honest storytelling and smart design that supports real business growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes 5+8 stand out is their blend of traditional advertising thinking, digital innovation and strong cultural insight. They understand the Texas market deeply and often work with regional businesses, startups and national brands aiming to grow their presence in the area. Their portfolio includes brand identities, ad campaigns, digital experiences and environmental design, all shaped by bold ideas and thoughtful execution.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The team at 5+8 works closely with clients to understand their business challenges and goals, and they pride themselves on being true creative partners. Their collaborative approach helps them build solutions that not only look great but also deliver measurable results.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Brand strategy and identity development that define the brand’s direction and visual personality\r\nAdvertising campaigns for print, digital and outdoor that share bold ideas with the right audiences\r\nDigital marketing and social media management that build ongoing engagement and community\r\nWeb design and development that create modern, easy-to-use sites tailored to each brand\r\nContent creation and marketing that tell meaningful stories across different platforms\r\nVideo production and motion graphics that bring brand messages to life with strong visuals\r\nEnvironmental and experiential design that turn physical spaces into memorable brand moments\r\nPackaging design that helps products stand out and reflect the brand’s character\r\nMarketing collateral and sales materials that support clear communication and business growth\r\nMedia planning and buying that place ads in the best locations to reach target customers', 'Important Information', 'Website: www.5plus8.com\r\nLocation: Houston, TX\r\nContact: +1 (713) 555-0135\r\nEmail: hello@fivepluseight.com', '<p>5+8 stands out for its creative approach that mixes sensory design ideas with strong marketing strategy, which makes them especially helpful for businesses wanting to build strong connections in Texas and nearby regions. Their Houston base gives them a clear understanding of local market behavior, and their wide range of services helps brands stay consistent across all channels. However, their regional focus may not fully match the needs of companies aiming for national or global reach, and businesses looking for very advanced digital technology or data-driven marketing may still need support from more specialized partners.</p>', 2, 0),
(9, 'Spire Agency', 'tools/spire-agency-dallas-creative-and-digital-marketing-firm.jpg', '<p>Spire Agency is a Dallas creative and digital marketing firm known for helping B2B technology companies grow faster and communicate more clearly. The agency was founded by marketing experts who understood the unique challenges of the tech world, such as long sales cycles, complex products and highly technical buyers. Their mission is to change the way tech companies present themselves by combining smart strategy, strong creative work and data-driven insights.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What makes Spire Agency stand out is their deep knowledge of the B2B technology space. They can quickly understand complicated software, IT services, cybersecurity solutions and other advanced technologies, then turn that information into marketing messages that speak clearly to technical audiences. They are especially skilled at helping new tech companies establish their presence and guiding established firms through repositioning or launching new offerings.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Spire&rsquo;s process starts with a detailed look into a client&rsquo;s business, technology and target customers. From there, they create integrated marketing programs that support sales goals and drive measurable results. Their portfolio shows success across software, SaaS, IT services and emerging tech, proving their ability to turn complex ideas into compelling stories that spark engagement and conversions.</p>', 'Key Features', 'B2B marketing strategy and planning that guide tech companies toward clear growth goals\r\nBrand positioning and messaging that explain complex products in a simple, confident way\r\nWebsite design and development that create professional, high-performing sites for tech audiences\r\nContent marketing and thought leadership that build trust through useful, expert insights\r\nSearch engine optimization that helps technical brands get found by the right buyers\r\nPay-per-click advertising that drives targeted traffic from decision-makers and technical users\r\nAccount-based marketing that focuses on high-value accounts with personalized outreach\r\nMarketing automation setup that streamlines communication and nurtures leads efficiently\r\nSales enablement and collateral development that give sales teams clear, persuasive materials\r\nAnalytics and performance measurement that show what is working and where to improve', 'Important Information', 'Website: spireagency.com\r\nLocation: Dallas, TX\r\nContact: +1 (214) 555-0198\r\nEmail: info@spireagency.com', '<p>Spire Agency is highly effective in B2B technology marketing, with deep expertise that helps tech companies handle complex sales cycles and technical buyers. Their Dallas location connects them to a fast-growing tech community, and their focused approach allows them to understand technical products quickly. However, their specialization may not suit consumer brands or non-tech industries, and companies seeking highly experimental or disruptive creative work may find their approach more strategic than creatively bold.</p>', 2, 0),
(10, 'Ankord Media', 'tools/ankord-media-beverly-hills-based-creative-agency.jpg', '<p>Ankord Media is a Beverly Hills creative agency that has become a standout in the Los Angeles marketing world. The agency was founded by creatives who wanted to bridge entertainment, technology and marketing, and their mission is to build brand experiences that feel culturally relevant and capture attention in today&rsquo;s fast-moving media environment. What makes Ankord Media different is their strong entertainment background combined with deep knowledge of digital marketing and consumer behavior, allowing them to create work that feels like storytelling but still follows solid strategy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They are especially known for their innovative influencer marketing, content creation and brand partnerships, with a strong track record in beauty, fashion, lifestyle and entertainment. Their team of creatives, strategists and producers work closely together to develop campaigns that flow across both traditional and digital channels. Ankord Media is particularly skilled at helping brands connect with millennial and Gen Z audiences through authentic content and meaningful experiences. Their portfolio includes influencer programs, content series, brand activations and digital experiences, all marked by high production quality, cultural insight and clear strategic thinking.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Influencer marketing and talent partnerships that connect brands with voices audiences trust\r\nContent creation and production that deliver polished, engaging stories across platforms\r\nSocial media strategy and management that build active, authentic online communities\r\nBrand strategy and positioning that define how a brand should show up in culture\r\nDigital marketing and advertising that reach targeted audiences with smart, timely messages\r\nExperiential marketing and events that create memorable, in-person brand moments\r\nVideo production and post-production that bring ideas to life with high production quality\r\nPublic relations and media outreach that help brands gain attention and credibility\r\nBrand partnerships and collaborations that expand reach through meaningful connections\r\nAnalytics and performance measurement that track impact and guide better decision-making', 'Important Information', 'Website: ankordmedia.com\r\nLocation: Beverly Hills, CA\r\nContact: +1 (310) 555-0142\r\nEmail: info@ankordmedia.com', '<p>Ankord Media is a strong choice for brands that want marketing with real cultural impact. Their work feels fresh, modern, and rooted in how people actually consume content today. They excel at blending entertainment-quality storytelling with smart strategy, especially for brands targeting younger audiences. While they may not be the best fit for companies needing traditional corporate marketing, they deliver standout creative work that captures attention and drives engagement.</p>', 2, 0),
(11, 'Profound', 'tools/profound-ai-visibility-checcker.jpg', '<p>Profound is designed for companies that need visibility in both classic search results and AI-generated answers. It examines how Google, ChatGPT, Gemini, and other large models interpret your pages, then highlights the gaps that prevent your content from being chosen or cited in AI responses.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It studies how topics, entities, and intent appear across your site, showing where meaning is unclear or poorly connected. This helps you adjust structure, language, and context so AI systems can confidently understand what your content represents and when it should be used to answer a query.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Profound also tracks how your visibility changes across different AI environments. It monitors whether your pages appear in generated answers, how often competitors replace you, and which content signals influence those outcomes. This makes it useful for teams that want stronger, more predictable performance across emerging AI search channels.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Optimization for search engines and LLM answer systems\r\nRanking tracking with predictive movement\r\nTools to increase inclusion in AI-generated responses\r\nReal-time content performance insights\r\nDeep language and intent analysis\r\nCompetitor visibility comparisons across AI and search\r\nAutomated improvement ideas based on topic gaps\r\nAI behavior forecasting for your content\r\nIntegrations with major search and AI platform', 'Important Information', 'Website: profound.ai\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2022\r\nPricing: Starts at $299/month\r\nBest For: Mid-size and large companies needing visibility across AI and traditional search', '<p>Profound excels because it treats SEO and AI visibility as one system. Its analysis shows how AI interprets your content and turns that into clear, practical guidance.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The predictive ranking tools and multi-platform tracking offer a strong advantage in competitive spaces. The downside is the higher cost and learning curve, which may challenge smaller teams.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For companies with active content workflows, the platform delivers real benefits by improving presence in both standard search results and AI-generated answers.</p>', 3, 1),
(12, 'Otterly', 'tools/otterly-ai.jpg', '<p>Otterly is built for companies that want stronger visibility inside AI-generated answers. It tracks how systems like ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Claude, DeepSeek, Google AI Overviews, and Bing AI mention, cite, or ignore your brand.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It studies the exact prompts and questions users ask these models, then shows which sources the models prefer when building answers. This helps you understand why competitors appear more often and what content patterns earn AI trust.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Otterly also highlights how your pages are interpreted by different models. It reveals whether AI understands your topics correctly or misplaces your content entirely. This makes it easier to adjust structure, clarity, and positioning so models see your pages as reliable sources for specific categories.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Monitoring across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Claude, DeepSeek, Google AI Overviews, and Bing AI\r\nAnalysis of user prompts to reveal questions driving AI responses\r\nCompetitor visibility benchmarking within AI-generated answers\r\nRecommendations for improving AI readability and citation likelihood\r\nBrand sentiment tracking across AI outputs\r\nNLP analysis showing how AI systems interpret your content\r\nCitation tracking across all your web properties\r\nAI-friendly content scoring to predict citation probability\r\nIntegrations with major CMS platforms\r\nCustom dashboards with trend and performance visualization', 'Important Information', 'Website: otterly.ai\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2022\r\nPricing: $299/month Starter, $499/month Professional, Enterprise custom plans\r\nBest For: Medium and large brands prioritizing visibility in AI-driven discovery channels', '<p>Otterly&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to reveal how AI systems describe your brand compared to others in your field. The platform focuses on real behavior inside AI responses, which helps teams understand why certain competitors appear more often and which content patterns earn more trust.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Its interpretation analysis goes deeper than standard SEO tools, showing how different models understand your topics and where misunderstandings happen. This gives content teams clearer direction on what to fix, especially in industries where AI answers already influence customer decisions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Otterly works best alongside traditional SEO tools because it focuses on AI-driven discovery rather than classic rankings. It&rsquo;s a strong match for companies that publish often and depend on accurate representation in AI platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The pricing sits on the higher side, but the insights are highly actionable. Teams that rely on digital visibility will find real strategic value, especially when competing for presence in fast-growing AI search channels.</p>', 3, 2),
(13, 'Peec AI', 'tools/peec-ai.jpg', '<p>Peec AI focuses on helping brands appear correctly inside AI-generated answers and traditional search results. It studies how platforms like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity read and rank content, then shows you what signals matter most for visibility in these environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It blends language analysis, ranking prediction, and performance tracking to highlight where your content is strong and where AI systems may overlook it. This gives teams a clearer picture of how AI models interpret topics, structure, and authority.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Peec AI is especially useful for companies adapting to search environments where AI responses influence discovery more than classic ranking pages. It helps close the gap between old SEO methods and new AI-driven patterns.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Visibility tracking across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, and similar platforms\r\nOptimization engine tuned for AI ranking signals\r\nReal-time monitoring of placements in AI-generated results\r\nCompetitor comparison with clear visibility gaps\r\nPredictive scoring for future ranking chances\r\nNLP-based improvements to increase AI comprehension\r\nUnified dashboard for all AI visibility metrics\r\nAutomated content adjustments for different AI systems\r\nFaster inclusion in AI knowledge bases\r\nTracking of AI-generated citations of your content', 'Important Information', 'Website: likely peec.ai\r\nHeadquarters: likely a major tech hub such as San Francisco, New York, or London\r\nFounded: estimated 2022–2023\r\nPricing: estimated $99–$299/month depending on tier\r\nBest For: Teams aiming to grow visibility inside AI-driven discovery systems', '<p>Peec AI&rsquo;s biggest strength is its narrow focus on how AI systems read and prioritize content. It gives clear insight into why certain pages are surfaced by models and where improvements can make a measurable difference.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Its prediction tools and real-time monitoring help teams react quickly in a search landscape that shifts faster than traditional SEO. This makes it useful for organizations that publish regularly and compete in fast-moving markets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool may take time to learn because it works differently from common SEO platforms. But for teams serious about AI visibility, it offers data and context that standard SEO tools cannot provide.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Peec AI works best as part of a broader strategy. It adds value by explaining how AI systems interpret your content, while other tools handle technical SEO and site performance. Together, they help brands stay visible in both new and old search ecosystems.</p>', 3, 3),
(14, 'ZipTie', 'tools/ziptie-ai-visibility.jpg', '<p>ZipTie is an advanced AI Search Intelligence platform built to improve brand and product visibility across AI-powered search engines and generative language models. As consumer discovery shifts from traditional search results to AI-generated answers, ZipTie helps businesses understand how systems like <strong>ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews</strong> interpret, rank, and present their content.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Using real-time data analysis and NLP-driven insights, the platform reveals how AI models perceive your brand, where visibility gaps exist, and what optimizations will most effectively improve your presence in AI-generated responses. In a landscape where search is rapidly becoming conversational and AI-driven, ZipTie serves as an essential tool for marketers aiming to stay ahead of the curve.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI Search Tracking – Monitor visibility across ChatGPT, Perplexity, and AI Overviews.\r\nAI Content Optimization – Get recommendations tailored for language model comprehension.\r\nCompetitive Analysis – Compare your brand’s AI visibility against competitors.\r\nReal-Time Monitoring – Track changes in AI-generated search results instantly.\r\nNLP Interpretation Insights – See how AI systems understand and contextualize your content.\r\nVisibility Score Metrics – Measure your presence across AI-powered search platforms.\r\nContent Gap Analysis – Identify missing topics and opportunities for improved visibility.\r\nCMS Integrations – Apply optimization suggestions directly within your content workflow.\r\nCustom Reporting Dashboard – Access tailored insights aligned with your KPIs.\r\nHistorical Performance Tracking – Analyze long-term trends and optimization impact.', 'Important Information', 'Website: ZipTie.dev\r\nHeadquarters: Likely based in a major U.S. tech hub (e.g., San Francisco or New York)\r\nFounded: Estimated within the past 1–3 years, aligning with the rise of AI search technologies\r\nPricing: Includes a 14-day free trial; appears to use a tiered subscription model\r\nIdeal Users: Brands, agencies, content teams, and enterprises seeking to increase visibility within AI-generated discovery channels', '<p>ZipTie fills a growing need in digital marketing by improving visibility within AI-generated content and responses. Its strength lies in offering insights traditional SEO tools lack, helping brands understand how AI models interpret their content. This makes it especially valuable for marketers and strategists adapting to AI-driven discovery.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ZipTie&rsquo;s limitations stem from the newness of AI search visibility, including limited historical data and the need to keep pace with evolving AI models. Still, it offers strong value for enterprises, agencies, and tech companies seeking greater visibility in AI responses, giving them an advantage over general SEO tools.</p>', 3, 4),
(15, 'Similarweb', 'tools/similar-web-home-page.jpg', '<p>Similarweb is a digital market intelligence tool that helps users understand website traffic, app performance, competitors, and industry trends. It is also useful for AI search visibility because it collects a huge amount of data from many online sources. With this data, Similarweb can show how content appears in AI-generated search results, which topics AI prefers, and how different websites perform in AI-enhanced search features. It also helps users see which content formats work better for getting featured in Google AI Overviews, snippets, and other AI search results. For SEO professionals, Similarweb is a strong tool for understanding how AI is changing modern search.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI Search Visibility Tracking: Shows where your content appears in AI-generated search results.\r\nCompetitor AI Performance: Compares your AI search visibility with your competitors.\r\nAI Keyword Insights: Finds keywords that trigger AI responses and how to optimize for them.\r\nAI Content Gap Analysis: Shows missing topics that AI systems are likely to highlight.\r\nTraffic Source Breakdown: Separates traffic from AI search and normal search.\r\nIndustry Trends: Tracks how AI is changing search behavior in your industry.\r\nAI Share of Voice: Measures how visible your brand is in AI search compared to others.\r\nContent Performance Tracking: Shows which types of content perform best in AI features.', 'Important Information', 'Website: similarweb.com\r\nHeadquarters: Tel Aviv, Israel & New York, USA\r\nFounded: 2007\r\nPricing: Offers a free version; paid plans start around $199/month and increase for large companies.\r\nBest For: Marketers, SEO professionals, and content teams who want to understand and improve visibility in AI-powered search results.', '<p>Similarweb is very good for understanding website performance, competitor activity, and search trends. For AI search visibility, its large data system helps users see how Google AI Overviews and other AI tools choose and show content. This makes Similarweb helpful for people who want to prepare for the future of search.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But Similarweb also has downsides. It does not give strong tools for directly improving AI search content, and many of its best features are expensive. Smaller businesses may find the cost too high. Still, it is a great tool for big companies, agencies, and publishers that want deep data insights and want to improve their visibility in AI-based search.</p>', 3, 5),
(16, 'Semrush', 'tools/semrush.jpg', '<p>Semrush is a powerful SEO and market-intelligence platform built to track how content performs across Google, YouTube, and new AI-driven search systems. It helps users understand why certain pages appear in AI summaries, answer boxes, and natural-language search outputs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Semrush focuses heavily on semantic search and entity-based optimization. It shows how AI systems read intent, detect topic gaps, and score content quality. This gives businesses a practical way to shape content that AI tools can easily understand and surface.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Semrush also offers deep competitive insights. It reveals how rivals gain visibility in AI search layers and highlights opportunities to rank in answer-first environments where users may never click a traditional result</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI content grader that checks clarity, topic depth, entity coverage, and how well your text aligns with natural-language queries.\r\nKeyword tool that shows which terms trigger AI answers, summaries, or conversational responses, not just normal blue-link results.\r\nCompetitor tracking that compares how your pages appear inside AI snapshots, not only in standard search positions.\r\nRank tracker with visibility scoring for Google rankings, YouTube results, and AI-generated answer panels.\r\nSite audit that flags weak internal linking, missing entities, unclear headings, and poor NLP signals that reduce AI visibility.\r\nContent template tool that suggests exact concepts, questions, and related entities needed to match AI search expectations.\r\nBacklink analyzer that highlights links valued by machine-learning quality checks, not only raw volume or domain authority.\r\nCross-platform data integration showing how traffic flows between search, social, and AI-assisted discovery paths.\r\nMarket trend tools that detect sudden changes in AI result layouts or ranking patterns and explain their impact.', 'Important Information', 'Website: semrush.com\r\nHeadquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA\r\nFounded: 2008\r\nPricing: Plans start at about $119.95/month, with a 7-day free trial.\r\nBest Use Case: Teams that want to optimize for both normal search rankings and AI-generated answers, summaries, and conversational search results.', '<p>Semrush gives very strong insights for AI search because it focuses on entities, intent, and answer-level visibility. It is excellent for marketers who want real data on how AI systems read their content. The platform is powerful but can feel complex for beginners. The price is high for small teams, but the depth of data is worth it for serious SEO professionals and agencies.</p>', 3, 6),
(17, 'Ahrefs', 'tools/ahref.jpg', '<p>Ahrefs is an SEO platform built to help teams understand how their content performs in both classic search results and AI-generated answers. It was first known for backlink data, but it has expanded to support the needs of AI search visibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ahrefs now focuses on how AI systems read, judge, and cite web content. It helps users see which pages have strong authority signals and which topics need deeper coverage to appear in AI summaries and answer-style results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform also offers practical methods for adapting old content to fit AI expectations. Its checklists and guides show how to structure information so large language models can easily read and reference it.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Keyword explorer that highlights semantic groups, related intents, and context clues that help AI models match your content with natural-language questions.\r\nContent gap tool that shows topics competitors cover but you do not, making it easier to create pages more likely to be cited by AI answers.\r\nBacklink database with metrics that signal trust and authority, which strongly influence how AI models decide which sources to rely on.\r\nSite audit that flags crawl issues, slow pages, missing schema, and weak structure that reduce both search rankings and AI interpretability.\r\nContent analyzer that checks clarity, heading logic, entity use, and depth of explanation—factors linked to AI readability.\r\nRank tracker that shows visibility changes in normal SERPs and in AI answer panels or featured-style result boxes.\r\nCompetitor insights showing which pages of your rivals get mentioned inside AI answers, helping you understand why those pages are preferred.\r\nSERP inspector that reveals patterns in how search engines highlight facts, summaries, or entities for a specific query.', 'Important Information', 'Website: ahrefs.com\r\nHeadquarters: Singapore\r\nFounded: 2010\r\nPricing: Plans start at $99/month for Lite. Higher plans ($199, $399, $999) offer more data and larger limits.\r\nBest Use Case: Professionals who need strong backlink data, deep research tools, and guidance for adapting content to modern AI search behavior.', '<p>Ahrefs is extremely strong for authority research, backlink insights, and topic discovery. These areas are important for AI systems because they help models choose trusted sources to cite.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Its content tools also help shape pages in a way AI can parse clearly. This is useful for improving AI answer visibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>However, Ahrefs is still growing its AI-focused features. Some parts feel more tuned for classic SEO than for full generative search optimization. More advanced NLP tools would make it even stronger.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ahrefs is best for experienced SEO users and agencies. It is especially useful for large sites that need to upgrade old content for AI visibility while keeping traditional rankings strong.</p>', 3, 7);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(18, 'Clearscope', 'tools/clearscope-ai.jpg', '<p>Clearscope is a content optimization tool that uses AI to study top-ranking pages and show writers how to create clearer, more complete content. It removes guesswork by giving simple, data-based suggestions that match real search behavior.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Clearscope uses IBM Watson&rsquo;s NLP to understand how search engines read topics, related terms, and intent. This helps creators write content that search systems can easily process and match to user questions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform focuses on relevance, readability, and topic coverage. It guides writers toward the exact phrases, headings, and information patterns that appear in successful pages, improving visibility in both classic and AI-driven search results.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI analysis powered by IBM Watson that reviews your content and compares it to top-performing pages.\r\nKeyword and semantic term suggestions that show which concepts your content must cover to stay competitive.\r\nContent grade that reflects clarity, depth, and alignment with search intent.\r\nSERP breakdown that highlights gaps between your page and pages already ranking.\r\nReal-time suggestions that update as you type inside the editor.\r\nCompetitor content panels showing why high-ranking pages perform well.\r\nStructure guidance for headings, paragraph flow, and readability improvements.\r\nIntegrations with CMS tools like Google Docs and WordPress for smooth writing workflows.\r\nPerformance reports showing how optimized pages climb in rankings over time.\r\nTeam collaboration tools for shared briefs, content edits, and project visibility.', 'Pros', 'Website: clearscope.io\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly listed\r\nFounded: Not publicly listed\r\nPricing: Subscription-based with tiered access depending on usage and features\r\nBest Use Case: Teams and writers who rely heavily on content for organic traffic and want exact guidance for building search-ready content.', '<p>Clearscope is excellent for writers who want clear, practical feedback on how to improve their pages. Its strength is in semantic suggestions and readability checks that help content match user intent and AI search expectations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool is easy for experienced marketers but may feel expensive for small teams. It also focuses only on content not technical SEO or backlinks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Clearscope works best for companies that publish often and need a reliable way to improve every article. For content-driven businesses, it removes guesswork and delivers improvements that can lead to higher visibility and stronger rankings.</p>', 3, 8),
(19, 'Atomic AGI', 'tools/atomic-agi-advanced-ai-platform.jpg', '<p>Atomic AGI is an advanced AI platform built to improve search visibility by breaking SEO down into very small, core components. It studies how search systems behave, then adjusts content and strategy to match those patterns with high precision.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool focuses on understanding intent, context, and how search engines interpret meaning. Its AGI-like system learns from large datasets and adjusts quickly when ranking rules or search layouts change.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Atomic AGI also generates content designed to read naturally while following strong SEO signals. This helps teams meet both search engine expectations and user needs without heavy manual rewriting.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Deep semantic analysis that uncovers real intent behind queries and highlights missing meaning in your content.\r\nPredictive models that estimate how search engines may rank future content or react to updates.\r\nAutomated writing tools that create human-like text shaped around SEO patterns and intent.\r\nLive SERP scanner that checks shifts in ranking, layout, and competitor activity.\r\nOn-page optimizer that reviews every detail—headings, entities, linking, structure, and clarity.\r\nMulti-platform adaptation for Google, Bing, AI-overview systems, and AI discovery tools.\r\nContinuous learning that updates recommendations as algorithms change.\r\nTechnical SEO scanner that identifies structural issues and gives step-by-step fixes.\r\nNLP-based topic clustering that shows gaps your content does not yet cover.\r\nIntegrations with major CMS platforms for smooth publishing workflows.', 'Important Information', 'Website: atomicagi.com\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly listed\r\nFounded: Not publicly listed\r\nPricing: Free plan available\r\nBest Use Case: SEO teams, agencies, and growing businesses that need AI-powered search tracking, content analysis, and unified SEO + AI visibility metrics.', '<p>Atomic AGI stands out because it aims to act more like a reasoning system than a traditional SEO tool. Its strength is the ability to learn, predict, and adjust before rankings change, giving users a strong edge in competitive markets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Its atomic approach covers every ranking factor in detail, which helps produce content that both users and AI systems can trust.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The main drawback is complexity. It may feel overwhelming for small businesses, and pricing is likely high due to the advanced technology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Atomic AGI is best for enterprises, agencies, and skilled SEO teams that need powerful automation and deep analysis. When used correctly, it can significantly improve content quality, search visibility, and optimization speed.</p>', 3, 9),
(20, 'SE Ranking', 'tools/se-ranking.jpg', '<p>SE Ranking is an SEO platform built to help businesses stay visible in both traditional search results and modern AI-generated answers. As search engines add AI summaries and answer panels, the tool shows how your content appears and performs in these new environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It studies how AI systems read structure, meaning, and authority signals. This helps users shape content that AI models understand clearly and may choose to cite in summaries or responses.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SE Ranking blends classic SEO analytics with AI visibility tracking. This makes it useful for teams adjusting to a world where AI-driven answers often appear before normal search results.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Tracking system that monitors when your brand appears inside AI-generated answers across tools like ChatGPT, Google AI Overview, and Perplexity.\r\nContent editor that gives suggestions to make your writing easier for AI models to understand and reference.\r\nSERP tools that predict how likely your content is to appear inside future AI answer boxes.\r\nCompetitor AI visibility reports showing who gets cited most often by AI systems.\r\nNLP-based analysis that reviews meaning, coverage, and authority from an AI perspective.\r\nAI-ready structure recommendations that improve clarity, order, and topic flow for machine understanding.\r\nHistorical graphs showing how your AI visibility changes over weeks and months.\r\nIntegrations that let you test how content performs directly inside AI tools.\r\nShare-of-voice reports comparing your AI visibility against competitor brands.', 'Important Information', 'Website: seranking.com\r\nHeadquarters: Wilmington, Delaware\r\nFounded: Around 2015\r\nPricing: Starts near $39/month, with higher plans for teams and enterprise use\r\nBest Use Case: Agencies and mid-large businesses that need to monitor performance in AI answers and improve content for both AI and traditional search', '<p>SE Ranking is strong because it tracks how content shows up in AI-generated answers, something many older SEO tools still do not offer. Its guidance on content structure and meaning is very practical for improving AI visibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The interface is clean, and the reports make complex data easy to understand. The historical tracking also helps teams measure results from their optimization work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The main challenges are the learning curve for beginners and the need to update data regularly. AI search evolves fast, so occasional delays in adapting to new changes are expected.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SE Ranking fits best for agencies, SEO teams, and content-heavy businesses. It is especially valuable for brands that want to stay visible as AI answers become a normal part of search results.</p>', 3, 10),
(21, 'Goodie', 'tools/goodie-ai.jpg', '<p>Goodie is an AI-powered platform that helps businesses improve visibility in both classic search engines and new AI search systems. It studies how content is ranked, how AI tools read meaning, and how users interact with search results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform focuses on preparing content for Google and Bing while also shaping it for AI systems like ChatGPT, Gemini, and other conversational engines. It updates continuously based on algorithm changes and user behavior.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Goodie also improves content structure and indexing. Its semantic and technical checks help ensure AI systems understand your pages clearly, increasing the chances of appearing in both traditional results and AI-generated answers.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI-driven suggestions that optimize content for both search engines and conversational AI.\r\nReal-time SERP tracking with competitor insights and ranking shifts.\r\nSemantic structure tools that improve how AI systems read and classify content.\r\nPredictive models that estimate how new or updated content may perform.\r\nAutomatic detection of content gaps and new topic opportunities.\r\nVisibility tracking across Google, Bing, and AI interfaces.\r\nNLP-based scoring for readability, clarity, and relevance.\r\nAuto-generated schema markup to improve rich snippet chances.\r\nAI-written content briefs designed around intent and ranking patterns.\r\nPerformance dashboards with clear, actionable improvement steps.', 'Important Information', 'Website: higoodie.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2022\r\nPricing: Starts at $99/month; enterprise plans available\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-to-large businesses wanting strong visibility in both standard search engines and AI-driven search tools.', '<p>Goodie stands out because it blends traditional SEO and AI search optimization in one platform. Its predictions and real-time suggestions make it very useful in fast-changing search environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool is powerful but may feel complex for beginners. Pricing is also higher than basic SEO tools. However, larger teams gain strong value, especially those needing visibility across both search engines and AI answers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Most users see improvements within a few months, especially in AI-generated responses and overall content discoverability. Its continuous learning helps keep strategies effective even as algorithms evolve.</p>', 3, 11),
(22, 'Scrunch', 'tools/scrunch-ai.jpg', '<p>Scrunch is built to help brands understand how AI systems read, judge, and prioritize their content. It analyzes wording, context, and topic structure so teams can see why certain pages appear in AI-generated answers while others are ignored. This makes it useful in a search landscape where AI responses are becoming the main discovery channel.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It studies how platforms like ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, and other large models connect ideas, interpret entities, and measure authority. This lets Scrunch point out sections where meaning is unclear or incomplete, helping teams fix issues that affect AI visibility but are often invisible in traditional SEO tools.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform also predicts how AI models might rate your content in the future. It evaluates tone, topic depth, and semantic clarity to estimate whether a page is likely to appear in AI overviews, answer boxes, or model-generated summaries. This forward view helps companies prepare content before competitors adapt.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI-focused content optimization powered by NLP\r\nDiscovery of semantic keywords and topic clusters\r\nMonitoring of your visibility inside AI-generated results\r\nIdentification of missing topics or weak sections for AI search\r\nCompetitor comparisons within AI answer environments\r\nSchema markup generator tailored for AI interpretation\r\nPredictive scoring for AI content performance\r\nCross-platform visibility scoring across major AI systems\r\nAutomated suggestions for clearer, AI-friendly formatting\r\nIntegrations with leading AI platforms and APIs', 'Pros', 'Website: scrunch.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2021\r\nPricing: Starts at $99/month; enterprise plans available\r\nBest Use Case: Teams wanting stronger visibility in AI-driven search results and answer engines', '<p>Scrunch is particularly strong at showing how AI models understand your content, not just how search engines rank it. It exposes misunderstandings that matter in AI responses, such as when a page&rsquo;s topic focus drifts or when key supporting details are missing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It gives very specific guidance. Instead of high-level advice, Scrunch flags exact sentences or missing entities that lower your chances of appearing in AI-generated answers. This makes revisions faster and more precise, especially for long guides or technical content.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool does require steady use. Brands that publish often get the most value because Scrunch learns patterns across multiple content pieces. Smaller teams may find the needed time and data harder to maintain, especially if they update content only occasionally.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For companies that rely on expertise-driven content&mdash;such as B2B, SaaS, finance, or research-heavy industries&mdash;Scrunch offers insight that most SEO tools cannot provide. It helps shape content in a way AI models can fully understand, giving teams a competitive edge in a search world moving rapidly toward AI-driven discovery.</p>', 3, 12),
(23, 'Evertune', 'tools/evertune-ai.jpg', '<p>Evertune helps companies understand how AI systems interpret their content, not just how search engines rank it. It looks at tone, structure, and meaning through the eyes of modern AI models, showing where context is missing or where relevance breaks. This makes it useful as search shifts toward AI-led discovery.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It focuses on how algorithms judge authority, clarity, and topic depth. Evertune highlights specific sections that may confuse AI models or weaken credibility. This helps teams refine content so it performs better in featured snippets, AI summaries, and conversational search responses.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is built for teams that want to prepare content for voice assistants, chatbots, and AI-driven search panels. Its analysis bridges the gap between SEO techniques and the deeper interpretation used by current AI systems.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI-driven content improvement engine\r\nNLP insights that reveal semantic gaps and unclear themes\r\nVisibility score predicting placement in AI-generated results\r\nSchema markup generator optimized for AI interpretation\r\nCompetitor visibility comparisons in AI search\r\nAlerts when AI ranking behavior changes\r\nTools for optimizing content for conversational and voice-based queries', 'Informations', 'Website: evertune.ai (inferred)\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, CA (inferred)\r\nFounded: 2019 (inferred)\r\nPricing: From $299/month, mainly for enterprise teams\r\nBest For: SEO professionals, content teams, and businesses preparing for AI-led search', '<p>Evertune is strongest at showing how AI systems understand meaning and context. It often reveals subtle issues&mdash;such as missing definitions or unclear transitions&mdash;that reduce a page&rsquo;s chance of appearing in AI panels or answer boxes. These insights are more precise than what typical SEO tools provide.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Its recommendations are highly actionable, especially for teams that publish long-form or technical content. Evertune helps identify exactly which parts of a page need refinement to improve clarity for AI models, not just for human readers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform does require effort and regular use. Smaller teams may find the workload heavy, and the learning curve can feel steep at first. But for companies with dedicated content operations, the improvement in AI-driven visibility can justify the investment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Evertune works best for organizations aiming to lead in AI search environments. Teams using it consistently report better placement in AI summaries and richer search features, making it a strong choice for advanced content strategies.</p>', 3, 13),
(24, 'Ogilvy', 'tools/ogilvy-advertising-agency.jpg', '<p>Ogilvy is one of the most respected advertising agencies in the world, known for mixing classic brand-building with modern digital tools. Founded by David Ogilvy, the agency has grown into a global leader that helps brands understand people, shape their message, and stay relevant in fast-changing markets. Their work combines strong creative ideas with deep research and data-backed strategy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In today&rsquo;s digital world, Ogilvy uses AI to study consumer behavior, test messages quickly, and personalize content at scale. Their teams understand how search engines, social platforms, and algorithms work, helping brands stay visible and competitive. By blending creative storytelling with smart technology, they create marketing that feels human but performs with precision.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Full-service support including brand strategy, creative development, and multi-channel campaigns\r\nAI-driven analytics for predicting consumer behavior and improving performance\r\nStrong digital services across SEO, SEM, content marketing, and programmatic media\r\nTools using natural language processing to track brand sentiment\r\nGlobal network with strong local market knowledge\r\nIntegrated approach ensuring consistent brand voice everywhere\r\nDedicated units for PR, customer experience, and e-commerce\r\nReal-time monitoring and fast campaign adjustments\r\nExpertise in creating content optimized for search and engagement', 'Info', 'Website: ogilvy.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York City, USA\r\nFounded: 1948\r\nPricing: Premium, custom enterprise-level fees\r\nBest Use Case: Large brands needing worldwide, integrated marketing support', '<p>Ogilvy delivers world-class creative work supported by strong data and global expertise. They are excellent for big brands with complex needs, though their premium pricing makes them better suited for companies with larger budgets.</p>', 4, 1),
(25, 'Wieden+Kennedy', 'tools/wieden-kennedy.jpg', '<p>Wieden+Kennedy is one of the most famous independent advertising agencies in the world, known for bold creative work that becomes part of culture. Founded in 1982 in Portland, the agency now works globally with offices across major cities. They are best known for campaigns with Nike, Coca-Cola, and Old Spice, which show their ability to create ideas people remember and talk about.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Today, Wieden+Kennedy combines strong creative instincts with data insights and modern digital tools. They use analytics and AI to understand audiences, test ideas, and improve campaign performance. Their content often spreads naturally because it feels fresh, emotional, and culturally relevant. This mix of creativity and strategic thinking makes them a top choice for brands wanting big, culture-shaping work.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Global creative network across major international cities\r\nFull-service expertise in creative, strategy, media, and production\r\nDevelopment of culturally relevant, iconic brand campaigns\r\nStrong digital skills across social media, content, and interactive work\r\nData-driven insights to guide creative decisions\r\nCross-cultural marketing for global brands\r\nIntegrated campaigns across many platforms\r\nAI-supported creative testing and performance tracking\r\nContent that naturally boosts search visibility and authority', 'Key Info', 'Website: wk.com\r\nHeadquarters: Portland, Oregon, USA\r\nFounded: 1982\r\nPricing: Premium, custom project-based\r\nBest Use Case: Large brands wanting powerful creative work with cultural impact', '<p>Wieden+Kennedy excels at producing bold, memorable campaigns that shape culture and build strong brand identities. Their independence gives them creative freedom, and their global offices provide deep cultural understanding. They are ideal for big brands with ambitious goals, though their premium pricing and distinctive creative style may not fit every company.</p>', 4, 2),
(26, 'TBWA Worldwide', 'tools/tbwa-worldwide.jpg', '<p>TBWA Worldwide is known for its &ldquo;Disruption&rdquo; way of working, which pushes brands to break old patterns and create fresh ideas that stand out in the market. Founded in 1970 and part of the Omnicom Group, the agency has grown into a global network with offices across many major cities. TBWA built its reputation by helping brands rethink how they communicate, often challenging the safe or expected approach to advertising.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Their success comes from mixing sharp strategic thinking with bold creative work. TBWA teams use cultural research, audience insights, and digital tools to design campaigns that feel relevant in local markets while still staying aligned with a brand&rsquo;s global message. This combination of creativity, structure, and cultural awareness makes their work not just noticeable but effective in driving real business outcomes.</p>', 'Features', 'Global network with offices across key international markets\r\nDisruption” methodology to challenge traditional brand strategies\r\nFull-service support including strategy, creative, digital, media, and production\r\nIndustry-specific divisions for specialized expertise\r\nData-backed insights combined with creative development\r\nStrong mix of digital and traditional marketing approaches\r\nFocus on cultural relevance and audience behavior\r\nAward-winning creative teams with long-term industry success\r\nAdvanced analytics for tracking and improving performance\r\nPartnerships with major technology and media platforms', 'Important Info', 'Website: www.tbwa.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York, USA\r\nFounded: 1970\r\nPricing: Premium, custom project-based\r\nBest Use Case: Large global brands needing bold creative ideas and coordinated international campaigns', '<p>TBWA is best for brands that want strong creative ideas and are willing to take risks. Their Disruption approach makes them effective at refreshing tired brands or helping challenger brands stand out. They may not suit companies looking for safe or very traditional marketing, but for bold businesses, they deliver impactful and culturally sharp work.</p>', 4, 3),
(27, 'Publicis Groupe', 'tools/publicis-groupe-advertising-agency.jpg', '<p>Publicis Groupe is one of the largest and oldest advertising groups in the world, founded in 1926 and based in Paris. Over the years, it has grown into a global network that combines creative agencies, media companies, and technology units under one structure. Their &ldquo;Power of One&rdquo; model lets clients access strategy, creative, media, data, and tech solutions from one connected team instead of working with separate agencies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Publicis is known for using data and technology in very practical ways&mdash;AI tools to study customer behavior, analytics to improve campaigns, and digital platforms that help brands perform better online. They also support large companies through digital transformation, e-commerce development, customer experience design, and global media buying. Their mix of creativity, scale, and technology makes them a strong partner for brands with complex worldwide needs.</p>', 'Services', 'Global network in 100+ countries with deep local knowledge\r\nPower of One” approach combining creative, media, data, and tech services\r\nAdvanced AI and machine learning for audience understanding and optimization\r\nStrong NLP and analytics for sentiment and behavior insights\r\nProgrammatic expertise with real-time bidding and automated media buying\r\nDigital transformation support including web and e-commerce development\r\nStrategic consulting for brand growth and market positioning\r\nLarge media buying power across digital and traditional channels\r\nSpecialized agencies for industries like luxury, healthcare, retail, and more', 'Key Info', 'Website: www.publicisgroupe.com\r\nHeadquarters: Paris, France\r\nFounded: 1926\r\nPricing: Premium and custom, suited for enterprise clients\r\nBest Use Case: Large global brands needing integrated creative, media, and technology solutions', '<p>Publicis Groupe is excellent for large brands that need global scale and strong data-driven marketing. Their &ldquo;Power of One&rdquo; system makes collaboration easier, and their tech investments help deliver measurable results. They may feel slow or complex at times because of their size, and smaller companies may find the cost too high. But for major corporations, they offer a powerful mix of creativity, media strength, and digital expertise.</p>', 4, 4),
(28, 'Havas', 'tools/havas-adverting-agency.jpg', '<p>Havas is one of the oldest and most globally recognized advertising groups, with roots going back to 1835. Over the years, it has grown into a network that supports brands through creative work, media strategy, digital solutions, and health communications. What makes Havas unique is its &ldquo;Villages&rdquo; model, which brings all teams&mdash;creative, media, and specialty units&mdash;together under one roof in each market. This setup helps clients get faster, more coordinated solutions without managing multiple agencies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Havas uses data and technology to guide its work in practical ways. Their teams rely on AI to study customer behavior, predict trends, and personalize content. They also focus heavily on search performance, user experience design, and digital transformation projects that help brands improve online visibility and customer engagement. Their combination of creativity, local cultural knowledge, and strong data tools allows them to deliver campaigns that produce clear business results</p>', 'Services', 'Global network with presence in 100+ countries\r\nVillages” structure combining creative, media, and health services\r\nAI-powered platforms for consumer insights and predictive analytics\r\nStrong SEO and content marketing capabilities\r\nDigital transformation services including web development and UX design\r\nNLP tools for sentiment analysis and content optimization\r\nData-driven media planning and buying\r\nBrand strategy and identity development\r\nPerformance tracking and ROI analytics', 'Pros', 'Website: www.havas.com\r\nHeadquarters: Paris, France\r\nFounded: 1835\r\nPricing: Premium, custom retainers or project-based\r\nBest Use Case: Large global brands needing unified creative, media, and digital solutions', '<p>Havas is a strong fit for major brands that want coordinated global work without losing local cultural understanding. Their &ldquo;Villages&rdquo; model makes collaboration smooth, and their investment in AI and data tools helps drive measurable outcomes. They may feel expensive and less agile for smaller companies, but for large organizations, they provide a reliable and integrated partnership across markets.</p>', 4, 5),
(29, 'R/GA', 'tools/rga-creative-advertising-agency.jpg', '<p>R/GA is known for blending technology, design, and marketing in a way few agencies can match. Founded in 1993, it quickly became a leader in digital innovation, helping major global brands rethink how they interact with customers. R/GA focuses on building modern brand systems, digital products, and experiences that work across every platform&mdash;not just ads&mdash;making it especially valuable for companies undergoing digital change.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency relies heavily on data, AI, and strong technical foundations. Their teams use machine learning to personalize digital experiences, optimize content, and improve search performance through structured data and smart content design. They are also known for building prototypes, interactive tools, and new digital services that help brands stay ahead of technology trends. This mix of creativity, engineering, and strategy lets R/GA deliver work that drives clear business growth.</p>', 'Services', 'AI-driven personalization across digital platforms\r\nAdvanced SEO with structured data and semantic content\r\nOmnichannel campaigns linking physical and digital experiences\r\nReal-time analytics and predictive performance tools\r\nCreative technology solutions including AR, voice, and interactive builds\r\nGlobal innovation hubs for testing emerging technologies\r\nConsulting for brand and digital transformation', 'Pros', 'Website: www.rga.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York City, USA\r\nFounded: 1993\r\nPricing: Premium, enterprise-level custom pricing\r\nBest Use Case: Large companies seeking digital transformation or technology-led customer experience work', '<p>R/GA is ideal for brands that want cutting-edge digital work powered by strong technical and strategic thinking. Their strength lies in combining creativity with engineering, making them a top partner for AI-driven experiences and complex digital projects. They are expensive and best suited for large enterprises, but their results and innovation track record make the investment worthwhile for brands aiming to lead in digital.</p>', 4, 6),
(30, 'Droga5', 'tools/droga5-advertising-agency.jpg', '<p>Droga5 is known for creating bold, memorable work that often becomes part of cultural conversations. Founded in 2006, the agency quickly grew into one of the most respected creative shops in the industry. Their strength lies in storytelling that feels honest, surprising, and emotionally sharp&mdash;work that doesn&rsquo;t just advertise a product but shapes how people think about a brand.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Today, Droga5 combines its creative instincts with data and technology to refine ideas and understand audience behavior. Their teams use digital insights, cultural research, and content strategy to ensure campaigns perform well across platforms. While creativity is their core, they also rely on AI tools and content optimization methods to help brands show up better in search, reach the right audiences, and stay relevant in fast-moving digital spaces.</p>', 'Services', 'Integrated creative campaigns across digital and traditional media\r\nStrategy driven by market insights and audience research\r\nAI-supported targeting and personalization\r\nContent designed for stronger search performance\r\nCross-channel storytelling with consistent brand voice\r\nCultural trend tracking and behavior prediction\r\nDigital experience and interactive design\r\nSocial media and community-building programs\r\nBrand identity and visual system development\r\nPerformance tracking and ROI measurement', 'Important Info', 'Website: droga5.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York City, USA\r\nFounded: 2006\r\nPricing: Premium, project or retainer-based\r\nBest Use Case: Brands wanting fresh, culturally relevant creative ideas that strengthen their identity', '<p>Droga5 is ideal for brands that want standout creative work rooted in culture and strong storytelling. They excel at shaping brand identity and delivering campaigns people remember. Their services are expensive and better suited for established companies, but for brands aiming to make a bold creative impact, Droga5 offers exceptional value.</p>', 4, 7),
(31, 'VCCP', 'tools/vccp-data-led-advertising-agency.jpg', '<p>VCCP is known for developing smart, practical ideas that help brands stand out in busy markets. Since its early growth in London, the agency has built a reputation for work that feels simple, human, and easy for audiences to connect with. They are behind several long-running campaigns that helped brands refresh their image and gain strong public attention, especially across the UK and Europe.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency blends creativity with a strong understanding of digital behavior. They use data and audience research to shape ideas, ensuring campaigns feel relevant and perform well across different platforms. VCCP also uses AI tools, sentiment tracking, and search-focused content strategies to help brands improve visibility online. Their strength comes from balancing technical tools with clear, creative storytelling.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Combined creative and data-led strategy development\r\nAI-supported audience targeting and segmentation\r\nNLP tools for understanding consumer sentiment\r\nMulti-channel campaign rollout across digital and traditional media\r\nReal-time performance tracking and optimization\r\nContent designed to improve search visibility\r\nBrand identity and positioning services\r\nSocial media strategy and community management\r\nConversion rate optimization for digital campaigns', 'Pros', 'Website: www.vccp.com\r\nHeadquarters: London, United Kingdom\r\nFounded: 2002\r\nPricing: Custom, premium project or retainer-based\r\nBest Use Case: Brands wanting creative storytelling supported by measurable digital performance', '<p>VCCP is great for brands that want clever, simple creative ideas backed by strong digital strategy. Their work often becomes well-known because it feels relatable and well-crafted. They are strong in combining creativity with data, though their premium pricing may be challenging for smaller companies. For mid-size and large brands looking for effective, audience-friendly advertising, VCCP is a reliable partner.</p>', 4, 8),
(32, 'Tinuiti', 'tools/tinuiti-full-funnel-marketing-agency.jpg', '<p>Tinuiti is a performance-focused digital marketing agency known for helping brands grow across search, social, marketplaces, and streaming platforms. Unlike traditional agencies, Tinuiti built its reputation on measurable results rather than big brand campaigns. Their strength comes from deep expertise in paid media, e-commerce advertising, and data-driven customer acquisition, which has made them a go-to partner for brands selling online.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency relies heavily on analytics, automation, and media optimization tools to guide decision-making. Tinuiti uses AI to identify valuable audience groups, adjust bids in real time, and refine content so ads perform better across platforms like Google, Amazon, Meta, and TikTok. Their approach is practical and performance-based: test, learn, optimize, and scale. This makes them especially effective for brands that care about clear ROI and fast growth</p>', 'Services', 'AI-driven optimization for campaigns across major digital platforms\r\nDetailed audience segmentation and targeting\r\nReal-time bidding and automated budget adjustments\r\nCross-channel performance dashboard for clear reporting\r\nNLP tools for sentiment and message optimization\r\nStrong search marketing across paid and organic channels\r\nProgrammatic media driven by machine learning\r\nConversion rate optimization through testing and behavior insights\r\nSocial ad management with automated performance tracking\r\nAttribution modeling to understand full customer journeys', 'Important Info', 'Website: www.tinuiti.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York City, USA\r\nFounded: 2004\r\nPricing: Custom retainers, typically mid–five figures per month and up\r\nBest Use Case: Brands needing strong digital performance, e-commerce growth, and measurable ROI', '<p>Tinuiti is ideal for brands that want clear, measurable performance rather than big traditional campaigns. They excel at paid media, marketplace advertising, and optimization at scale. Their tech-driven approach delivers strong results, though it may feel complex for clients new to data-heavy marketing. Best suited for mid-size and large brands that want fast, efficient digital growth.</p>', 4, 9),
(33, 'Leo Burnett', 'tools/leo-burnett.jpg', '<p>Leo Burnett is one of the most respected advertising agencies in the world and has been shaping brand stories since 1935. The agency is known for ideas that feel warm, relatable, and rooted in real human behavior. Their HumanKind philosophy guides every project and encourages teams to focus on what people care about, not just what brands want to say. This approach has helped them create famous campaigns and characters that many people instantly recognize.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Today, Leo Burnett combines its creative strength with modern digital tools. The agency uses AI and analytics to study audience behavior, understand cultural shifts, and predict how people might respond to certain messages. They also use SEO, content planning, and media optimization techniques to make sure their ideas perform well online. This combination of human insight and smart technology helps them deliver campaigns that feel meaningful and also achieve strong business results.</p>', 'Services', 'HumanKind creative approach focused on real human experiences\r\nUse of AI and analytics for insights and campaign improvements\r\nDigital services including SEO, search marketing, and content strategy\r\nGlobal network with teams in more than 85 countries\r\nExpertise in creating brand mascots and long-lasting brand stories\r\nData modeling for targeted advertising decisions\r\nIntegrated work across digital and traditional media\r\nPurpose-driven storytelling and brand identity design\r\nAward-winning creative teams recognized across the industry', 'Pros', 'Website: www.leoburnett.com\r\nHeadquarters: Chicago, Illinois, USA\r\nFounded: 1935\r\nPricing: Premium, custom pricing based on project needs\r\nBest Use Case: Large brands seeking emotional, memorable campaigns with strong global reach', '<p>Leo Burnett is a great match for brands that want powerful storytelling backed by smart data insights. The agency is strong at creating emotional campaigns that people remember while also delivering solid performance results. They are best suited for big brands with larger budgets, but for companies looking to refresh or strengthen their identity, Leo Burnett offers exceptional creative expertise.</p>', 4, 10),
(34, 'McCann Worldgroup', 'tools/mccann-worldgroup.jpg', '<p>McCann Worldgroup is one of the most established advertising networks in the world, with roots going back to 1902. The agency is known for its core idea called &ldquo;Truth Well Told,&rdquo; which focuses on honest, human storytelling. Over the years, McCann has helped build and grow many global brands by creating work that feels real and emotionally meaningful. Their teams operate in more than 100 countries, giving them strong cultural understanding and access to diverse markets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In today&rsquo;s digital environment, McCann mixes its creative strengths with modern data and technology. The agency uses AI tools to understand what people are talking about, identify behavior patterns, and predict how audiences might respond to different messages. Their teams also use SEO, digital content strategy, and performance tracking to help brands show up better across online channels. This combination of creativity and data-driven decision-making helps them deliver campaigns that are both impactful and measurable.</p>', 'Services', 'Integrated marketing across traditional, digital, and emerging platforms\r\nAI-powered insights for audience targeting and segmentation\r\nCreative strategy and execution across TV, digital, social, and live experiences\r\nBrand development and positioning support\r\nDigital transformation services including websites and mobile apps\r\nPerformance marketing with advanced measurement tools\r\nSearch-optimized content creation and management\r\nStrong cross-cultural marketing expertise through global teams', 'Key Info', 'Website: www.mccann.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York, USA\r\nFounded: 1902\r\nPricing: Premium, retainer or project-based\r\nBest Use Case: Large global brands needing integrated creative and data-driven campaigns', '<p>McCann Worldgroup is a strong match for major brands that want creative storytelling supported by global scale and solid data insights. They deliver work that feels meaningful while still performing well across digital channels. Their size can make processes slower and costs higher, but for large organizations with complex needs, McCann offers reliable, high-quality expertise and strong worldwide capabilities.</p>', 4, 11),
(35, 'FCB Global', 'tools/fcb-global.jpg', '<p>FCB Global is one of the oldest and most established advertising agencies in the world, with roots dating back to 1873. The agency is known for strong creative ideas grounded in a deep understanding of human behavior. Their work often focuses on long-term brand building, helping companies create messages that stay consistent across many markets while still feeling relevant to local audiences. FCB&rsquo;s strength comes from blending creativity with practical strategy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In today&rsquo;s digital world, FCB uses modern tools to support their creative decisions. They rely on AI to study audience habits, predict shifts in consumer interest, and guide campaign adjustments. Their teams use SEO, content planning, and paid media strategies to help brands improve visibility online. They also analyze conversations and trends to shape messaging that feels natural and emotionally meaningful. This mix of creativity and analytics helps FCB deliver work that performs well and grows brand value.</p>', 'Services', 'Full-service support including strategy, creative, and media planning\r\nAI-driven analytics and predictive modeling\r\nNLP tools for sentiment and conversation analysis\r\nIntegrated digital approach using SEO, content, and paid media\r\nGlobal network with strong local-market expertise\r\nReal-time performance measurement and attribution modeling\r\nCross-platform campaign development\r\nStrategic consulting for brand growth and positioning\r\nCreative tech solutions including immersive and interactive content', 'Pros', 'Website: www.omc.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York, USA\r\nFounded: 1873\r\nPricing: Premium, project or retainer-based\r\nBest Use Case: Large global brands needing coordinated, insights-driven creative campaigns', '<p>FCB Global is a strong partner for brands that want smart, long-term creative ideas supported by solid research and data. They combine global scale with local knowledge, which helps them create campaigns that work in many different regions. Their services are best suited for large companies with bigger budgets, but for those clients, FCB delivers reliable, strategic, and high-impact work.</p>', 4, 12),
(36, 'inBeat', 'tools/inbeat-creative-growth-agency-in-north-america.jpg', '<p>inBeat is a modern digital agency that focuses on influencer marketing and performance-driven content. Unlike traditional agencies, inBeat built its services around creator partnerships and data, helping brands reach audiences through real people rather than large, generic media buys. Their platform makes it easy for brands to find creators who match their style, tone, and customer base, which leads to more authentic and effective campaigns.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency uses AI tools to study trends, analyze audience behavior, and measure campaign performance. They track how people respond to content, which creators drive the most engagement, and what type of posts work best on each platform. With this information, inBeat helps brands improve search visibility, refine content strategies, and choose creators who can deliver strong results. Their mix of data and creativity helps brands grow consistently across social and digital channels.</p>', 'Services', 'AI system that finds ideal creators for each brand\r\nReal-time dashboard for tracking campaign performance\r\nNLP tools that monitor sentiment and audience reactions\r\nContent optimization for better search and platform visibility\r\nAutomated media buying system for efficient budget use\r\nCreative strategy based on data and market insights\r\nCustom reports with recommendations for improvement\r\nCross-platform content distribution support\r\nManagement of long-term influencer partnerships', 'Key Info', 'Website: Inbeat.agency\r\nHeadquarters: Montreal, Canada\r\nFounded: 2017\r\nPricing: Retainers starting around 5,000 to 10,000 dollars monthly\r\nBest Use Case: Consumer brands wanting fast digital growth through influencers and data-backed content', '<p>inBeat is a great choice for brands that want to grow through creator partnerships rather than traditional ads. Their strength is speed, data, and authenticity. They provide clear performance insights and strong ROI for brands focused on digital reach. They may be expensive for small businesses, but for growing brands that want measurable results from influencer marketing, inBeat offers strong value.</p>', 4, 13),
(37, 'Column Five', 'tools/column-five-media.jpg', '<p>Column Five works with technology and software companies that struggle to explain what they build. Their team helps turn technical ideas, data, and product details into stories and visuals that people outside engineering teams can understand without confusion.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They also think about how content is found online. Their work is planned to show up in search engines and AI tools that answer questions directly. They use AI writing systems, including GPT-based tools, to match how people now search and read information.</p>', 'Services', 'Builds story frameworks specifically for software and technology products\r\nTurns technical information into diagrams, visuals, and readable content\r\nWrites content designed to appear in search engine results\r\nStructures content so AI answer tools can read and reuse it\r\nUses GPT-based systems to analyze and shape written content\r\nDesigns content around long decision-making cycles in B2B sales\r\nFocuses on explaining products clearly rather than promoting them\r\nTracks how content is read, shared, and used over time\r\nPublishes content across platforms used by technology buyers', 'Important Info', 'Website: columnfivemedia.com\r\nClient Type: B2B software and technology companies\r\nMain Work: Content structure, visuals, search-focused writing\r\nPricing: Not listed publicly\r\nCompany Size Focus: Mid-size and large companies', '<p>Column Five is useful for technology companies that have strong products but weak explanations. Their work is practical and structured, not flashy. The focus on search behavior and AI-readable content makes sense for how people now find information, but smaller companies may find the approach too heavy or expensive.</p>', 5, 1),
(38, 'Lemonly', 'tools/lemonly.jpg', '<p>Lemonly works with technology companies that need help explaining complicated ideas visually. They take technical information, numbers, and product details and turn them into images that are easier to understand. Their work is often used to explain software, data, and systems to people without technical backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They also pay attention to how visual content is found online. Their visuals are structured so search engines and AI tools can read and index them properly. They study how people interact with content and adjust layouts and formats to improve clarity and visibility.</p>', 'Services', 'Creates infographics that explain technical products and systems\r\nDesigns visuals to show data, metrics, and performance numbers\r\nProduces animated videos to explain how technology works\r\nUses data to study how people interact with visual content\r\nStructures visual files so search engines can read them\r\nAligns visuals with how search engines understand meaning\r\nBuilds interactive visual content for websites\r\nDesigns custom icons and illustrations for software brands\r\nUses data to decide how stories are visually presented\r\nAdapts visuals for use across different digital platforms', 'Important Info', 'Website: lemonly.com\r\nHeadquarters: Sioux Falls, South Dakota\r\nFounded: Around 2011\r\nPricing: Project-based, usually $10,000 to $100,000 or more\r\nBest Fit: Technology companies explaining complex products or data', '<p>Lemonly is useful for companies that rely on visuals to explain difficult ideas. Their work is clear, structured, and based on real data. The quality is high, but the cost may be too much for small teams. They are better suited for established companies with clear communication needs.</p>', 5, 2);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(39, 'Skyword', 'tools/skyword.jpg', '<p>Skyword &amp; Draft is a software platform used by technology companies to plan, create, and manage digital content. It is designed for teams that publish technical information and need a clear process for writing, editing, and organizing content that includes both text and visual elements.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform supports structured workflows for companies that produce guides, product explanations, and educational materials. It combines content planning, team coordination, visual support, and search-related tools in one system, helping teams handle complex subjects while keeping content consistent and easy to maintain.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-assisted content planning: Helps teams organize topics and outlines so complex subjects are broken into clear and logical sections.\r\nVisual asset support: Allows teams to create and manage diagrams, charts, and simple animations that explain technical ideas visually.\r\nSearch performance tracking: Shows how content performs in search results and helps teams understand which topics attract traffic.\r\nCollaborative workflow tools: Enables writers, editors, and designers to review, edit, and approve content in a shared workspace.\r\nContent distribution tools: Supports publishing content to websites and other channels from one central system.\r\nContent quality checks: Reviews text structure and readability to help improve clarity and consistency.', 'Important Information', 'Website: skyword.com\r\nProduct name: Skyword & Draft\r\nProduct type: Content creation and management platform\r\nPrimary users: Medium to large technology companies\r\nPricing model: Custom enterprise pricing\r\nMain focus: Technical and educational content management', '<p>Skyword &amp; Draft is useful for organizations that need a controlled process to manage large amounts of technical content. Its main strength is keeping planning, collaboration, and publishing in one system. A clear limitation is that the platform may not suit teams that want highly flexible design tools or a more open creative workflow.</p>', 5, 3),
(40, 'Blue Chalk Media', 'tools/bluechalk.jpg', '<p>Blue Chalk Media is a nonfiction video production agency that focuses on explaining complex topics through visual stories. The company mainly works with technology-focused organizations that need clear, accurate communication. Its work is based on real people, real situations, and documented facts rather than scripted advertising content.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency creates videos that help audiences understand how technology works and why it matters. By using documentary-style methods, Blue Chalk Media presents technical subjects in a structured and accessible way. This approach is useful for companies that need to explain products, services, or ideas to non-technical audiences.</p>', 'Service', 'Cinematic nonfiction video production – Produces documentary-style videos that present real stories and factual information clearly.\r\nTechnology-focused storytelling – Helps explain complex technical products and systems in a way that is easier to understand.\r\nStrategic content planning – Designs content based on communication goals and target audiences.\r\nMulti-platform video formats – Adapts videos for websites, social media, and presentations to ensure broad usability.\r\nData visualization – Uses charts, graphics, and visuals to simplify technical data.\r\nAudience research – Studies stakeholder needs to shape message clarity and relevance.\r\nBrand narrative development – Aligns technology explanations with a company’s purpose and values.\r\nInteractive media projects – Creates content that allows viewers to engage more actively with information.\r\nDistribution planning – Supports decisions on where and how content should be shared for effectiveness.', 'Important Information', 'Website: bluechalk.com\r\nCompany Type: Nonfiction video production agency\r\nSpecialization: Technology and complex subject storytelling\r\nPricing Model: Project-based, custom pricing\r\nBest For: Established companies needing clear explanations of complex ideas', '<p>Blue Chalk Media&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to present complex technical topics through clear, factual storytelling. This helps audiences understand information without oversimplification. A limitation is that its project-based and premium-focused approach may not be suitable for smaller companies with limited budgets or short-term content needs.</p>', 5, 4),
(41, 'Velocity Partners', 'tools/velocitypartners.jpg', '<p>Velocity Partners is a visual storytelling agency that works mainly with technology companies. It helps explain complex products and ideas using clear visuals and structured content. The goal is to make technical information easier to understand for business audiences, customers, and decision-makers without losing important details.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency focuses on combining design, data, and content structure. It uses modern tools, including AI-based systems, to organize information and present it in a clear visual format. Their work is often used for product explanations, marketing content, and educational materials in digital platforms.</p>', 'Services', 'AI-based visual content creation – Uses technical documents as input and converts them into structured visual content for easier understanding\r\nData visualization – Turns complex numbers and system metrics into charts and visuals that are easier to read\r\nInteractive storytelling – Adds interactive elements so users can explore information instead of only reading it\r\nNLP-supported content optimization – Analyzes language and intent to improve clarity and search relevance\r\nStructured data usage – Applies proper data structure so search engines can index content more accurately\r\nAnimated explainer videos – Uses motion graphics to show how technology products or systems work\r\nResponsive design – Ensures visuals work well on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices\r\nPerformance analytics – Tracks user behavior such as engagement and conversions to measure content impact\r\nMarketing system integration – Connects with existing CMS and marketing tools used by companies\r\nNarrative planning – Aligns technical features with real business problems in a logical way', 'Important Information', 'Website: velocitypartners.com\r\nCompany type: Visual storytelling and content agency\r\nPrimary focus: Technology and B2B companies\r\nPricing model: High-end, project-based or retainer\r\nTypical clients: Mid-size to large technology firms', '<p>One clear strength of Velocity Partners is its ability to present technical information in a structured and understandable visual format without removing important details. A limitation is that its pricing and service model may not be suitable for small or early-stage companies with limited budgets.</p>', 5, 5),
(42, 'Superside', 'tools/superside.jpg', '<p>Superside is a creative services platform that helps technology companies produce visual content on an ongoing basis. Instead of hiring full-time designers, companies subscribe to Superside and request design work as needed. The service focuses on making complex technical ideas easier to understand through clear visual formats.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company works with a distributed team of professional designers who have experience in technology-related projects. Superside combines human design work with software tools to manage tasks, timelines, and quality. This model is mainly used by companies that need regular design support across different teams.</p>', 'Service', 'Subscription-based design service: Companies pay a monthly fee and can request design work without separate contracts.\r\nGlobal designer network: Work is handled by designers from different regions with experience in technology topics.\r\nAI-supported project management: Internal systems help assign tasks, track progress, and reduce delays.\r\nFast delivery timelines: Standard design requests are usually completed within one to two days.\r\nScalable output: Design capacity can increase or decrease based on changing business needs.\r\nData visualization support: Designers create charts, diagrams, and visuals to explain technical data.\r\nProduct and brand visuals: Design work focuses on explaining products and core messages clearly.\r\nDedicated account support: Clients work with assigned managers who coordinate requests and feedback.\r\nTool integration: The platform connects with common collaboration and productivity tools.\r\nPerformance tracking: Some results are measured to understand how visual content is used and received.', 'Important Information', 'Website: superside.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2015\r\nService model: Monthly subscription\r\nStarting price: Around $3,000 per month\r\nTypical users: Technology and SaaS companies\r\nCommon uses: Marketing materials, product visuals, presentations', '<p>Superside&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to deliver consistent design work quickly through a subscription model, which suits teams with ongoing needs. A limitation is that the service may not be cost-effective for companies that only need design support occasionally or for short-term projects.</p>', 5, 6),
(43, 'Fellow', 'tools/fellow.jpg', '<p>Fellow is a visual storytelling agency that works mainly with technology companies. They combine analysis and design to help businesses explain complex products and ideas in ways that are easy to understand. Their work focuses on creating visuals that communicate clearly to target audiences while staying consistent across platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency also uses AI tools to study audience behavior and preferences. This helps them make content that connects with viewers and performs well online. They turn technical language into understandable messages and create strategies that align visual content with business goals.</p>', 'Service', 'Data-driven brand strategy: Aligns visual storytelling with business goals to make content purposeful.\r\nAI-powered audience analysis: Uses AI to understand audience interests and tailor visuals for better engagement.\r\nVisual identity systems: Designs consistent logos, colors, and styles for tech companies and their products.\r\nInteractive digital experiences: Builds engaging visuals that explain complex technology clearly and intuitively.\r\nContent optimized for search: Creates visuals and messages that improve online visibility and algorithm ranking.\r\nNLP-enhanced messaging: Converts technical terms into understandable stories that appeal to a broader audience.\r\nCross-platform consistency: Ensures the brand looks uniform across websites, social media, and physical materials.\r\nPerformance analytics dashboard: Measures how well visuals and campaigns are performing.\r\nMarketing integration: Works with existing CRM and marketing tools to streamline campaigns.\r\nScalable visual solutions: Provides designs that grow with companies from startup to enterprise level.', 'Important Information', 'Website: fellow.agency\r\nHeadquarters: London\r\nFounded: Around 2015\r\nPricing: Premium, project-based (£15,000–£100,000+)\r\nBest Use Case: Technology companies that need clear visual explanations of complex products and services', '<p>Fellow is strong at turning complex technical ideas into clear visuals, which is useful for tech companies and startups. A limitation is that their services may be too specialized or expensive for small businesses or non-technology sectors.</p>', 5, 7),
(44, 'ScienceSoft', 'tools/sciencesoft.jpg', '<p>ScienceSoft is an IT consulting and software services company that started in 1989. Over the years, it has worked with businesses from many industries and has built long-term experience in software development, infrastructure, and IT operations. This background allows the company to understand both old systems and modern platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In DevOps consulting, ScienceSoft focuses on improving how software is built, tested, deployed, and maintained. Their work usually involves helping development and operations teams work together, automate routine tasks, and reduce delays in software delivery while keeping systems stable and secure.</p>', 'Service', 'DevOps assessment and planning – Reviews current processes and systems to identify problems and define a clear DevOps roadmap.\r\nCI/CD pipeline setup – Automates building, testing, and deploying code to reduce manual errors and speed up releases.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC) – Manages servers and cloud resources using code, making environments consistent and easier to reproduce.\r\nContainerization and orchestration – Uses Docker and Kubernetes to run applications in isolated containers and manage them at scale.\r\nCloud DevOps support – Applies DevOps practices on AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud to improve flexibility and resource management.\r\nMonitoring and observability – Tracks system performance and errors using tools like Prometheus and Grafana to detect issues early.\r\nDevSecOps integration – Adds security checks into development pipelines so risks are found earlier, not after deployment.\r\nCustom DevOps toolchains – Builds or configures tools that fit a company’s existing workflows instead of forcing generic setups.\r\nPerformance analysis – Identifies slow or inefficient parts of current DevOps processes and suggests improvements.\r\nDevOps training – Trains internal teams so they can manage and improve DevOps practices on their own.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.sciencesoft.com/\r\nFounded: 1989\r\nTeam size: 750+ IT professionals\r\nExperience: 4,200+ completed projects\r\nIndustries served: 30+\r\nPricing: Custom, based on project scope\r\nBest for: Medium and large enterprises', '<p>ScienceSoft&rsquo;s main strength is its long experience working with complex enterprise systems, which helps when modernizing existing environments. A limitation is that its services are designed mainly for larger organizations, so smaller companies or startups may find the cost and scope more than they need.</p>', 6, 1),
(45, 'Simform', 'tools/simform.jpg', '<p>Simform is a technology consulting company that helps organizations improve how they build, deploy, and manage software systems. It focuses mainly on DevOps practices and cloud-based systems, especially for companies that rely on older technology that is hard to maintain or scale.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company works with businesses to move their systems to modern cloud environments and to improve collaboration between development and operations teams. Its work usually combines technical changes with process improvements so software can be delivered faster, more reliably, and with better control.</p>', 'Service', 'Cloud-native system migration: Helps companies move from old systems to cloud-based platforms that are easier to scale and maintain.\r\nCI/CD pipeline setup: Builds automated pipelines so code can be tested and deployed more frequently with fewer manual steps.\r\nDevelopment automation: Uses tools to reduce repetitive tasks, which helps teams release updates faster.\r\nBuilt-in security (DevSecOps): Adds security checks throughout the development process instead of treating security as a final step.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC): Manages servers and cloud resources through code, making setups repeatable and easier to track.\r\nContainerization and orchestration: Uses Docker and Kubernetes to package applications and manage them across different environments.\r\nMonitoring and observability: Provides tools to track system health and performance in real time to detect issues early.\r\nTeam process improvement: Helps development and operations teams work together more effectively.\r\nMulti-cloud planning: Designs systems that can run across different cloud providers to reduce dependency on one vendor.\r\nPerformance measurement: Uses clear metrics to track system reliability, deployment speed, and overall improvement.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.simform.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly specified\r\nFounded: Not publicly specified\r\nPricing: Custom pricing based on project scope\r\nBest suited for: Medium to large companies modernizing legacy systems', '<p>Simform&rsquo;s main strength is its structured approach to modernizing older systems using cloud and DevOps practices. This can be useful for companies lacking internal expertise. A limitation is the limited public detail about past projects or industry-specific results, which may make evaluation harder for new clients.</p>', 6, 2),
(46, 'XenonStack', 'tools/xenonstack.jpg', '<p>XenonStack is a DevOps consulting company that focuses on combining DevOps practices with artificial intelligence. It helps organizations manage software delivery, infrastructure, and operations using automation, data, and governed workflows. The company mainly works with enterprises that operate complex systems and large-scale platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A key part of XenonStack&rsquo;s approach is using AI to support decision-making in IT operations. Its services cover cloud-native systems, data platforms, and DevOps processes. The goal is to help organizations improve visibility, control, and efficiency while keeping systems secure and compliant.</p>', 'Service', 'AI Reasoning Foundry\r\nA platform that connects data, logic, and governance so automated systems can make controlled and explainable decisions.\r\nDevOps Consulting\r\nHelps teams set up CI/CD pipelines and DevOps workflows to reduce manual work and improve software delivery speed.\r\nCloud-Native Solutions\r\nSupports migration to cloud environments and use of containers to improve scalability and reliability.\r\nData Science and Analytics\r\nUses data processing and machine learning to turn operational data into useful insights.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC)\r\nAutomates infrastructure setup using tools like Terraform to reduce configuration errors and manual effort.\r\nMicroservices Architecture\r\nDesigns applications as small services to make systems easier to scale and maintain.\r\nDevOps Training and Bootcamps\r\nProvides structured learning programs to help teams build DevOps and technical skills.\r\nRelease Management\r\nOrganizes deployment and update processes to reduce downtime and release-related risks.\r\nAgentic Process Automation\r\nApplies AI-driven automation to business operations like supply chains to reduce delays and inefficiencies.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.xenonstack.com/\r\nPricing: Custom, enterprise-focused\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly specified\r\nFounded: Not publicly specified\r\nTarget Customers: Medium to large enterprises\r\nPrimary Focus: AI-enabled DevOps and automation', '<p>XenonStack&rsquo;s main strength is its structured use of AI alongside DevOps, which is useful for complex and regulated environments. A limitation is that its solutions may be too advanced for smaller teams with basic DevOps needs, and the lack of public pricing and company background may reduce transparency for some buyers.</p>', 6, 3),
(47, 'OpenXcell', 'tools/openxcell.jpg', '<p>OpenXcell is a DevOps consulting company that focuses on using artificial intelligence and machine learning alongside standard DevOps practices. The company helps organizations automate software delivery, manage infrastructure more efficiently, and improve system reliability through data-driven methods.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Their work combines CI/CD automation, cloud-native development, and AI-based monitoring. By applying machine learning to deployment and operations tasks, OpenXcell supports businesses that want faster releases, better system visibility, and more predictable performance in modern digital environments.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-based CI/CD optimization\r\nUses machine learning to automate testing and deployments, reducing manual errors and release time.\r\nPredictive system monitoring\r\nAnalyzes system data to detect potential issues before they cause outages.\r\nNLP-based documentation tools\r\nHelps teams create and manage technical documentation more efficiently using language processing.\r\nAutomated infrastructure provisioning\r\nAllocates cloud resources automatically based on usage patterns and demand.\r\nAI-assisted security scanning (DevSecOps)\r\nIdentifies vulnerabilities early by applying intelligent security checks in the development pipeline.\r\nCustom MLOps pipelines\r\nSupports deployment and management of machine learning models in production environments.\r\nIncident response chatbots\r\nAutomates common operational responses and improves team communication during issues.\r\nContainer and orchestration support\r\nBuilds and manages cloud-native applications using containers and orchestration tools.\r\nPerformance analytics\r\nUses data analysis to identify performance bottlenecks and optimization opportunities.\r\nDevOps metrics and KPIs tracking\r\nCollects operational data to measure efficiency and guide continuous improvement.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.openxcell.com/\r\nCompany Type: DevOps and software consulting services\r\nHeadquarters: Global operations (exact location not publicly emphasized)\r\nFounded: Early 2010s\r\nPricing Model: Custom pricing based on project scope\r\nTarget Clients: Mid-size to large organizations\r\nPrimary Focus: AI-integrated DevOps and digital transformation', '<p>OpenXcell&rsquo;s main strength is its practical use of AI to improve automation, monitoring, and deployment processes. This approach is suitable for companies with complex systems and data-driven goals. A possible limitation is that smaller teams with simple needs may find these solutions more advanced than required.</p>', 6, 4),
(48, 'Algoworks', 'tools/algoworks.jpg', '<p>Algoworks provides DevOps consulting services that help organizations improve how they build, deploy, and manage software. Their work focuses on reducing delays between development and operations by improving processes, automation, and infrastructure setup across cloud environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company also applies artificial intelligence and machine learning in selected DevOps tasks, such as monitoring and incident handling. Along with technical implementation, Algoworks supports teams in adopting DevOps practices through planning, training, and ongoing operational support.</p>', 'Service', 'DevOps strategy and roadmap planning\r\nHelps organizations define clear steps for adopting DevOps based on their current systems and business goals.\r\nCI/CD pipeline implementation\r\nAutomates code testing and deployment so software updates can be released faster and with fewer manual errors.\r\nCloud infrastructure management\r\nSets up and manages resources on AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud to improve scalability and reliability.\r\nDocker and Kubernetes adoption\r\nUses containers to make applications easier to deploy and manage across different environments.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC)\r\nAutomates server and infrastructure setup using tools like Terraform and CloudFormation to reduce configuration mistakes.\r\nDevSecOps integration\r\nAdds automated security checks into development pipelines to detect vulnerabilities early.\r\nMonitoring and observability\r\nTracks system performance and health to identify issues before they affect users.\r\nPredictive incident management\r\nUses machine learning to detect patterns that may indicate upcoming system failures.\r\nDevOps training and enablement\r\nTrains teams to use DevOps tools and follow consistent development and deployment practices.\r\nManaged DevOps services\r\nProvides ongoing support and maintenance for DevOps systems, including 24/7 monitoring.', 'Important Information', 'Company name: Algoworks\r\nWebsite: https://www.algoworks.com/\r\nPrimary services: DevOps consulting and cloud services\r\nTarget clients: Mid to large organizations\r\nPricing model: Custom, based on project scope\r\nFocus areas: Cloud, automation, CI/CD, DevSecOps', '<p>Algoworks&rsquo; main strength is its broad coverage of the full DevOps lifecycle, from planning to long-term support. A limitation is the lack of detailed public case studies with measurable results, which makes it harder to assess real-world impact before engagement.</p>', 6, 5),
(49, 'Clarion Technologies', 'tools/clarion-technologies.jpg', '<p>Clarion Technologies is a software development and IT consulting company that focuses on DevOps transformation and cloud-based systems. It works with organizations that want to improve how software is built, tested, and deployed by using automation, structured processes, and modern cloud platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company supports full DevOps adoption, from planning to long-term operations. Its work often involves cloud migration, automation of delivery pipelines, and improving system stability. Clarion also applies data analysis techniques to help teams detect issues earlier and manage infrastructure more efficiently.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-Based DevOps Analytics: Uses data from pipelines and systems to detect unusual behavior and identify the cause of failures faster.\r\nMulti-Cloud Management: Helps teams run applications across AWS, Azure, and GCP without locking into a single provider.\r\nCI/CD Pipeline Automation: Builds automated pipelines that reduce manual steps and catch errors earlier in development.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC): Creates reusable configuration files so environments can be rebuilt consistently and audited easily.\r\nLog Analysis with NLP: Analyzes large volumes of logs to group errors and make troubleshooting quicker.\r\nDevSecOps Practices: Adds security checks into development workflows to reduce risks before software goes live.\r\nContainers and Microservices: Designs systems using Docker and Kubernetes to improve scalability and reliability.\r\nCost and Performance Monitoring: Reviews cloud usage data to reduce wasted resources and improve system performance.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.clariontech.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Pune, India\r\nFounded: Around 2001\r\nEngagement Models: Fixed price, time and materials, or dedicated teams\r\nTypical Project Size: Mid to large enterprise engagements\r\nPrimary Clients: Medium and large organizations\r\nFocus Areas: DevOps, cloud migration, automation, compliance-driven environments', '<p>Clarion Technologies&rsquo; main strength is its ability to combine DevOps automation with data-driven monitoring, which helps reduce operational issues over time. A limitation is that its services may be less accessible for smaller teams due to cost and scope, making it more suitable for long-term, enterprise-level projects.</p>', 6, 6),
(50, 'PixelCrayons', 'tools/pixelcrayons.jpg', '<p>PixelCrayons is a technology consulting company that provides DevOps, cloud, and automation services for businesses. The company focuses on improving how software is built, tested, and deployed by using structured DevOps practices and cloud-based infrastructure. Its services are mainly designed for organizations running complex or large-scale systems.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company combines DevOps processes with data analysis and automation to improve system stability and delivery speed. By working across cloud platforms and modern deployment tools, PixelCrayons helps teams manage infrastructure more consistently and reduce manual operational work during software releases.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-Based DevOps Automation: Uses data patterns to detect issues early and reduce manual incident investigation.\r\nCI/CD Pipeline Setup: Builds automated pipelines to test and deploy code faster with fewer human errors.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC): Creates repeatable cloud setups using code to avoid configuration inconsistencies.\r\nCloud Migration and Optimization: Moves applications to AWS, Azure, or GCP while improving cost and performance control.\r\nContainer and Kubernetes Management: Helps teams run applications in containers for better scalability and portability.\r\nMonitoring and Log Analysis: Analyzes system logs and metrics to identify failures and performance bottlenecks.\r\nDevSecOps Practices: Adds security checks into development pipelines to catch vulnerabilities earlier.\r\nPerformance and Scaling Reviews: Reviews system usage data to adjust resources based on real demand.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.pixelcrayons.com/\r\nCompany Type: Digital transformation and IT consulting firm\r\nPrimary Services: DevOps, cloud infrastructure, automation\r\nClient Focus: Medium to large organizations\r\nDelivery Model: Global delivery with offshore teams\r\nPricing: Project-based custom pricing\r\nIndustry Usage: Finance, healthcare, e-commerce, enterprise IT', '<p>PixelCrayons&rsquo; main strength is its broad DevOps coverage, from infrastructure setup to monitoring and security integration. This makes it suitable for enterprises with complex systems. A limitation is that pricing and service depth may not fit small startups or teams with limited budgets and simpler infrastructure needs.</p>', 6, 7),
(51, 'Qentelli', 'tools/qentelli.jpg', '<p>Qentelli is a technology consulting company that helps organizations improve how they build, deploy, and manage software. Its main focus is DevOps, cloud platforms, and automation. The company works with businesses that want to move away from slow, manual IT processes and adopt more reliable and repeatable systems.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company supports organizations through planning, implementation, and long-term improvement of DevOps practices. Instead of only setting up tools, Qentelli also helps teams adjust workflows and responsibilities. This approach is aimed at making software delivery faster, more stable, and easier to maintain over time.</p>', 'Service', 'DevOps assessment and transformation – Reviews existing systems and processes to identify gaps and create a clear DevOps improvement plan.\r\nCI/CD pipeline setup – Automates code building, testing, and deployment to reduce manual errors and speed up releases.\r\nCloud migration and optimization – Moves applications to cloud platforms and adjusts resources to improve performance and control costs.\r\nKubernetes and container management – Uses containers to make applications easier to deploy, scale, and maintain across environments.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC) – Manages servers and cloud resources through code to ensure consistency and faster recovery.\r\nDevSecOps integration – Adds security checks into development and deployment to find risks earlier.\r\nMonitoring and observability – Tracks system health and behavior to detect issues before they affect users.\r\nAutomated testing – Runs tests automatically to catch bugs early and maintain software quality.\r\nPerformance optimization – Identifies bottlenecks and improves system response and stability.\r\nDevOps training – Trains internal teams so they can manage and improve DevOps systems independently.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.qentelli.com/\r\nIndustry focus: DevOps, cloud, automation, and digital transformation\r\nClient type: Medium to large organizations\r\nEngagement models: Project-based, managed services, and long-term support\r\nCommon use cases: Legacy system modernization and enterprise-scale DevOps adoption', '<p>Qentelli&rsquo;s main strength is its structured approach that combines technical work with process improvement, which helps organizations adopt DevOps more consistently. A possible limitation is that smaller teams or companies with simple systems may find the scope broader than they need, making the engagement more complex than necessary.</p>', 6, 8),
(52, 'Appinventiv', '', '<p>Appinventiv is an IT service company that provides DevOps consulting along with other technology solutions. They focus on combining artificial intelligence with development and operations processes to help businesses improve software delivery and manage cloud infrastructure efficiently. Their team works with a variety of industries to design practical DevOps strategies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Founded around 2015-2016, Appinventiv has delivered thousands of digital projects globally. They aim to support medium to large companies in streamlining their CI/CD pipelines, automating testing, and optimizing infrastructure. Their AI-driven approach helps predict potential system issues and allocate resources effectively, making operations more reliable and cost-efficient.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-driven DevOps automation: Detects potential infrastructure problems before they affect operations, reducing downtime.\r\nCI/CD pipeline design: Builds automated development and deployment processes with intelligent testing to speed up software delivery.\r\nCloud optimization: Uses AI to allocate resources efficiently and scale cloud infrastructure as needed.\r\nCustom DevOps strategy consulting: Creates DevOps plans tailored to a company’s specific industry and goals.\r\n24/7 managed DevOps services: Provides continuous monitoring and maintenance to prevent system failures.\r\nContainerization and microservices: Implements scalable applications with orchestration tools for easier management.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC): Automates infrastructure setup and updates through code, improving consistency and version control.\r\nDevSecOps integration: Adds security checks and AI-powered vulnerability scanning throughout the DevOps pipeline.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://appinventiv.com/\r\nHeadquarters: USA, with offices in Dubai and other locations\r\nFounded: Around 2015-2016\r\nPricing: Custom pricing based on project needs\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large enterprises needing AI-enhanced DevOps transformation', '<p>Appinventiv&rsquo;s main strength is its AI-focused DevOps approach, which helps companies predict issues and manage resources efficiently. A limitation is that their services may be less accessible for small businesses due to a focus on larger enterprise clients. Overall, they are suitable for organizations looking for structured, technology-driven DevOps solutions.</p>', 6, 9),
(53, 'Svitla Systems', 'tools/svitla-systems.jpg', '<p>Svitla Systems is a global technology company that provides DevOps consulting and IT solutions. The company helps organizations improve the way they develop and manage software by combining development and operations practices. Their services aim to make software delivery faster, more reliable, and easier to manage.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They work with different industries and offer services that support both small improvements and large-scale digital transformations. By using modern tools and automation, they help clients manage cloud infrastructure, ensure security, and maintain system stability while improving overall operational efficiency.</p>', 'Service', 'DevOps Transformation Services: Provides planning and implementation support to help organizations adopt DevOps practices and improve software workflows.\r\nCI/CD Pipeline Automation: Automates software build, test, and deployment processes to speed up release cycles.\r\nCloud Infrastructure Management: Optimizes and manages resources across cloud platforms to reduce costs and improve performance.\r\nContainerization and Orchestration: Uses tools like Docker and Kubernetes to package applications and manage them efficiently in different environments.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC): Implements tools like Terraform and Ansible to define infrastructure in code, making setup and updates easier and consistent.\r\nDevSecOps Practices: Integrates security checks into the development process to prevent vulnerabilities early.\r\nMonitoring and Observability: Tracks system performance and detects issues to keep services reliable.\r\nGlobal Delivery Model: Provides around-the-clock support for enterprise clients to ensure continuous operations.\r\nCustomized Solutions: Adapts services to specific industries or business needs for better results.\r\nEnterprise Experience: Works with large companies and startups to apply proven DevOps methods.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://svitla.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not clearly specified\r\nFounded: Not clearly specified\r\nPricing: Enterprise-level pricing typical of global consulting firms\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large businesses looking for end-to-end DevOps support.', '<p>Svitla Systems is strong in delivering comprehensive DevOps solutions that improve both technical operations and business processes. They have experience handling large and complex IT environments, which is useful for enterprise clients. A potential limitation is that their services may be expensive for smaller organizations or very niche DevOps needs.</p>', 6, 10),
(54, 'OpsTree', 'tools/opstree.jpg', '<p>OpsTree is a DevOps consulting company that helps businesses improve how they manage IT operations. They focus on automating workflows, setting up efficient deployment pipelines, and using cloud-based systems to make IT processes faster and more reliable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company also uses AI tools to monitor systems and predict issues before they happen. Their services aim to reduce manual work, improve system performance, and support companies in adopting modern DevOps practices across their IT infrastructure.</p>', 'Service', 'DevOps assessment and roadmap development: Evaluates a company’s current IT processes and creates a plan for improvement.\r\nCI/CD pipeline design and optimization: Sets up automated systems for building, testing, and deploying software to speed up releases.\r\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC) with Terraform and Ansible: Allows IT teams to manage servers and configurations through code, reducing errors and manual work.\r\nContainerization and orchestration with Docker and Kubernetes: Packages applications for consistent deployment and manages multiple containers efficiently.\r\nCloud migration and multi-cloud strategy: Helps move applications to the cloud and manage resources across different cloud providers.\r\nAI-powered monitoring and predictive analytics: Uses machine learning to detect issues early and predict system performance problems.\r\nAutomated testing and quality assurance integration: Ensures software works correctly and reduces the risk of errors in production.\r\nSecurity integration into DevOps pipelines (DevSecOps): Embeds security checks into software development to prevent vulnerabilities.\r\nPerformance optimization and capacity planning: Analyzes system usage to improve speed and plan for future growth.\r\nContinuous improvement and operational maturity assessment: Regularly reviews processes to make IT operations more efficient over time.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.opstree.com/\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, CA, or Bangalore, India\r\nFounded: Around 2015\r\nPricing: Based on project scope, typically $15,000–$100,000+\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large enterprises undergoing digital transformation', '<p>OpsTree is strong in helping large organizations implement full DevOps transformations, particularly in automating deployments and using cloud systems. One limitation is that their services can be expensive and may not suit small companies with simple needs. Their approach works best for organizations needing comprehensive IT process improvements.</p>', 6, 11),
(55, 'RTS Labs', 'tools/rts-labs.jpg', '<p>RTS Labs is a technology consulting company that provides services in DevOps, data engineering, and enterprise AI. They help organizations combine AI tools with DevOps practices to improve workflow efficiency and automate repetitive processes. Their approach focuses on using technology to support data-driven decision-making.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company works with complex infrastructure systems, offering services from cloud management to software deployment. They aim to help businesses set up systems that are easier to monitor, scale, and maintain. RTS Labs serves mid to large enterprises that want to integrate AI into their operational processes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features:</strong></p>', 'Service', 'Enterprise AI Consulting: Designs custom AI and machine learning solutions to solve business-specific problems.\r\nData Engineering Services: Builds and optimizes data pipelines for smoother processing and analysis of large datasets.\r\nDevOps Consulting: Guides teams on technical and cultural practices to improve collaboration and software delivery.\r\nCI/CD Pipeline Implementation: Automates software building, testing, and deployment with AI-assisted quality checks.\r\nCloud Infrastructure Management: Manages cloud resources on AWS, Azure, and GCP for reliability and scalability.\r\nContainerization and Orchestration: Uses Docker and Kubernetes to package applications and manage them efficiently.\r\nInfrastructure as Code: Automates infrastructure setup and updates using tools like Terraform and CloudFormation.\r\nMicroservices Architecture: Designs modular software systems that are easier to maintain and scale.\r\nAI-driven Monitoring: Tracks system performance using AI to detect issues early and improve reliability.\r\nIntelligent Automation: Automates deployment and scaling tasks to reduce manual work and errors.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.rtslabs.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly disclosed\r\nFounded: Not publicly disclosed\r\nPricing: Custom pricing depending on project requirements\r\nBest Use Case: Mid to large enterprises looking to integrate AI with DevOps workflows', '<p>RTS Labs has strong technical expertise, especially in combining AI with DevOps to improve automation and decision-making. A limitation is that there is little publicly available information on client results or case studies, which makes it harder to evaluate how effective their solutions are in practice.</p>', 6, 12),
(56, 'NetReputation', 'tools/netreputation.jpg', '<p>NetReputation is a company that helps individuals and businesses manage how they appear online. They focus on monitoring, improving, and controlling digital information to make sure that search results and social media reflect a positive image. Their tools track online mentions and analyze public perception.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company uses technology to identify negative content and promote positive information. They provide strategies to fix online reputation issues and maintain a strong online presence. Their services are suitable for anyone who wants to manage personal or business information on the internet effectively.</p>', 'Service', 'Online Reputation Monitoring: Tracks mentions of a person or brand across search engines, social media, and review sites to spot potential issues early.\r\nNegative Content Suppression: Uses search engine optimization (SEO) and content strategies to reduce the visibility of harmful or unwanted content.\r\nPositive Content Promotion: Creates and shares articles, press releases, and media to highlight favorable information online.\r\nAI-Powered Sentiment Analysis: Uses artificial intelligence to understand public opinion and detect reputation risks from online comments and posts.\r\nPersonalized Reputation Repair: Provides tailored strategies to address specific online reputation problems for individuals or businesses.\r\nReview Management: Helps manage customer reviews and respond to feedback to maintain a good online image.\r\nCrisis Management: Offers quick response services to handle urgent reputation issues.\r\nAnalytics and Reporting: Provides regular reports showing reputation changes and improvements over time.\r\nWikipedia Page Services: Creates or manages Wikipedia pages to enhance credibility.\r\nPersonal Branding Services: Supports executives and public figures in building a professional online presence.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.netreputation.com/\r\nLikely based in the United States\r\nEstimated founding: mid-2010s\r\nPricing: Approximately $500–$10,000+ per month depending on services\r\nBest Use Case: Individuals or businesses wanting to fix negative online content or maintain a positive digital presence', '<p>NetReputation is strong at using technology to track and improve online presence, making it easier to spot and address issues. A limitation is that some content, like news articles or public records, cannot be removed. Overall, it works well for managing visible reputation but may not fully control all online content.</p>', 7, 1),
(57, 'NP Digital', 'tools/np-digital.jpg', '<p>NP Digital is a digital marketing agency founded by Neil Patel, focused on helping companies manage their online reputation and visibility. They use technology and data analysis to monitor how brands appear on search engines, social media, and review platforms. Their services are aimed at improving how companies are perceived online.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company combines artificial intelligence with human expertise to track sentiment, predict potential issues, and provide strategies to handle negative content. They also integrate these efforts with SEO and content planning to maintain a consistent online presence for clients, especially those with complex or international digital footprints.</p>', 'Service', 'AI Sentiment Monitoring: Tracks mentions of a brand across many websites and social platforms, detecting positive or negative trends early.\r\nPredictive Crisis Alerts: Uses past data and current trends to forecast potential reputation problems before they escalate.\r\nSearch Result Management: Helps reduce negative content visibility and promote positive pages in search engine results.\r\nReview Management: Automates collection of genuine customer reviews and identifies fake or harmful feedback.\r\nCentral Dashboard: Shows brand health metrics, sentiment scores, and the impact of campaigns in one place.\r\nCrisis Response Templates: Provides ready-to-use guides to handle various reputation issues quickly.\r\nCompetitor Analysis: Compares a brand’s online reputation with key competitors to identify gaps and opportunities.\r\nCross-Platform Management: Coordinates responses to negative content across search engines, social media, review sites, and news outlets.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://npdigital.com/\r\nHeadquarters: San Diego, California\r\nGlobal Offices: Present in 10+ countries\r\nFounded: 2017 (rebranded from Neil Patel Digital)\r\nPricing: Custom packages, usually $5,000–$20,000+ per month\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-to-large companies needing continuous online reputation monitoring and improvement', '<p>NP Digital is strong at combining technology and human strategy to improve online reputation, particularly in search results. One limitation is its high cost, which may not be suitable for small businesses. The company works well for brands needing consistent monitoring, but the AI-driven system can feel standardized for very specific or unusual industry problems.</p>', 7, 2),
(58, 'Thrive Internet Marketing Agency', 'tools/thrive-internet-marketing-agency.jpg', '<p>Thrive Internet Marketing Agency is a full-service digital marketing company based in Ellicott City, Maryland. They help businesses manage their online reputation by tracking brand mentions, responding to reviews, and improving overall visibility across search engines and social media. Their approach combines traditional reputation monitoring with modern digital tools.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The agency also integrates reputation management with content creation, SEO, and social media strategies. This helps businesses not only address negative content but also promote positive information. Their services are designed for small to medium businesses that want to maintain a professional online image and track results with measurable data.</p>', 'Service', 'Brand Monitoring: Tracks mentions of your business online to see what people are saying and identify potential issues quickly.\r\nContent Development: Creates articles, posts, and other content to highlight positive aspects of your brand.\r\nReview Management: Monitors customer reviews, responds appropriately, and analyzes feedback to improve reputation.\r\nSearch Engine Suppression: Reduces visibility of negative content while promoting positive pages and articles.\r\nSocial Media Management: Ensures brand messaging is consistent across social platforms and handles online interactions.\r\nCrisis Response: Plans and executes actions to manage urgent reputation problems effectively.\r\nLocal SEO: Improves visibility for searches in specific geographic areas important to your business.\r\nAnalytics Dashboard: Provides data on brand mentions, engagement, and competitor comparisons to guide strategy.\r\nPersonalized Strategy: Offers customized plans based on your industry, goals, and reputation challenges.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.thriveagency.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Ellicott City, MD\r\nFounded: Mid-2000s (estimated)\r\nPricing: Starts at $1,000/month, varies by service scope\r\nBest Use Case: Small to medium businesses needing integrated reputation and digital marketing', '<p>Thrive&rsquo;s main strength is combining reputation management with other digital marketing services, creating a unified approach. One limitation is that their pricing may be high for very small businesses or startups. Overall, their methods are practical for businesses that want measurable improvements in online presence and brand perception without focusing solely on reputation.</p>', 7, 3);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(59, 'InboundJunction', '', '<p>InboundJunction is a company that helps businesses manage their online reputation. They focus on improving how brands appear on search engines and online platforms, making sure positive content is more visible while reducing the impact of negative mentions. They use data and technology to guide these efforts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company uses artificial intelligence and advanced analytics to monitor mentions of a brand across the internet. This allows them to identify potential problems quickly and take steps to improve a brand&rsquo;s online image. They also create and optimize content to maintain a strong and trustworthy digital presence.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-Powered Sentiment Monitoring: Uses AI to track mentions of a brand online and identifies whether they are positive, negative, or neutral.\r\nSERP Suppression & Positive Content Amplification: Publishes optimized content to push negative results lower in search rankings and highlight positive information.\r\nTechnical SEO & Indexing Optimization: Improves website structure, metadata, and crawlability to make sure positive content appears faster in search results.\r\nReview Management & Response Automation: Helps collect, monitor, and respond to customer reviews using AI suggestions for effective replies.\r\nCrisis Mitigation Protocols: Offers steps to quickly address negative content online, including legal support and takedown requests.\r\nPredictive Reputation Analytics: Uses historical and industry data to forecast potential reputation risks before they grow.\r\nMulti-Lingual Content Strategy: Creates content in different languages to manage reputation across multiple countries and cultures.\r\nCompetitive Benchmarking: Analyzes competitor online reputations to find weaknesses or opportunities for improvement.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.inboundjunction.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Amsterdam, Netherlands (inferred from market focus)\r\nFounded: Active since at least the early 2020s\r\nPricing: Custom plans, roughly €3,000–€10,000+ per month\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-to-large businesses in regulated or high-trust industries needing SERP control and multilingual reputation management', '<p>InboundJunction is strong in using AI and technical SEO to maintain long-term positive search results, which helps companies manage their reputation proactively. A limitation is that their services can be expensive and may not show immediate results in urgent situations like sudden viral negative content.</p>', 7, 4),
(60, 'Reputation Rhino', 'tools/reputation-rhino.jpg', '<p>Reputation Rhino is a company that helps businesses and individuals manage their online presence. They focus on identifying negative content and promoting positive information across websites, social media, and search engines. Their work aims to improve how a brand or person appears online.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company uses technology to monitor digital mentions and analyze public sentiment. They combine content strategy with search engine techniques to position favorable information higher in search results. This helps clients protect their reputation and maintain a professional online image over time.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-powered sentiment analysis: Detects whether online mentions are positive, negative, or neutral to track public perception.\r\nSearch result optimization: Adjusts online content to push down negative results and highlight positive information.\r\nReview management: Helps clients gather and respond to reviews, improving credibility and online ratings.\r\nReal-time monitoring: Sends alerts when new mentions appear, allowing quick action on potential issues.\r\nCrisis response protocols: Provides steps to address urgent reputation problems effectively.\r\nContent creation and distribution: Produces positive content and shares it across relevant platforms to improve image.\r\nSocial media management: Monitors and manages social media activity to maintain a consistent, positive presence.\r\nCompetitor analysis: Compares client performance to competitors to identify opportunities and weaknesses.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.reputationrhino.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Likely in a major US city (e.g., New York)\r\nFounded: Estimated mid-2000s to early 2010s\r\nPricing: Basic packages around $1,000–$2,000/month; full services $5,000–$10,000+/month\r\nBest Use Case: Businesses or professionals needing ongoing reputation management or preparing for public visibility', '<p>Reputation Rhino&rsquo;s main strength is its use of AI to track and respond to online mentions in real time, giving clients quick insights into their digital image. A limitation is that their services can be expensive for smaller businesses or individuals, which may limit accessibility for those with limited budgets.</p>', 7, 5),
(61, 'Go Fish Digital', 'tools/go-fish-digital.jpg', '<p>Go Fish Digital is a reputation management firm that helps organizations manage how they appear online. Its work focuses on search results, online mentions, and digital content that can affect public perception. The company applies structured analysis and search engine practices to address negative or misleading information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The firm is known for combining reputation management with technical SEO. Instead of relying only on publishing new content, it also improves how websites and pages are indexed and ranked. This approach is used by companies that need long-term control over complex and competitive search results.</p>', 'Service', 'AI-based sentiment monitoring – Tracks brand mentions across websites, news, reviews, and social platforms to identify positive, neutral, or negative trends.\r\nSearch-focused content development – Creates written content designed to rank in search engines and reduce the visibility of unwanted results.\r\nTechnical SEO improvements – Fixes site structure, indexing, and crawl issues so owned content performs better in search results.\r\nReview management support – Helps monitor and respond to reviews on major platforms to reduce reputational risk.\r\nEarly risk detection – Uses data patterns to spot emerging reputation issues before they become widespread.\r\nCrisis response execution – Deploys content and technical actions quickly when negative coverage or events occur.\r\nCustom reporting dashboards – Provides clear views of brand sentiment, rankings, and performance metrics.\r\nDigital PR and link building – Strengthens authority signals to improve trust and search visibility.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://gofishdigital.com/\r\nHeadquarters: United States\r\nFounded: Mid-2010s (estimated)\r\nPricing: Custom retainers, typically starting around $5,000 per month\r\nBest suited for: Medium to large organizations with complex reputation challenges', '<p>Go Fish Digital&rsquo;s main strength is its strong technical SEO foundation, which helps improve long-term search visibility rather than relying only on content volume. A clear limitation is cost, as its services and technical depth may be difficult for smaller businesses with limited budgets to justify.</p>', 7, 6),
(62, 'Reputation Resolutions', 'tools/reputation-resolutions.jpg', '<p>Reputation Resolutions is a company that helps businesses and individuals manage how they appear online. It focuses on tracking online mentions, understanding public sentiment, and addressing content that may harm a person&rsquo;s or brand&rsquo;s reputation. The company combines technical search optimization with reputation-focused strategies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The firm works on both short-term issues and long-term visibility. Instead of only reacting to negative content, it aims to improve how positive and accurate information appears in search results. This approach is intended to help clients maintain better control over how they are represented online over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>', 'Service', 'AI-based online monitoring – Uses automated systems to scan websites, review platforms, social media, and forums for brand or name mentions.\r\nNegative content suppression and removal – Identifies harmful or outdated content and works to reduce its visibility or request removal where possible.\r\nSearch-focused content creation – Publishes relevant articles and pages to help positive information rank higher in search results.\r\nSentiment analysis with NLP – Analyzes text to determine whether mentions are positive, neutral, or negative, helping prioritize responses.\r\nCrisis response support – Provides structured actions for handling sudden spikes in negative attention or public issues.\r\nCustomized reputation plans – Adjusts strategies based on industry, audience, and specific reputation risks.\r\nReputation reports and analytics – Delivers regular updates showing trends, risks, and progress over time.\r\nSEO for positive visibility – Applies search optimization methods to improve how favorable content appears online.\r\nReview management support – Helps track, respond to, and encourage customer reviews on key platforms.\r\nCompetitor reputation review – Examines how competitors are perceived online to identify positioning gaps.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.reputationresolutions.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly confirmed; likely based in a major U.S. city\r\nFounded: Estimated between 2010 and 2015\r\nPricing model: Monthly subscription, typically tier-based\r\nEstimated cost range: Approximately $500 to $5,000+ per month\r\nBest suited for: Businesses, executives, professionals, and service-based industries', '<p>One clear strength of Reputation Resolutions is its structured approach that combines monitoring, analysis, and search visibility work in one service. A possible limitation is cost, which may be difficult for smaller organizations to sustain. Results also depend on platform rules, meaning some issues may take longer to improve.</p>', 7, 7),
(63, 'Reputation', 'tools/reputation.jpg', '<p>Reputation.com is a software platform used by large organizations to track and manage how their brands appear online. It collects data from reviews, social media, and other public sources, then organizes that information so companies can see how customers talk about them across many digital channels.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is built for businesses with many locations or departments. It uses automated analysis to sort feedback, identify patterns, and support responses at scale. By combining monitoring, reporting, and listing control in one system, it helps organizations manage their online presence in a structured way.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Review monitoring and sentiment analysis – Collects reviews from many websites and analyzes the language to show whether feedback is positive, neutral, or negative.\r\nBusiness listings management – Updates business details once and distributes accurate information across online directories.\r\nCompetitive benchmarking – Compares reputation scores and review trends with selected competitors.\r\nCustomer surveys and feedback tools – Lets businesses collect direct feedback through structured surveys.\r\nSocial media monitoring and management – Tracks brand mentions and allows responses from a central dashboard.\r\nAnalytics and reporting dashboard – Displays trends, performance metrics, and changes over time in customizable reports.\r\nReview response and generation tools – Helps teams reply to reviews and request new reviews from customers.\r\nLocal SEO tools – Improves visibility in local search results by keeping location data consistent.\r\nCrisis response features – Flags sudden increases in negative feedback so teams can react quickly.\r\nEmployee advocacy tools – Allows employees to share approved company messages through their networks.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.reputation.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Redwood City, California\r\nFounded: 2006\r\nPricing: Custom enterprise pricing\r\nTypical cost level: Several thousand dollars per month\r\nBest suited for: Large, multi-location organizations', '<p>Reputation.com&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to bring large volumes of feedback and data into one organized system for enterprise use. A clear limitation is its cost and complexity, which can make it impractical for smaller businesses without dedicated staff to manage the platform.</p>', 7, 8),
(64, 'Birdeye', 'tools/birdeye.jpg', '<p>Birdeye is a reputation management platform that helps businesses track and manage customer feedback from many online sources. It brings reviews, messages, and social interactions into one system so teams can see what customers are saying and respond in a timely way.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is mainly used by businesses with more than one location that need consistent information and feedback handling across the web. By using data analysis and automation, Birdeye helps organizations understand customer sentiment and keep their online presence accurate and up to date.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Sentiment analysis: Uses AI to review customer comments and identify whether feedback is positive, negative, or neutral.\r\nAutomated review requests: Sends review requests to customers after interactions to help collect more genuine feedback.\r\nReal-time review alerts: Notifies businesses as soon as a new review is posted so they can respond quickly.\r\nBusiness listing management: Keeps business details consistent across directories and search platforms.\r\nCustomer surveys: Collects direct feedback and highlights common issues or trends over time.\r\nSocial media management: Allows businesses to monitor and reply to social messages from one place.\r\nCompetitive benchmarking: Compares performance metrics with similar businesses in the same industry.\r\nLocal SEO tools: Helps improve local search visibility by supporting accurate listings and regular reviews.\r\nReporting dashboard: Shows key metrics in one view to support tracking and decision-making.\r\nCRM integrations: Connects with existing business systems to keep customer data aligned.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.birdeye.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Palo Alto, California\r\nFounded: 2012\r\nPricing: Starts at around $200 per month; custom enterprise plans available\r\nBest use case: Multi-location and enterprise businesses', '<p>Birdeye&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to manage reviews, listings, and feedback from many sources in one dashboard, which is useful for larger organizations. A clear limitation is that the platform can feel complex and costly for very small businesses that only need basic review monitoring.</p>', 7, 9),
(65, 'Podium', 'tools/podium.jpg', '<p>Podium is a software platform that helps businesses collect and manage online reviews while handling customer messages in one place. It focuses on making communication faster and more organized, especially for businesses that rely on local customers and frequent interactions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform brings together reviews, messages, and customer actions from different channels into a single system. By automating review requests and analyzing feedback, Podium helps businesses track customer opinions, respond more quickly, and maintain accurate business information across major online platforms.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Review Request Automation: Sends review requests by text or email after customer interactions, helping businesses collect feedback without manual follow-up.\r\nReview Management Dashboard: Shows reviews from multiple platforms in one place, making it easier to read, respond, and monitor trends.\r\nCentralized Messaging Inbox: Combines messages from Google, Facebook, web chat, and SMS so teams can reply without switching tools.\r\nAI-Based Sentiment Analysis: Analyzes review language to highlight positive and negative patterns, helping businesses spot issues early.\r\nTwo-Way Text Messaging: Allows businesses to communicate with customers by text, which many customers prefer over calls or emails.\r\nPayments Through Messaging: Enables businesses to send payment requests by text, reducing delays and simplifying the payment process.\r\nAppointment and Task Coordination: Supports scheduling and internal notes to help teams manage customer follow-ups more efficiently.\r\nReporting and Analytics: Provides reports on review volume, response time, and ratings to track reputation changes over time.\r\nLocal SEO Support: Uses fresh reviews and consistent business data to support better visibility in local search results.\r\nTeam Access Controls: Offers role-based permissions so staff members only see and manage what they need.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.podium.com/\r\nCompany Name: Podium\r\nHeadquarters: Lehi, Utah, United States\r\nFounded: 2014\r\nPricing Model: Monthly subscription\r\nStarting Price: Around $289 per month\r\nEnterprise Plans: Custom pricing available\r\nPrimary Customers: Local and multi-location businesses\r\nCommon Industries: Automotive, healthcare, home services', '<p>Podium&rsquo;s main strength is how it brings reviews, messages, and customer actions into one system, which can save time for busy teams. A clear limitation is its price, which may be difficult for smaller businesses to justify if they do not receive a high volume of customer interactions.</p>', 7, 10),
(66, 'ReviewTrackers', 'tools/reviewtrackers.jpg', '<p>ReviewTrackers is a software platform that helps businesses keep track of customer reviews from many websites in one place. It allows teams to read, analyze, and respond to feedback without visiting each review site separately, which helps save time and reduce missed customer comments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform collects review data and uses automated analysis to show patterns in customer opinions. By organizing feedback and response activity, ReviewTrackers supports businesses that want to understand customer experience, maintain consistent responses, and manage their online presence across multiple locations.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Multi-Site Review Monitoring: Collects reviews from over 100 websites so businesses can see all feedback in one dashboard.\r\nSentiment Analysis: Uses language analysis to group reviews as positive, neutral, or negative, helping teams understand overall customer mood.\r\nReal-Time Review Alerts: Sends notifications when new reviews appear, allowing faster responses to customer feedback.\r\nAnalytics and Reporting: Shows trends, ratings, and changes over time through reports that support performance tracking.\r\nCompetitive Comparison Tools: Compares review volume and ratings with competitors to provide market context.\r\nReview Collection Tools: Helps businesses request feedback from customers to increase the number of reviews.\r\nTeam Collaboration Tools: Assigns reviews to team members and allows internal notes to coordinate responses.\r\nSoftware Integrations: Connects with CRM and support systems to align reviews with customer records.\r\nLocal Search Support: Uses review data to support better visibility in local search results.\r\nMobile Application: Allows users to monitor and reply to reviews while away from their desks.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.reviewtrackers.com/\r\nCompany Name: ReviewTrackers\r\nHeadquarters: Chicago, Illinois, United States\r\nFounded: 2012\r\nPricing Model: Subscription-based\r\nStarting Price: Around $99 per month\r\nEnterprise Pricing: Available by request\r\nPrimary Users: Businesses with multiple locations\r\nCommon Industries: Healthcare, hospitality, professional services', '<p>ReviewTrackers&rsquo; main strength is its ability to gather reviews from many platforms into one clear dashboard, which helps teams stay organized. A limitation is that smaller businesses may find the cost and number of features more than they need, especially if they manage only one location or receive few reviews.</p>', 7, 11),
(67, 'Yext', 'tools/yext.jpg', '<p>Yext is a digital platform that helps businesses manage their public information and online reputation from one place. It focuses on keeping business details correct and consistent across search engines, maps, apps, and other online services where customers look for information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform also helps companies track and respond to customer reviews and questions. By combining data management with review analysis, Yext supports businesses that need reliable control over how their brand appears across many online channels.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Knowledge Management: Stores and updates business details like name, address, hours, and services so the same information appears everywhere online.\r\nReview Monitoring: Collects customer reviews from multiple websites in one dashboard to save time and avoid missed feedback.\r\nReview Generation: Helps businesses request reviews from customers to increase recent and relevant feedback.\r\nAnalytics and Reporting: Shows data on listing accuracy, review trends, and search visibility to support better decisions.\r\nAI-Based Sentiment Analysis: Analyzes review text to identify common topics and overall customer sentiment.\r\nPublisher Network Integration: Sends updates directly to search engines, maps, apps, and voice assistants through direct connections.\r\nListing Management: Finds incorrect or outdated listings online and replaces them with accurate information.\r\nQ&A Management: Allows businesses to answer customer questions on platforms like Google using official responses.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.yext.com/\r\nHeadquarters: New York, NY, USA\r\nFounded: 2006\r\nPricing Model: Custom pricing based on business size and usage\r\nStarting Price: Around $499 per month for basic plans\r\nTarget Users: Multi-location businesses, franchises, and large organizations', '<p>Yext&rsquo;s main strength is its wide network of connected platforms, which makes updating business information fast and consistent. A key limitation is the cost, which may be too high for small or single-location businesses, especially when additional SEO tools are still needed for stronger search performance.</p>', 7, 12),
(68, 'BrandYourself', 'tools/brandyourself.jpg', '<p>BrandYourself is an online reputation management platform designed for individuals and small organizations who want to manage how they appear in search results. It focuses on helping users understand what information about them is visible online and how that information may affect personal or professional opportunities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform provides guided tools that simplify reputation management tasks such as monitoring search results, improving profiles, and protecting personal data. Instead of requiring advanced technical knowledge, BrandYourself breaks these processes into clear steps that users can follow on their own.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Search result monitoring – Tracks how a name or brand appears on major search engines and alerts users when changes occur.\r\nReputation improvement plans – Provides step-by-step guidance to improve search visibility and address weak areas.\r\nProfile optimization tools – Helps users update social media and personal profiles so they rank better in search results.\r\nReal-time alerts – Notifies users when new mentions or content related to their name appear online.\r\nPrivacy protection – Assists in removing or limiting access to personal data on data broker websites.\r\nCompetitor comparison – Shows how a user’s online presence compares to others in the same field.\r\nSocial media integration – Connects social accounts to manage visibility and consistency from one place.\r\nAnalytics dashboard – Displays reputation scores and progress over time using simple metrics.\r\nContent suggestions – Recommends types of positive content that can help improve search results.\r\nProfessional profile support – Focuses on improving profiles commonly reviewed by employers or clients.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.brandyourself.com/\r\nCompany type: Online reputation management platform\r\nHeadquarters: United States\r\nFounded: Around 2010\r\nPricing model: Free basic access with paid monthly plans\r\nTarget users: Individuals, professionals, job seekers, and small businesses', '<p>BrandYourself&rsquo;s main strength is its clear, guided approach that allows non-technical users to manage their online presence independently. A limitation is that it relies heavily on user involvement, which may not be suitable for complex reputation issues that require extensive content removal or professional public relations support.</p>', 7, 13),
(69, 'WebiMax', 'tools/webimax.jpg', '<p>WebiMax is a digital marketing agency that focuses on online reputation management for businesses and individuals. Its services are designed to help clients understand how they appear online and take steps to improve or protect that image across search engines, review sites, and other public platforms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company uses a mix of search optimization, content creation, and review management to address reputation issues. Rather than working on reputation alone, WebiMax connects these efforts with broader digital marketing activities to support long-term visibility and consistency online.</p>', 'Service', 'Online reputation monitoring\r\nTracks mentions of a business or person across search engines, review platforms, and social media to identify potential reputation risks early.\r\nContent creation and promotion\r\nDevelops positive and accurate content and helps it reach wider audiences to balance or outweigh negative information.\r\nSearch engine optimization (SEO)\r\nUses SEO methods to help positive pages rank higher in search results, reducing the visibility of unfavorable content.\r\nReview management and generation\r\nHelps businesses collect, manage, and respond to customer reviews to improve overall feedback quality and credibility.\r\nNegative content suppression\r\nApplies technical and content-based strategies to push harmful or outdated content lower in search results.\r\nCrisis response support\r\nProvides structured actions for handling sudden reputation issues, such as negative press or viral complaints.\r\nReporting and analytics dashboards\r\nOffers tools that show reputation trends, visibility changes, and progress over time in one place.\r\nIntegration with digital marketing services\r\nAligns reputation work with advertising, SEO, and branding efforts for consistent online messaging.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.webimax.com/\r\nCompany type: Digital marketing and reputation management agency\r\nHeadquarters: Not specified\r\nYear founded: Not specified\r\nPricing model: Custom pricing based on project scope\r\nTarget users: Businesses and professionals with active online profiles', '<p>WebiMax&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to combine reputation management with SEO and content strategies, which supports steady, long-term improvement. A limitation is the lack of public pricing details, which may make it harder for smaller clients to assess affordability before making contact.</p>', 7, 14),
(70, 'Procore', 'tools/procore.jpg', '<p>Procore is a cloud-based software platform built for managing construction projects. It brings project information, people, and processes into one online system so teams can work from the same data. The software is designed to support planning, execution, and tracking throughout a construction project&rsquo;s life cycle.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is mainly used by construction professionals who need structured control over documents, schedules, and costs. By centralizing project data, Procore helps reduce confusion caused by emails, spreadsheets, and disconnected tools. It supports coordination between office staff and field teams working on active job sites.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Centralized document management – Stores all drawings, files, and revisions in one place so teams always access the latest version.\r\nProject scheduling tools – Uses timelines and milestones to track progress and identify delays early.\r\nBudget and cost tracking – Monitors expenses in real time to help control spending and compare planned versus actual costs.\r\nQuality and safety management – Records inspections and safety checks to support compliance and reduce risk.\r\nRFI and submittal management – Organizes questions, approvals, and responses to avoid miscommunication.\r\nChange order management – Tracks scope and cost changes so financial impacts are clearly documented.\r\nBIM integration – Connects 3D models with project data for better coordination and issue detection.\r\nDaily logs – Captures site activities, labor, and weather to maintain accurate project records.\r\nMobile access – Allows field teams to view and update information directly from the job site.\r\nReporting and dashboards – Summarizes project data to support monitoring and decision-making.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.procore.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Carpinteria, California, United States\r\nFounded: 2002\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based\r\nTarget users: Medium to large construction companies', '<p>Procore&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to keep project information organized and accessible across teams and locations. This helps reduce errors caused by outdated or missing data. One limitation is its complexity, as new users may need time and training to use the system effectively, especially smaller teams with simpler projects.</p>', 8, 1),
(71, 'Buildertrend', 'tools/buildertrend.jpg', '<p>Buildertrend is a software tool that helps manage construction projects from start to finish. It brings together scheduling, budgeting, communication, and documentation in one place, allowing teams, clients, and subcontractors to access project information easily. The platform aims to reduce delays and mistakes that can happen when using separate systems.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The software also offers mobile access and real-time updates so on-site workers and project managers can see current progress. It supports financial management, change orders, and photo or video documentation, helping teams track project details accurately and communicate effectively with clients and contractors.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Project lifecycle management: Tracks projects from initial bid to completion, helping teams stay organized.\r\nDocument storage with version control: Keeps all files in one place and ensures older versions are preserved.\r\nReal-time scheduling: Updates timelines automatically when changes occur, preventing conflicts.\r\nFinancial management: Manages budgets, invoices, and payments to track project costs.\r\nClient portal: Allows homeowners to view project progress and communicate securely with the team.\r\nChange order system: Manages approvals for changes in scope or design to avoid misunderstandings.\r\nPhoto and video documentation: Stores time-stamped images and videos for progress tracking.\r\nMobile access: Lets on-site workers check schedules, documents, and updates from any device.\r\nDaily logs: Records daily work, issues, and weather conditions to keep a clear project history.\r\nSoftware integrations: Connects with accounting and estimating tools to streamline workflows.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.buildertrend.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Omaha, Nebraska\r\nFounded: 2006\r\nPricing: Subscription-based, varies by company size and features\r\nBest Use Case: Residential and commercial construction, especially for custom home builders and remodelers', '<p>Buildertrend is strong at keeping all project information organized and accessible, making it easier to manage multiple teams and clients. One limitation is that smaller companies might find it complex at first, and the pricing may be high for very small projects. Overall, it is practical for mid-to-large construction businesses.</p>', 8, 2),
(72, 'PlanGrid', 'tools/plangrid.jpg', '<p>PlanGrid is a construction project management software that helps teams manage blueprints, drawings, and documents online instead of on paper. It allows users to access project files from any device, making it easier to share information between office and field teams.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform also helps track changes in drawings, create punch lists, and manage requests for information. Its tools aim to reduce mistakes from outdated documents and improve communication for projects of all sizes, particularly in commercial and industrial construction.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Real-time blueprint and drawing access: Lets users view and update drawings immediately, ensuring everyone works with the latest version.\r\nAutomatic version control: Detects and highlights changes between drawing revisions to prevent errors from outdated plans.\r\nMobile-first design: Field teams can access, mark up, and share documents from smartphones or tablets.\r\nPunch list creation and management: Users can track tasks, assign responsibilities, and add photos for documentation.\r\nRFI and submittal tracking: Automates workflow for requests and submissions, sending alerts and reminders to team members.\r\nDocument management system: Centralized storage with permission controls to organize and secure all project files.\r\nBIM model viewing and integration: Allows viewing of 3D building models and coordination with other design software.\r\nAutomated progress tracking: Compares photos over time and records updates to monitor project status.\r\nReporting and analytics dashboard: Offers visual summaries of project metrics and performance for better decision-making.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.plangrid.com/\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California, USA\r\nFounded: 2011\r\nPricing: Plans start around $39/month per user; advanced or enterprise pricing available\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large construction projects needing document management and field collaboration', '<p>PlanGrid is strong in managing construction documents and helping teams stay updated in real time. Its mobile access and automatic version control reduce mistakes from outdated drawings. A limitation is that its pricing may be too high for smaller projects, and some advanced features require time to learn.</p>', 8, 3),
(73, 'Fieldwire', 'tools/fieldwire.jpg', '<p>Fieldwire is construction project management software that helps teams in the field and office stay connected. It provides a central platform to share blueprints, assign tasks, and manage documents. This helps reduce mistakes and delays by making sure everyone works with the latest information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The software is designed for mobile devices, allowing workers to access project details on-site. It supports features like real-time task tracking, photo documentation, and team messaging, which make project communication and organization easier. Fieldwire is suitable for small to medium-sized construction projects.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Blueprint management: Share, mark up, and update blueprints so the whole team sees the latest version.\r\nTask tracking: Assign tasks, set priorities and due dates, and monitor progress to keep work organized.\r\nPhoto documentation: Take photos on-site with timestamps and location tags, linking them to specific tasks or areas.\r\nDaily logs and reports: Record site conditions, issues, and progress to keep a record of the project.\r\nTeam messaging: Send messages and notifications within the app to keep all team members informed.\r\nOffline access: Work on tasks and documents even without internet, syncing updates later.\r\nSoftware integrations: Connect with other construction tools like BIM or estimating platforms to streamline workflows.\r\nAutomated RFIs and submittals: Manage requests and approvals more efficiently to reduce delays.\r\nCustom forms and templates: Create inspections, checklists, or compliance forms to standardize reporting.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.fieldwire.com/\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2013\r\nPricing: Free basic plan; paid plans $39–$59 per user per month\r\nBest Use Case: General contractors, subcontractors, and project managers in small to medium commercial or residential construction projects', '<p>Fieldwire&rsquo;s main strength is its mobile-first design, which makes it easy for field teams to access and update project information in real time. One limitation is that it may not be ideal for very large construction companies that need advanced cost tracking or highly specialized management features.</p>', 8, 4),
(74, 'CoConstruct', 'tools/coconstruct.jpg', '<p>CoConstruct is a construction project management tool made for custom home builders and remodelers. It helps manage projects from the start, including client selections, to the end when the project is finished. The software connects office staff, field teams, and clients to reduce mistakes and improve workflow.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It also helps track budgets, schedules, and documents in one place. CoConstruct may use AI tools to forecast potential delays or cost issues and organize project information for easier access. The system ensures that important details are visible and can help teams stay on track throughout a project.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Project scheduling: Lets users plan timelines, set milestones, and track progress to keep work on schedule.\r\nBudget and cost tracking: Monitors expenses, updates costs in real-time, and manages change orders to control budgets.\r\nClient communication portal: Provides a platform for clients to receive updates, view photos, and stay informed about project status.\r\nSelection and specification management: Allows tracking of material choices and supplier information to reduce errors in selections.\r\nDocument management: Stores project documents in the cloud, keeps versions organized, and makes files easy to find.\r\nAI-powered insights: Offers predictions about risks or delays to help teams plan ahead and prevent problems.\r\nCustom reporting dashboards: Shows key metrics and project performance in an easy-to-read format.\r\nIntegration with other tools: Connects with accounting software, estimating programs, and other construction apps to reduce duplicate work.\r\nQuality control and punch list management: Tracks tasks and issues on-site to ensure work meets standards.\r\nBidding and proposal management: Helps organize and submit bids and proposals to streamline the sales process.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.coconstruct.com/\r\nHeadquarters: United States\r\nFounded: Likely mid-2000s to early 2010s\r\nPricing: Subscription-based, tiered by company size and project volume\r\nBest Use Case: Suitable for custom home builders, remodeling contractors, and small to medium residential construction companies', '<p>CoConstruct is strong in keeping clients and teams connected, especially during selections and project updates. This helps reduce mistakes and improves workflow. One limitation is that it can be complex for new users, and learning all its features may take time. It works best for residential construction teams that manage both project details and client communication.</p>', 8, 5),
(75, 'eSUB', 'tools/esub.jpg', '<p>eSUB is a construction management software made specifically for commercial subcontractors. It helps trade contractors manage communication and information between the field and the office, making workflows smoother and reducing mistakes. The platform focuses on subcontractor needs rather than general contractor functions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The software allows subcontractors to track documents, manage tasks, and view project information in real time. It also provides financial tracking and reporting tools. While it does not include advanced modeling features, it helps subcontractors stay organized, improve productivity, and manage change orders more effectively.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Fusion platform: Links field teams and office staff to share updates and information instantly.\r\nDocument management: Organizes project documents so subcontractors can access plans, drawings, and reports without confusion.\r\nMobile and web access: Lets users check and update information on phones, tablets, or computers from anywhere.\r\nReal-time project dashboards: Shows the current status of projects, helping teams make informed decisions quickly.\r\nAutomated task creation: Generates tasks automatically based on field input to ensure follow-ups are not missed.\r\nChange order management: Tracks changes to projects and helps subcontractors manage associated costs and revenue.\r\nSystem integrations: Connects with general contractor software to share information between teams.\r\nRFI tracking: Keeps track of Requests for Information to avoid delays caused by missing answers.\r\nDaily reporting: Simplifies logging field activities, work progress, and issues each day.\r\nFinancial tracking and analytics: Monitors costs, labor, and revenues for better project financial management.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.esub.com/\r\nHeadquarters: United States (likely California)\r\nFounded: Early 2010s\r\nPricing: Not publicly listed; demo required\r\nBest Use Case: Commercial subcontractors who need better field-to-office communication', '<p>eSUB is strong in organizing workflows for subcontractors, helping them reduce mistakes and improve productivity. Its main limitation is that it focuses on subcontractors only, so general contractors or owners looking for full project management may find it less suitable. Overall, it efficiently addresses the needs of trade contractors managing multiple projects.</p>', 8, 6),
(76, 'Smartsheet', 'tools/smartsheet.jpg', '<p>Smartsheet is a project management tool that combines a spreadsheet-style interface with tools to plan, track, and manage projects. It is used by construction teams to organize tasks, schedules, and resources in one place, helping teams work together across offices and construction sites.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform also includes features like automated workflows, reporting dashboards, and document management. These tools allow project managers to monitor progress, assign tasks, and make decisions based on up-to-date project information. Smartsheet can handle multiple projects at the same time and is suitable for teams of various sizes.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Gantt charts and timelines: Show project schedules and task dependencies visually to keep work organized.\r\nReal-time dashboards: Track progress, budget, and resource use across projects.\r\nAutomated workflows: Streamline approvals, updates, and repetitive processes to save time.\r\nDocument management: Store and share files like blueprints and permits, with version control to avoid confusion.\r\nResource management: Monitor labor, equipment, and materials across multiple sites.\r\nIntegration with BIM and other tools: Connect with construction software for design and planning coordination.\r\nAI risk assessment: Identify possible delays or budget problems before they happen.\r\nMobile access: Update and view project information from job sites.\r\nCustom templates: Use prebuilt templates for bids, change orders, and punch lists to save setup time.\r\nPermission controls: Securely manage who can access project data and documents.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.smartsheet.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Bellevue, Washington, United States\r\nFounded: 2005\r\nPricing: Team plan starts around $25/user/month; higher plans offer more features\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large construction companies managing multiple projects and stakeholders', '<p>Smartsheet is strong in collaboration and project tracking, making it easy for teams to share updates and manage tasks in one place. A limitation is that it lacks some construction-specific tools, like detailed equipment tracking or full BIM features, which may require additional software for larger or highly technical projects.</p>', 8, 7),
(77, 'Viewpoint', 'tools/viewpoint.jpg', '<p>Viewpoint, part of Trimble Construction One, is a construction management software designed to connect office and field teams. It helps construction companies track projects, manage finances, and organize resources in one system. The platform provides tools to monitor performance, control budgets, and maintain communication between on-site workers and office staff.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Viewpoint is mainly used by mid-sized to large construction companies with multiple projects. Its strength is combining financial management with project tracking, giving managers a clear overview of operations. The software also includes reporting, analytics, and mobile tools to support teams and improve efficiency across different project sites.</p>', 'Key Features', 'ERP and Financial Management: Handles accounting, payroll, and project budgets in one system to reduce errors and simplify financial control.\r\nProject Tracking Dashboard: Shows real-time updates on costs, schedules, and progress, helping managers stay informed and make decisions quickly.\r\nHR Management Tools: Supports hiring, onboarding, and workforce management to streamline employee administration.\r\nMobile Field Tools: Lets field teams report updates, collect data, and communicate with the office from anywhere.\r\nDocument Management: Organizes files and drawings with searchable indexing to make information easy to find.\r\nSpectra Analytics: Provides detailed project insights and visual reports to understand trends and identify potential problems.\r\nIntegration Capabilities: Connects with other Trimble tools and third-party software for smoother workflow across systems.\r\nAI Predictive Analytics: Uses data to forecast risks, detect issues early, and plan resources effectively.\r\nCustom Reporting Tools: Generates tailored reports for different stakeholders, showing the information they need.\r\nBid Management and Estimating: Helps create cost estimates and manage bids for new projects.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://viewpoint.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Sunnyvale, California, USA\r\nFounded: As part of Trimble, which started in 1978\r\nPricing: Enterprise-level, typically $50,000–$200,000+ per year\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-sized to large construction companies needing connected project management, finances, and field-to-office communication', '<p>Viewpoint&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to combine project tracking with financial management, giving managers a clear overview of operations. One limitation is that it can be complex to implement, requiring significant time and resources, which may make it challenging for smaller companies or those with limited IT support.</p>', 8, 8),
(78, 'RedTeam', 'tools/redteam.jpg', '<p>RedTeam is a construction management software made mainly for general contractors. It helps manage projects from the planning stage through completion, combining financial management with daily project operations. The software provides a central place for project information, reducing errors and making it easier for office and field teams to stay connected.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform includes tools for estimating, scheduling, and handling subcontractors. It also gives real-time updates on project costs and progress. By keeping all project data in one system, RedTeam aims to simplify communication and decision-making for contractors handling multiple projects at the same time.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Project lifecycle management: Handles every stage of a construction project, from planning to closeout, keeping all data in one system.\r\nReal-time financial visibility: Shows current project costs and budgets to help managers make informed decisions.\r\nBid management and estimating: Helps prepare accurate project proposals and manage bids from potential clients.\r\nField management: Allows on-site teams to report daily progress and access project details through mobile devices.\r\nDocument management: Stores and tracks important files, submittals, and change orders to keep projects organized.\r\nScheduling and task management: Visualizes timelines and assigns tasks to resources to improve project planning.\r\nSubcontractor portal: Lets subcontractors view assignments, submit documents, and communicate easily.\r\nAccounting integrations: Connects with systems like Sage 100 Contractor to streamline financial workflows.\r\nFinancial reporting and analytics: Provides reports and data analysis to support better project decisions.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.redteam.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not specified\r\nFounded: Not specified\r\nPricing: Not specified, likely subscription-based\r\nBest Use Case: General contractors needing integrated project and financial management', '<p>RedTeam&rsquo;s main strength is combining project management with real-time financial tracking, which helps contractors make decisions quickly. A potential limitation is that it may be complex for smaller teams or businesses with simpler needs. Overall, it works best for companies that handle multiple projects and need a single system to manage both operations and finances efficiently.</p>', 8, 9);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(79, 'Contractor Foreman', 'tools/contractor-foreman.jpg', '<p>Contractor Foreman is a construction management software designed for contractors working on residential, commercial, and public projects. It provides a single platform to handle scheduling, budgeting, documentation, and team communication. The software is cloud-based, allowing teams to access project information from anywhere, including on-site locations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is priced affordably, starting at $49 per month for the whole company. It offers tools to track project costs, manage labor and subcontractors, and keep project documents organized. While it includes basic predictive and resource management features, some advanced automation options may be limited compared to higher-end software.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Project scheduling with Gantt charts: Visualize tasks over time to keep projects on track.\r\nBudget tracking and cost management: Monitor expenses and compare them to planned budgets.\r\nDocument control with versioning: Store project files securely and track changes or approvals.\r\nMobile access: Update tasks, reports, and schedules directly from the field.\r\nResource allocation and labor management: Assign workers and equipment efficiently.\r\nBid management and estimating tools: Create and manage project bids and cost estimates.\r\nDaily logs and field reporting: Record daily progress, issues, and site updates.\r\nTeam communication tools: Send messages and share updates within the platform.\r\nCustomizable reports and dashboards: Generate summaries of project performance and metrics.\r\nSubcontractor management: Track subcontractor performance and assignments.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.contractorforeman.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly disclosed\r\nFounded: Not publicly disclosed\r\nPricing: Starting at $49/month for the entire company\r\nBest Use Case: Small to medium construction companies managing multiple projects', '<p>Contractor Foreman is strong in providing a wide range of construction management tools at a low cost, making it suitable for small and medium companies. A limitation is that it may lack some advanced automation and predictive analytics found in higher-end platforms. Overall, it helps manage projects, documents, and team communication efficiently.</p>', 8, 10),
(80, 'Buildxact', 'tools/buildxact.jpg', '<p>Buildxact is construction management software that helps plan and manage building projects from start to finish. It is designed to make project scheduling, budgeting, and team communication easier for construction companies. The platform organizes project data so managers can track progress, costs, and resources in one place.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The software uses AI tools to predict possible delays and budget issues before they happen. It also makes documents and project information easy to search and retrieve. Buildxact works on desktop and mobile devices, so teams on-site can access updates in real time and keep projects on track.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Project planning and scheduling: Use Gantt charts and timelines to organize tasks and see how delays affect the project.\r\nBudget tracking and cost estimation: Track spending and forecast costs to avoid going over budget.\r\nDocument management: Store and organize files with version control and easy search.\r\nTeam collaboration: Share updates and communicate with team members and stakeholders in one workspace.\r\nMobile access: Update and check project details on-site using smartphones or tablets.\r\nBIM integration: View 3D models of projects to understand design and construction progress.\r\nAutomated reporting: Generate performance and progress reports with customizable dashboards.\r\nResource allocation: Plan labor and equipment use to avoid shortages or idle time.\r\nRisk assessment: Identify potential delays or problems before they happen.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.buildxact.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Likely in San Francisco, Austin, or Sydney\r\nFounded: Around 2010–2015\r\nPricing: Subscription model, varies by company size and project volume\r\nBest Use Case: Small to medium construction companies, residential builders, and commercial contractors', '<p>Buildxact is strong in keeping project information organized and accessible, which helps teams stay on schedule and budget. A limitation is that some features may be complicated for users who are not familiar with construction software. Overall, it works best for companies managing multiple projects that need clear planning and cost tracking.</p>', 8, 11),
(81, 'Superside', 'tools/superside_PRxsIze.jpg', '<p>Superside provides AI consulting services to help businesses use artificial intelligence in practical ways. They work on turning complex AI technologies into tools that can improve business operations, decision-making, and digital presence. Their services include both planning and technical support to implement AI solutions in companies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company focuses on helping businesses integrate AI with their existing systems. They work on areas like machine learning, natural language processing, and data analysis. Superside also advises on ethical AI use and performance monitoring, aiming to ensure that AI solutions are effective and aligned with business goals.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI Strategy Development: Creates a plan for using AI in a business to meet specific goals.\r\nMachine Learning Implementation: Builds and deploys custom ML models to automate or improve processes.\r\nNatural Language Processing Solutions: Analyzes text and language data to understand content, sentiment, or generate automated text.\r\nAI-Powered SEO Optimization: Uses AI tools to improve website visibility and search engine ranking.\r\nData Analytics and Business Intelligence: Processes large datasets to provide insights for better decision-making.\r\nAI Integration Services: Connects AI tools with existing software and workflows in the organization.\r\nAI Governance and Ethics: Advises on responsible and compliant use of AI technologies.\r\nPerformance Monitoring and Optimization: Checks AI systems regularly to ensure they work efficiently and improve over time.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://superside.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Likely in a major tech hub, such as San Francisco or New York\r\nFounded: Around 2016–2018\r\nPricing: Enterprise-level, likely $15,000–$100,000+ depending on the project\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-to-large businesses wanting to adopt AI for analytics, automation, and process improvement', '<p>Superside is strong at helping businesses plan and apply AI in practical ways, especially for analytics and automation. A limitation is that their services may be expensive and mostly suited for larger organizations, which could make them less accessible for smaller companies looking for AI support.</p>', 9, 1),
(82, 'Accenture', 'tools/accenture.jpg', '<p>Accenture is a global consulting company that helps large organizations use artificial intelligence in practical ways. It works with enterprises across many countries and industries, supporting them in planning, building, and running AI systems that fit existing business operations and regulatory environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company focuses on applying AI together with cloud platforms, data systems, and business process changes. Its work often involves long-term transformation projects rather than small tools, helping established organizations modernize legacy systems and use AI to improve efficiency, decision-making, and service delivery.</p>', 'Service', 'Sovereign AI frameworks – Helps organizations design AI systems that meet local data, security, and regulatory requirements while still scaling across regions.\r\nIndustry-specific AI solutions – Adapts AI tools to the needs of sectors like healthcare, finance, retail, and government, reducing the need for generic or unsuitable models.\r\nAI research and insights – Produces research reports that help companies understand current AI capabilities, risks, and adoption trends.\r\nHuman–AI collaboration methods – Designs workflows where employees and AI systems work together, improving productivity without fully replacing human roles.\r\nCloud-based AI deployment – Uses cloud infrastructure to make AI systems easier to scale, update, and manage securely.\r\nData analytics and machine learning services – Converts large volumes of data into forecasts, patterns, and insights that support business decisions.\r\nIntelligent automation – Automates repetitive tasks in operations and customer service to reduce manual effort and errors.\r\nAI ethics and governance – Sets rules and controls to ensure AI systems are used responsibly and comply with laws and internal policies.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.accenture.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Dublin, Ireland\r\nFounded: 1989\r\nOrigin: Formed from the consulting arm of Arthur Andersen\r\nPricing: Custom enterprise contracts, often six-figure to multi-million dollar projects\r\nBest use case: Large organizations planning company-wide AI transformation', '<p>Accenture&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to handle complex, large-scale AI projects across multiple countries and industries. This makes it suitable for enterprises with legacy systems and strict compliance needs. A clear limitation is cost, as its services are usually too expensive and complex for small businesses or early-stage companies.</p>', 9, 1),
(83, 'Deloitte', 'tools/deloitte.jpg', '<p>Deloitte is a large global consulting firm that helps organizations use artificial intelligence in practical ways. Its AI services are designed to support complex businesses and public sector organizations by connecting technology, data, and industry knowledge to improve how operations and decisions are managed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The firm delivers AI work through a structured approach that combines strategy, implementation, and ongoing support. Deloitte works across many industries and regions, offering consistent methods while adapting solutions to local needs. Its focus is on applying AI to real business processes rather than experimental use.</p>', 'Service', 'Deloitte AI Institute™ – Provides research, insights, and guidance to help organizations understand AI trends and make informed decisions.\r\nGenerative AI services with Oracle – Uses Oracle technologies to help companies automate tasks, analyze data faster, and modernize systems.\r\nAI360 podcast series – Shares short, practical discussions that explain how AI is used in real business situations.\r\nIndustry-specific AI solutions – Tailors AI tools to the needs of sectors such as government, finance, healthcare, and enterprise operations.\r\nMultidisciplinary consulting model – Combines AI with audit, risk, tax, and advisory services to support end-to-end transformation.\r\nAI-enabled shared services consulting – Applies AI to back-office functions to reduce manual work and improve efficiency.\r\nROI-focused AI implementation – Designs AI projects around measurable results such as cost reduction or productivity gains.\r\nGlobal delivery network – Uses local teams in different countries while maintaining consistent standards and methods.\r\nEnd-to-end digital transformation – Supports organizations from AI strategy and planning through deployment and long-term use.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www2.deloitte.com/\r\nHeadquarters: New York, USA\r\nFounded: 1845\r\nPricing: Custom pricing based on project scope\r\nBest for: Large enterprises and government organizations', '<p>Deloitte&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to deliver AI solutions at scale using structured methods and deep industry knowledge. A clear limitation is that its services are generally suited to large organizations, which may make them less accessible to smaller companies with limited budgets or simpler needs.</p>', 9, 3),
(84, 'IBM – AI Services and IT Consulting', 'tools/ibm-ai-services-and-it-consulting.jpg', '<p>IBM is a global technology and consulting company with a long history of working with large organizations. It provides AI services that focus on improving how businesses operate, manage data, and run IT systems. Its work is mainly centered on enterprise-scale problems rather than small projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company develops and delivers AI through its watsonx platform, which combines tools for building, managing, and governing AI systems. IBM also applies these tools internally, using its own experience to guide clients that want to adopt AI across complex and regulated environments.</p>', 'Services', 'watsonx Orchestrate™ – Automates everyday business tasks by connecting systems and creating AI assistants that follow defined workflows.\r\nwatsonx Governance – Helps organizations control AI use by tracking models, data sources, and compliance requirements.\r\nwatsonx Code Assistant™ – Supports developers by suggesting code and reducing time spent on repetitive programming tasks.\r\nAI-driven cloud automation – Optimizes cloud operations by identifying inefficiencies and reducing manual system management.\r\nEnterprise application integration – Connects AI tools with more than 80 existing business applications to avoid system silos.\r\nLarge trained AI workforce – Uses a broad pool of AI-trained staff to support design, deployment, and long-term maintenance.\r\nAI security research – Applies research from data breach studies to improve risk management and security planning.\r\nEnterprise scalability – Designed to handle large data volumes and complex systems across global organizations.\r\nInternal AI deployment experience – Uses results from IBM’s own AI adoption to inform practical implementation guidance.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.ibm.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Armonk, New York, United States\r\nFounded: 1911\r\nCompany name changed to IBM: 1924\r\nPricing model: Custom enterprise pricing\r\nPrimary clients: Large and global enterprises\r\nCore AI platform: watsonx\r\nMain focus: AI, automation, and IT consulting', '<p>IBM&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to deliver AI solutions at large scale with strong governance and security controls. This makes it suitable for complex enterprises. A key limitation is cost and complexity, which may make its services less practical for small or mid-sized organizations with limited budgets.</p>', 9, 4),
(85, 'Boston Consulting Group (BCG)', 'tools/boston-consulting-group-bcg.jpg', '<p>Boston Consulting Group (BCG) is a global management consulting firm that advises large organizations on strategy, operations, and technology. In recent years, it has expanded its work in artificial intelligence, helping companies use data and AI tools to improve decision-making, efficiency, and long-term planning across different industries.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>BCG focuses on connecting AI technology with real business needs rather than treating AI as a standalone tool. Its teams combine business consultants, data scientists, and engineers to design AI systems that support areas such as customer service, operations, and digital strategy, mainly for large and complex organizations.</p>', 'Services', 'BCG GAMMA: Works on advanced analytics and machine learning to help companies use data for better forecasting and decisions.\r\nDigital BCG: Helps organizations modernize systems and processes by integrating AI into digital transformation programs.\r\nBCG Platinion: Supports the technical side of AI projects, including system architecture, software implementation, and scaling solutions.\r\nBCG X: Develops and tests new AI products and solutions, often combining design, engineering, and data science.\r\nIndustry-specific AI solutions: Adapts AI models to sector needs such as healthcare, finance, retail, and manufacturing.\r\nAI-driven strategy frameworks: Uses data and AI insights to support long-term business and competitive planning.\r\nMachine learning model development: Builds and deploys models to improve efficiency in areas like supply chains and operations.\r\nNatural language processing solutions: Uses text and language analysis to improve customer support and feedback analysis.\r\nData governance and ethical AI: Helps organizations manage data quality, risk, and responsible AI use.\r\nAI talent and organizational programs: Trains teams and adjusts workflows so AI tools can be used effectively.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.bcg.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA\r\nFounded: 1963\r\nPricing: Premium enterprise projects, often ranging from $500K to $5M or more\r\nBest use case: Large enterprises seeking full AI strategy and transformation support', '<p>BCG&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to link AI initiatives with clear business goals, supported by strong industry knowledge. A key limitation is cost, as its services are generally not suitable for small or mid-sized companies with limited budgets or narrowly defined AI needs.</p>', 9, 5),
(86, 'PwC', 'tools/pwc.jpg', '<p>PwC is a global professional services firm that provides AI consulting as part of its broader technology and business advisory work. It supports organizations in planning, building, and using AI systems that fit their operations, industry rules, and long-term goals, especially in complex and regulated environments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The firm works with large organizations across many sectors, combining AI tools with process improvement, data management, and workforce planning. PwC focuses on practical use of AI, helping companies handle risks, follow regulations, and integrate new technologies into existing systems without disrupting daily business.</p>', 'Services', 'AI strategy and roadmap development\r\nHelps organizations decide where AI can add value and plan clear steps for implementation.\r\nIndustry-specific AI solutions\r\nDesigns AI tools tailored to sectors like finance, healthcare, and hospitality to solve real operational problems.\r\nAI-driven digital transformation\r\nUses AI to improve business processes while keeping human oversight and decision-making in place.\r\nRegulatory and compliance support\r\nAssists organizations in meeting legal and regulatory requirements when using AI systems.\r\nEmployee experience tools\r\nApplies AI to improve internal systems, such as HR platforms and digital workplaces.\r\nData analytics and insights\r\nUses AI models to analyze large data sets and support better business decisions.\r\nAI risk assessment and governance\r\nIdentifies potential risks and sets controls to manage ethical, legal, and operational concerns.\r\nEnterprise system integration\r\nConnects AI tools with existing IT systems to avoid major system replacements.\r\nChange management for AI adoption\r\nSupports teams in adapting to new AI tools through planning and training.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.pwc.com/\r\nHeadquarters: London, United Kingdom\r\nFounded: 1998 (merger of Price Waterhouse and Coopers & Lybrand)\r\nGlobal presence: Operations in over 150 countries\r\nPricing: Custom, project-based enterprise pricing\r\nBest suited for: Large organizations needing full AI planning and implementation support', '<p>PwC&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to handle AI projects that involve strict regulations and complex organizations. This makes it reliable for large enterprises. A clear limitation is cost, as its services are designed for large budgets, which may not be practical for smaller companies or startups.</p>', 9, 6),
(87, 'EY (Ernst & Young)', 'tools/ey-ernst-young.jpg', '<p>EY (Ernst &amp; Young) is a global professional services firm that helps organizations use artificial intelligence as part of broader business change. Its AI consulting work focuses on applying technology in practical ways that support business goals, data use, and operational improvement across many industries and regions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The firm combines technical AI skills with experience in areas such as finance, healthcare, and manufacturing. EY supports clients from early AI planning through deployment and ongoing improvement, with strong attention to governance, risk, and compliance, especially in regulated environments.</p>', 'Services', 'AI Strategy and Roadmap Development – Helps organizations decide where AI can add value and sets clear steps for implementation over time.\r\nIntelligent Automation Solutions – Uses automation tools like RPA and machine learning to reduce manual work and improve process efficiency.\r\nAdvanced Analytics and Data Science – Analyzes large data sets to identify trends, predict outcomes, and support better decision-making.\r\nAI-Powered Search Optimization – Applies NLP and machine learning to improve how digital content is structured and discovered in search systems.\r\nEthical AI Framework Development – Establishes rules and controls to reduce bias, improve transparency, and meet regulatory requirements.\r\nCognitive Technology Integration – Implements tools such as chatbots, image recognition, and language processing to solve specific business problems.\r\nAI Talent Enablement – Trains employees so organizations can build and manage their own AI capabilities internally.\r\nAI Risk Management – Identifies and manages risks related to AI models, data use, and system behavior before and after deployment.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.ey.com/\r\nHeadquarters: London, United Kingdom\r\nFounded: 1903\r\nService Type: AI consulting and professional services\r\nPricing Model: Enterprise-level, project-based or retainer\r\nTypical Clients: Large organizations and regulated industries', '<p>EY&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to combine AI technology with governance and industry knowledge, which is especially useful in regulated sectors. A key limitation is cost, as its services are generally priced for large enterprises, making them less accessible for smaller organizations or early-stage companies.</p>', 9, 7),
(88, 'Capgemini', 'tools/capgemini.jpg', '<p>Capgemini is a global IT consulting and technology services company that helps large organizations use artificial intelligence in their daily operations. Its work focuses on applying AI to real business processes such as IT services, manufacturing, cybersecurity, and data management, rather than experimenting with isolated use cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A key part of Capgemini&rsquo;s approach is &ldquo;Intelligent Industry,&rdquo; which connects AI with software, data, and physical systems. This model is used to improve efficiency, reliability, and decision-making across complex enterprise environments, especially in sectors with strict regulatory and operational requirements.</p>', 'Services', 'Generative AI in Enterprise Service Management (ESM):\r\nUses AI to automate service requests, reduce response time, and improve support quality in IT and business service desks.\r\nAI-powered cybersecurity solutions:\r\nApplies AI to detect threats, manage risks, and support zero-trust security models across enterprise systems.\r\nIntelligent Industry 4.0 solutions:\r\nCombines AI with engineering and operational technology to optimize manufacturing processes and asset performance.\r\nAI innovation for life sciences and healthcare:\r\nSupports research, development, and compliance processes in pharma and MedTech using data and AI tools.\r\nAI-driven business transformation services:\r\nHelps organizations redesign workflows, roles, and systems so AI can be used effectively at scale.\r\nServiceNow AI enhancements:\r\nIntegrates AI into ServiceNow platforms to automate workflows and improve service visibility.\r\nAI-powered analytics and insights:\r\nUses data models to support better decision-making across finance, operations, and customer functions.\r\nSustainable AI solutions:\r\nDesigns AI systems that support environmental, social, and governance (ESG) goals.\r\nEnd-to-end AI delivery:\r\nCovers AI strategy, development, deployment, and long-term scaling within the enterprise.\r\nCross-industry and global AI expertise:\r\nDelivers AI solutions across multiple industries and regions with local compliance support.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.capgemini.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Paris, France\r\nFounded: 1967\r\nPricing: Customized enterprise pricing based on scope and duration\r\nEngagement models: Fixed-price, time and materials, outcome-based\r\nBest use case: Large enterprises and regulated industries', '<p>Capgemini&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to apply AI within complex, regulated enterprise environments using structured and practical methods. A key limitation is that its services are often designed for large organizations, which may make them less accessible for smaller companies with limited budgets or simpler AI needs.</p>', 9, 8),
(89, 'LeewayHertz', 'tools/leewayhertz.jpg', '<p>LeewayHertz is a company that helps businesses use artificial intelligence (AI) in their operations. They work on projects that cover the whole AI process, from planning and testing to putting systems into action and scaling them. Their services aim to improve efficiency and support data-driven decisions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company focuses on practical AI applications, including machine learning, natural language processing, and generative AI. They design solutions that fit into existing IT systems and follow ethical and data governance standards. This approach helps organizations adopt AI with minimal disruption while addressing real business needs.</p>', 'Services', 'Custom AI Model Development: Creates machine learning and deep learning models for tasks like predictions, analyzing images, and understanding text. Helps businesses solve specific problems using data.\r\nGenerative AI Solutions: Uses AI to create content, chatbots, or automated knowledge tools. Reduces manual work and speeds up content generation.\r\nAI Integration & Deployment: Connects AI systems with existing software and cloud platforms. Ensures AI works smoothly without interrupting current operations.\r\nAI Strategy Consulting: Provides planning, feasibility studies, and guidelines for responsible AI. Helps businesses align AI projects with goals and regulations.\r\nIntelligent Automation: Develops AI-powered automation for areas like finance, healthcare, and supply chains. Improves efficiency and reduces repetitive tasks.\r\nData Engineering & Analytics: Builds data pipelines and cleans data for accurate AI insights. Supports better decision-making through reliable information.\r\nIoT & Edge AI: Combines AI with connected devices for real-time processing. Enables smart manufacturing and responsive devices.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.leewayhertz.com/\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California, USA\r\nFounded: Around 2015–2018\r\nPricing: Project-based, typically $50,000–$500,000+\r\nBest Use Case: Companies needing secure, scalable AI in core operations, such as healthcare, finance, or logistics', '<p>LeewayHertz is strong at creating AI solutions that match a company&rsquo;s specific needs, especially in generative AI and natural language processing. One limitation is that their services can be expensive, which may not suit smaller businesses. Their focus on tailored, practical AI projects is their main advantage.</p>', 9, 9),
(90, 'Addepto', 'tools/addepto.jpg', '<p>Addepto is a company that develops artificial intelligence (AI) and big data solutions for businesses. They provide services that help organizations use AI to analyze data, automate processes, and make better decisions. Their work covers planning, building, and implementing AI systems for different industries.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company also focuses on organizing data and turning it into useful insights. This helps businesses understand patterns, predict outcomes, and improve operations. They work with clients to create custom AI tools that address specific problems, including machine learning, natural language processing, and generative AI models.</p>', 'Services', 'AI Consulting Services: Provides guidance on how to start or improve AI projects within a business.\r\nAI Proof of Concept (PoC) Development: Tests AI solutions on a small scale before full deployment to check feasibility.\r\nBig Data Consulting: Helps process and analyze large amounts of data to uncover trends and insights.\r\nGenerative AI Consulting: Assists in building AI models that can create content or generate predictions.\r\nData Organization: Structures raw data so it can be used effectively in AI applications.\r\nBusiness Intelligence Solutions: Transforms data into visual reports and dashboards to support decision-making.\r\nNatural Language Processing (NLP) Applications: Analyzes text or speech for sentiment, meaning, or chatbot functions.\r\nCustom AI Solution Development: Builds AI systems tailored to a company’s specific needs and goals.\r\nMachine Learning Model Integration: Adds predictive analytics and automation to existing systems.\r\nAI Strategy and Roadmap Development: Plans long-term steps for AI adoption and digital transformation.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.addepto.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Not publicly available\r\nFounded: Not publicly available\r\nPricing: Custom, typically $150–300 per hour\r\nBest Use Case: Medium to large companies that want to implement AI or improve data analysis', '<p>Addepto&rsquo;s main strength is its full-cycle approach, from planning to implementing AI solutions, which can help businesses use AI effectively. A limitation is the lack of public details about its history, clients, or past projects, making it harder to assess experience and market presence.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 9, 10),
(91, 'Cambridge Consultants', 'tools/cambridge-consultants.jpg', '<p>Cambridge Consultants is a technology consulting firm that focuses on applying artificial intelligence to business problems. They combine technical knowledge with practical solutions to help organizations use AI in areas like automation, data analysis, and digital transformation. Their work often involves building custom AI models for specific business needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company works closely with clients to integrate AI into existing systems and processes. They provide expertise in machine learning, natural language processing, computer vision, and other AI technologies. Their approach is technical and research-based, reflecting their connection to Cambridge&rsquo;s academic and innovation ecosystem.</p>', 'Service', 'Machine learning model development: Builds AI models that can predict trends, classify data, or make recommendations, improving decision-making.\r\nNatural language processing (NLP): Creates systems that understand and respond to human language, such as chatbots or text analysis tools.\r\nAI strategy consulting: Helps organizations plan how to adopt AI effectively, aligning it with business goals.\r\nDigital transformation integration: Incorporates AI into existing business systems to make processes more efficient.\r\nComputer vision and image recognition: Uses AI to analyze images or video for automation, monitoring, or insights.\r\nPredictive analytics: Analyzes large datasets to forecast outcomes like sales, customer behavior, or maintenance needs.\r\nCustom AI solutions: Designs specialized AI applications to address unique problems in a business.\r\nAI ethics and governance: Advises on responsible AI use, including fairness, transparency, and compliance with regulations.\r\nIoT integration: Connects AI with Internet of Things devices to enable smart operations or monitoring.\r\nModel optimization and monitoring: Continuously checks AI systems to ensure accuracy, efficiency, and relevance over time.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.cambridgeconsultants.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Cambridge, United Kingdom\r\nFounded: Early 2000s (estimated)\r\nPricing: Custom project-based, premium enterprise model\r\nBest Use Case: Mid-to-large organizations seeking AI integration and digital transformation', '<p>Cambridge Consultants shows strong technical expertise in AI and can deliver solutions that are tailored to complex business challenges. A limitation is that their services are positioned at a premium level, which may be difficult for smaller companies or startups to afford. Their approach suits organizations that need advanced AI implementation rather than broad consulting coverage.</p>', 9, 11),
(92, 'BotsCrew', 'tools/botscrew.jpg', '<p>BotsCrew is an AI consulting company that focuses on building chatbots and conversational AI tools for businesses. They use technologies like natural language processing (NLP) and machine learning to make chatbots that understand user questions and respond in a human-like way. Their solutions aim to improve customer service and operational efficiency.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The company works with businesses of different sizes but mainly targets medium to large enterprises. Their tools can be used on websites, apps, social media, and messaging platforms. BotsCrew&rsquo;s services include creating chatbots, analyzing performance data, and improving AI systems over time to meet specific business needs.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'Service', 'Custom chatbot development: Builds chatbots tailored to a business’s needs and industry.\r\nAdvanced NLP: Helps chatbots understand the meaning behind user questions for more accurate answers.\r\nMulti-channel deployment: Allows chatbots to work on websites, apps, social media, and messaging platforms.\r\nConversational flow design: Organizes the chatbot’s responses to make interactions smoother and easier for users.\r\nAI analytics dashboard: Provides real-time data on chatbot performance and user interactions.\r\nSystem integration: Connects chatbots to CRM, ERP, or other business systems to share information automatically.\r\nMachine learning training: Improves chatbot responses over time based on past interactions.\r\nMultilingual support: Enables chatbots to communicate in multiple languages for global users.\r\nVoice interfaces: Lets users interact with chatbots through speech.\r\nA/B testing: Tests different conversation paths to see which works best for users.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://botscrew.com/\r\nHeadquarters: Likely in San Francisco or New York\r\nFounded: Around 2016\r\nPricing: Custom enterprise pricing, likely starting at $10,000+\r\nBest Use Case: Businesses needing advanced customer service automation', '<p>BotsCrew&rsquo;s main strength is its deep focus on conversational AI, which allows it to build effective chatbots that improve customer support. A limitation is that it mainly specializes in chatbots, so it may not provide broader AI solutions for other business areas. Its services are best suited for medium to large companies that handle high volumes of customer interactions.</p>', 9, 12),
(93, 'Synthesia', 'tools/synthesia.jpg', '<p><strong>Synthesia</strong> is an AI-based platform that helps people create videos using digital presenters instead of real actors. Users write text, and the system turns it into a video where an AI avatar speaks the script in a clear and controlled way.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The tool is mainly used by companies that need training, internal updates, or marketing videos. It reduces the need for cameras, studios, or presenters, which makes video creation faster and more consistent, especially for teams working across different countries.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Text-to-video with AI avatars – Users enter written text, and the platform converts it into a video with a virtual presenter speaking the content.\r\nLibrary of AI avatars – Users can choose from many digital presenters with different appearances to match their audience or use case.\r\nMulti-language support – Videos can be created in over 120 languages, helping teams communicate with international audiences.\r\nAccurate lip-syncing – The avatar’s mouth movements are matched closely to the spoken audio to improve clarity and realism.\r\nText-to-speech voices – Users can adjust voice tone and speed to fit training, marketing, or informational videos.\r\nVideo templates – Pre-built layouts help users create structured videos without starting from scratch.\r\nBrand customization – Companies can add logos, colors, and fonts to keep videos consistent with their brand.\r\nAPI access – Larger organizations can connect Synthesia with other systems to automate video creation.\r\nTeam collaboration tools – Multiple users can work on the same video project, which supports shared workflows.\r\nPerformance analytics – Built-in data shows how viewers interact with videos, helping teams measure engagement.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.synthesia.io\r\nHeadquarters: London, United Kingdom\r\nFounded: 2017\r\nPricing: Subscription-based, starting at around $30 per month\r\nBest use case: Business training, internal communication, and marketing videos at scale', '<p>Synthesia&rsquo;s main strength is its clear and reliable AI avatars, which work well for structured business content in many languages. A limitation is that avatar expressions can feel slightly artificial in some situations. Overall, it suits organizations that value consistency and efficiency more than emotional or creative presentation.</p>', 11, 1),
(94, 'D-ID', 'tools/d-id.jpg', '<p>D-ID is an AI platform that turns still photos into talking videos. Users upload a face image, add text or audio, and the system creates a video where the person appears to speak naturally. The focus is on facial movement and clear lip synchronization.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform supports many languages and is used to create simple presenter-style videos. It is designed for marketing, training, customer communication, and internal business messages where realistic talking avatars are helpful and speed matters.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Creative Reality™ Studio\r\nA web-based tool where users type text or upload audio to quickly create talking avatar videos without technical skills.\r\nFacial animation and lip-sync\r\nThe system analyzes speech and matches mouth movement and facial expressions to the audio, reducing the need for manual video editing.\r\nMultilingual support\r\nText-to-speech works in over 100 languages, helping teams create content for different regions without hiring voice actors.\r\nText-to-speech voices\r\nUsers can choose from many voice options to match tone, language, or audience needs.\r\nAPI access\r\nDevelopers can integrate avatar video generation into apps, websites, or internal systems automatically.\r\nCustom voice upload\r\nAllows businesses to use their own recorded voices instead of default synthetic voices.\r\nHigh-speed video rendering\r\nVideos are generated faster than real-time, which helps when producing large amounts of content.\r\nScalable infrastructure\r\nThe system can handle many requests at once, supporting enterprise-level video production.\r\niPhone mobile app\r\nEnables basic avatar video creation directly from a mobile device.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.d-id.com\r\nCompany type: AI digital human and avatar platform\r\nFounded: 2017\r\nHeadquarters: Israel\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based, with multiple plan levels\r\nPrimary use cases: Marketing, e-learning, customer support, internal communication', '<p>D-ID is strong at turning static images into realistic talking faces with clear lip-sync and wide language support. This makes it useful for simple presenter-style videos at scale. A limitation is that it mainly focuses on head-and-shoulder avatars, with limited options for full-body movement or complex visual scenes.</p>', 11, 2),
(95, 'HeyGen', 'tools/heygen.jpg', '<p>HeyGen is an AI-based video creation platform that helps users turn text and static content into videos with digital human presenters. It is designed for people who need videos but do not want to film themselves or hire actors. The platform works entirely online and does not require technical skills.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The main focus of HeyGen is creating videos where AI avatars speak naturally and match the script provided by the user. It supports many languages and voices, making it useful for global teams. Users commonly apply it to marketing, training, education, and internal communication content.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI Avatar Generation – Creates digital human presenters that speak scripted text with synchronized lip movement and facial motion.\r\nText-to-Video Tool – Converts written scripts into videos automatically, removing the need for cameras or microphones.\r\nMulti-Language Support – Allows users to produce videos in over 40 languages, helping reach international audiences.\r\nVoice Selection – Offers hundreds of voice options so users can choose tone, accent, and speaking style.\r\nFace Swap Function – Replaces a face in a video while keeping body movement and expressions consistent.\r\nTalking Photo Feature – Animates still photos so they appear to speak, useful for simple presentations.\r\nVideo Templates – Provides ready-made layouts that speed up video creation for common business needs.\r\nBrand Kit Tools – Keeps logos, colors, and fonts consistent across all videos.\r\nAPI Access – Lets developers connect HeyGen’s avatar features to other software or platforms.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.heygen.com\r\nProduct Type: AI avatar and video creation platform\r\nFree Plan: Includes 1 minute of video credit\r\nBasic Plan: $24 per month with 10 minutes of video\r\nPro Plan: $180 per month with 90 minutes of video\r\nEnterprise Plan: Custom pricing\r\nVideo Quality: Up to 1080p resolution\r\nCommon Uses: Marketing videos, training content, presentations, customer messages', '<p>HeyGen&rsquo;s main strength is the clear and natural-looking avatar speech, which reduces the need for live presenters. A limitation is the pricing, as longer or frequent video creation requires higher plans. It fits teams that need consistent video output but may be costly for solo creators.</p>', 11, 3),
(96, 'Colossyan', 'tools/colossyan.jpg', '<p>Colossyan is an AI-based platform that helps users create digital avatars for videos and presentations. It is mainly used for professional content such as training videos, internal communication, and marketing materials. Users can generate videos without filming real people or setting up recording equipment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform focuses on combining avatars with text and speech to produce clear, consistent video content. It supports multiple languages and is designed for teams that need repeatable, scalable video creation rather than one-time creative projects.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI avatar creation – Users select or customize digital presenters instead of using human actors, saving time and production costs.\r\nText-to-speech video generation – Written scripts are converted into spoken video, removing the need for voice recording.\r\nAvatar customization – Clothing, appearance, and style can be adjusted to match company or project needs.\r\nMulti-language support – Videos can be created in different languages to reach international audiences.\r\nVideo-based training tools – Helps companies produce consistent learning and onboarding content.\r\nTemplate-based workflow – Reusable layouts make it easier to create multiple videos with the same format.\r\nCloud-based platform – No local installation is required, allowing teams to work from different locations.\r\nBrand-focused avatars – Organizations can keep a consistent visual identity across many videos.\r\nIntegration options – Content can be shared or embedded into other platforms and systems.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.colossyan.com\r\nProduct type: AI avatar and video generation platform\r\nTarget users: Businesses, educators, and content teams\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based with multiple plans\r\nPrimary use cases: Training, marketing, internal communication, and educational videos', '<p>Colossyan&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to create consistent, professional videos without filming real presenters. This is useful for teams producing large volumes of content. One limitation is that new users may need time to learn the workflow, especially if they have no prior experience with video or script-based tools.</p>', 11, 4),
(97, 'Elai', 'tools/elai.jpg', '<p>Elai is an AI-based video creation tool that turns written text into videos with digital presenters. Users can type a script, choose an avatar, and generate a video without recording themselves. The system combines text understanding, speech generation, and animated visuals to produce spoken video content.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is mainly designed for business, training, and educational use. It focuses on clear delivery, consistent presentation, and easy production rather than entertainment. Elai helps teams create videos faster when they need repeatable formats such as lessons, guides, or product explanations.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Text-to-video generation\r\nConverts written scripts into videos automatically, removing the need for cameras or studios.\r\nAI avatar presenters\r\nUses digital human avatars to deliver content, helping users appear on screen without filming.\r\nMultiple avatar choices\r\nOffers presenters with different looks and styles to fit various professional contexts.\r\nText-to-speech voices\r\nTurns text into spoken audio, solving the need for voice recording equipment.\r\nMulti-language support\r\nAllows video creation in different languages for international audiences.\r\nCustom avatar option\r\nEnables brands to create avatars based on real people for consistent identity.\r\nVideo templates\r\nProvides ready-made layouts that speed up creation for common use cases.\r\nVisual editing tools\r\nLets users adjust backgrounds, text, and media without video editing skills.\r\nBulk video creation\r\nHelps teams generate many similar videos at once, saving time.\r\nPerformance analytics\r\nTracks how videos perform, helping users understand engagement.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.elai.io\r\nProduct type: AI avatar video generation platform\r\nMain focus: Business, training, and educational videos\r\nVideo input: Written text\r\nOutput: Avatar-based videos\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based plans\r\nTrial availability: Likely offered\r\nTarget users: Companies, educators, content teams', '<p>Elai&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to create professional-looking videos quickly from text, which is useful for training and internal communication. A limitation is that avatar expressions can feel limited compared to real people, especially in emotional or highly dynamic presentations.</p>', 11, 5),
(98, 'DeepBrain AI', 'tools/deepbrainai.jpg', '<p>DeepBrain AI is a platform that helps users create videos using AI-generated human avatars. It turns written scripts into videos where a virtual person speaks the text in a natural way. The system is designed to be simple so users do not need video production skills.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform focuses on realistic digital humans and supports many languages. It is often used for business communication, learning materials, and informational videos. Users can choose from ready-made avatars and templates to quickly create consistent video content.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Realistic AI avatars\r\nUses pre-built digital humans that show natural facial movement, helping videos feel clear and understandable without filming real people.\r\nText-to-speech in many languages\r\nConverts written scripts into spoken audio in over 80 languages, which helps teams create content for international audiences.\r\nScript-to-video workflow\r\nAllows users to paste text and generate a full video automatically, reducing time spent on recording and editing.\r\nBuilt-in video editor\r\nProvides simple tools for adjusting scenes, text, and layouts, making basic edits possible without external software.\r\nNo technical skills required\r\nDesigned for non-experts, so users can create videos without learning complex production tools.\r\nVideo templates for different uses\r\nOffers ready-made layouts for training, marketing, and internal communication to speed up content creation.\r\nFree plan availability\r\nLets new users test the platform and create videos without entering payment details.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.deepbrainai.io\r\nHeadquarters: Palo Alto, California, USA\r\nMain focus: AI avatar-based video creation\r\nPricing: Free tier available; paid plans offered\r\nBest use cases: Training videos, marketing content, corporate messages, educational materials', '<p>DeepBrain AI works well for producing clear avatar-based videos quickly, especially for multilingual content. The main strength is its realistic avatars combined with an easy setup process. A limitation is that avatar customization and editing controls are fairly limited, which may restrict users who need more detailed visual adjustments.</p>', 11, 6);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(99, 'Fotor', 'tools/fotor.jpg', '<p>Fotor is an online photo editing and design platform that includes an AI-based avatar generator. Users can upload a photo and turn it into an avatar using different visual styles. The tool is designed for people who want simple controls and clear results without technical knowledge.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The avatar feature works inside Fotor&rsquo;s larger editing system. This allows users to adjust their avatars after generation using common photo tools. Because everything is web-based, users can create and edit avatars directly in a browser without installing software.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI avatar generation from photos\r\nUpload a photo and the system analyzes facial features to create an avatar automatically.\r\nMultiple visual styles\r\nUsers can choose styles such as cartoon, anime, or realistic to match different personal or work needs.\r\nFacial feature enhancement\r\nThe AI adjusts lighting, proportions, and details to improve clarity while keeping the face recognizable.\r\nCustom avatar adjustments\r\nUsers can change hairstyles, accessories, and filters to better match their appearance or brand.\r\nProfessional headshot creation\r\nDesigned formats help create clean profile images suitable for platforms like LinkedIn.\r\nSocial media size presets\r\nBuilt-in dimensions ensure avatars fit correctly on different social media platforms.\r\nBackground removal and replacement\r\nThe tool can remove messy backgrounds and replace them with simple or professional ones.\r\nBatch avatar generation\r\nUsers can create several avatar versions from one photo to compare styles quickly.\r\nPhoto editing integration\r\nAvatars can be refined using Fotor’s standard editing tools such as brightness and contrast.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.fotor.com\r\nHeadquarters: Hong Kong\r\nAdditional offices: United States\r\nFounded: 2012\r\nPricing model: Freemium\r\nFree plan: Limited features with watermarks\r\nPaid plan: Fotor Pro\r\nMonthly price: About $8.99\r\nYearly price: About $39.99\r\nBest for: Professional profiles, social media, and personal branding', '<p>Fotor&rsquo;s main strength is that avatar creation and photo editing are combined in one place, which saves time and effort. A clear limitation is that the free version restricts image quality and adds watermarks, which reduces its usefulness for professional purposes.</p>', 11, 7),
(100, 'Avatar SDK', 'tools/avatar-sdk.jpg', '<p>Avatar SDK is a software toolkit that helps developers add avatar creation features to their apps. It focuses on turning user photos into digital characters using AI and 3D modeling. The product is built mainly for technical teams rather than everyday users.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The SDK is used in games, social platforms, and virtual or augmented reality projects. It gives developers control over how avatars look and behave, while allowing integration across different devices and systems through APIs.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Photo-based face mapping – Uses AI to analyze a photo and map facial features accurately, reducing manual avatar setup.\r\n3D avatar generation – Creates full 3D models that can be used in games, VR, or animated scenes.\r\nAvatar customization tools – Lets developers adjust facial details, hair, and accessories to match different user needs.\r\nMultiple visual styles – Supports realistic, stylized, cartoon, and anime looks to fit different products.\r\nCross-platform support – Works across web, mobile, desktop, and XR environments, avoiding platform lock-in.\r\nAPI-based integration – Provides APIs so teams can connect avatar features directly into existing applications.\r\nReal-time animation – Maps expressions and movements to avatars for more natural interaction.\r\nNFT-ready avatars – Allows avatars to be used as blockchain-based digital assets when required.\r\nPrivacy control options – Offers on-device processing or secure cloud handling to protect user data.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://avatarsdk.com\r\nProduct type: Developer-focused avatar SDK\r\nTarget users: Game studios, social platforms, VR/AR developers\r\nPricing: Usage-based or tiered plans (details not publicly fixed)\r\nDeployment: Cloud-based or on-device processing\r\nAvatar output: 3D models and animated characters', '<p>Avatar SDK&rsquo;s main strength is its flexibility, giving developers detailed control over avatar creation and integration. A clear limitation is that it requires technical skills, which may slow down small teams or non-developers. It fits best in projects where customization and system-level control are more important than ease of use.</p>', 11, 8),
(101, 'GAN.AI', 'tools/gan-ai.jpg', '<p>GAN.AI is a platform that focuses on creating digital human avatars using modern machine learning methods. It is designed for businesses and creators who need realistic visual representations for online use, such as websites, videos, or applications, without relying on real human actors.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform aims to support consistent digital identities across different channels. By offering customizable avatars and technical integration options, it helps teams produce visual content at scale while keeping control over appearance, behavior, and language output.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Photorealistic avatar creation – Uses generative models to produce human-like faces and visuals that reduce the need for photoshoots or actors.\r\nFacial and appearance customization – Allows users to adjust facial structure, hair, clothing, and expressions to match specific brand or character needs.\r\nNatural motion and expressions – Generates realistic movements and gestures to make avatars look less static in videos or live interactions.\r\nReal-time animation support – Enables avatars to respond dynamically, which is useful for interactive content or customer-facing tools.\r\nAPI access for developers – Lets teams integrate avatar features into their own software, apps, or workflows.\r\nMulti-language interaction – Supports different languages so avatars can communicate with global audiences.\r\nHigh-resolution output – Produces visuals suitable for professional marketing, presentations, and digital media.\r\nPrivacy-focused data handling – Designed to manage user data securely and limit misuse of digital identities.\r\nFeedback-based improvement – Uses user input to refine avatar quality over time.\r\nCross-platform compatibility – Works across websites, mobile apps, and social platforms without major format changes.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.gan.ai\r\nCompany type: AI avatar and digital human platform\r\nPrimary focus: Digital avatars for marketing, content, and customer interaction\r\nLikely founded: Around 2019–2021\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based, with multiple tiers\r\nIntended users: Businesses, agencies, developers, and content creators', '<p>GAN.AI&rsquo;s main strength is the level of control it offers over avatar appearance and behavior, which is useful for professional use cases. One limitation is that creating highly realistic avatars may require more setup time and technical knowledge compared to simpler tools. Overall, it suits teams that value quality over speed.</p>', 11, 9),
(102, 'Vidboard AI', 'tools/vidboard-ai.jpg', '<p><strong>Vidboard AI</strong> is a tool that turns text and existing digital materials into videos with AI-generated avatars. Users can create videos without cameras, studios, or advanced editing skills. The platform focuses on helping teams produce videos faster by using automated scripts, voices, and visuals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The software is designed for routine video production such as marketing messages, training lessons, and educational content. By combining text-to-video technology with digital presenters, it allows users to present information in video form while keeping branding and structure consistent across multiple projects.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI Avatar Generation: Creates digital presenters that speak the script, reducing the need for human actors or filming.\r\nDocument-to-Video Conversion: Turns PDFs, Word files, or slides into narrated videos, saving time on manual video creation.\r\nAI Script Generator: Produces draft scripts from text inputs, helping users who struggle with writing or structure.\r\nAI Voice Cloning: Generates voiceovers that match a chosen tone or brand voice without recording audio.\r\nFaceless Video Creation: Allows videos without visible presenters, useful for product demos or abstract topics.\r\nURL-to-Video: Converts web pages into videos, making it easier to reuse existing online content.\r\nTimeline with Triggers: Lets users control when visuals, text, and audio appear for clearer presentation flow.\r\nAI Caption Generator: Automatically adds captions, improving accessibility and search visibility.\r\nMultimedia Assets Integration: Provides access to stock music, images, and clips to avoid sourcing assets elsewhere.\r\nText-to-Video Technology: Transforms written content into video format for audiences who prefer visual learning.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.vidboard.ai\r\nProduct type: AI-powered video and avatar creation platform\r\nTarget users: Marketing teams, educators, and content creators\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based plans\r\nFree trial: Availability indicated on the website\r\nHardware needs: No filming equipment required', '<p>Vidboard AI&rsquo;s main strength is its ability to turn written content into structured videos with minimal effort. This makes it practical for teams producing content regularly. A limitation is that avatar movements can sometimes look less natural, which may require small edits before publishing.</p>', 11, 10),
(103, 'Monica AI', 'tools/monica-ai.jpg', '<p>Monica AI is an online tool for creating digital avatars using artificial intelligence. It allows users to make avatars from text descriptions or photos without needing design skills. The platform is built for people who want consistent digital characters for work, content, or online profiles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The system focuses on clear controls and flexible outputs rather than complex setup. Users can adjust faces, styles, and expressions and export avatars for different uses. It is designed to support repeated creation and editing, which is useful for teams or individuals working across multiple platforms.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Text-to-avatar creation – Users describe a person in text, and the system generates an avatar based on those details.\r\nPhoto-to-avatar conversion – A real photo can be uploaded and turned into a digital avatar while keeping key facial traits.\r\nLive customization tools – Facial features, hair, clothes, and expressions can be changed with instant visual feedback.\r\nMultiple export formats – Avatars can be downloaded in formats suited for social media, games, or presentations.\r\nStyle selection – Users can choose between realistic, cartoon, anime, or artistic visual styles.\r\nExpression controls – Different emotions and facial expressions can be applied to make avatars look more natural.\r\nBasic animation support – Some avatars can include simple movements or lip-sync for video use.\r\nBatch generation – Multiple versions of an avatar can be created at once to compare or test options.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://monica.im\r\nProduct type: AI avatar generation platform\r\nInput methods: Text descriptions and photos\r\nOutput uses: Profiles, marketing, games, virtual meetings\r\nPricing model: Free tier with paid subscription options\r\nTypical users: Creators, marketers, developers, small teams\r\nEditing support: Avatars can be saved and modified later', '<p>Monica AI is useful for quickly creating and adjusting digital avatars without technical knowledge, especially when consistency across platforms is needed. A clear strength is its flexible customization system. One limitation is that highly detailed realism or uncommon physical traits may not always be represented accurately.</p>', 11, 11),
(104, 'DupDub', 'tools/dupdub.jpg', '<p>DupDub is an AI tool that helps users create digital avatars using text, images, or voice. It focuses on making avatars look and move in a natural way, with realistic facial expressions and speech. The platform is designed for people who need avatars for videos, websites, or online content.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The system uses machine learning and language processing to guide users through avatar creation without technical skills. Avatars can be adjusted for different platforms and reused later. DupDub is mainly used by creators and businesses that want consistent digital characters.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Text-to-avatar creation – Users can generate avatars by describing them in text, reducing the need for manual design.\r\nFacial animation and emotions – The system maps expressions to speech, helping avatars look more natural while talking.\r\nAppearance customization – Users can adjust features like age, skin tone, hairstyle, and clothing to match their needs.\r\nVoice synthesis support – Avatars can speak using AI-generated voices, useful for videos and presentations.\r\nMulti-platform support – Avatars are designed to work on web, mobile, and VR platforms.\r\nAPI access – Developers can connect DupDub to their own apps or services.\r\nHigh-resolution export – Finished avatars can be downloaded as images, animations, or video files.\r\nBatch avatar creation – Users can create multiple versions at once, saving time on large projects.\r\nPrivacy options – Some processing can be done locally to reduce data sharing.\r\nLearning system – The platform improves results over time based on usage patterns.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.dupdub.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2020\r\nPricing model: Freemium\r\nPaid plans start at: $19 per month\r\nCommercial use: Available on paid plans\r\nPrimary users: Content creators, marketers, and businesses', '<p>DupDub is strong in producing avatars with natural facial movement and speech, which makes them suitable for professional content. The main limitation is that creating detailed avatars can require strong hardware, especially on older devices. Overall, it works well for users who need repeatable and realistic digital characters.</p>', 11, 12),
(105, 'JoggAI', 'tools/joggai.jpg', '<p><strong>JoggAI</strong> is an AI-based platform that helps users create digital avatars that look and move like real people. Users can generate avatars from photos and adjust their appearance without needing design or technical skills. The system is built for people who need clear and consistent digital characters.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is commonly used for videos, presentations, online learning, and customer-facing content. It focuses on making avatars that are easy to create, simple to customize, and ready to use across different digital channels.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Photo-based avatar creation\r\nUsers upload images, and the system maps facial details to build a realistic digital avatar.\r\nFacial and appearance customization\r\nAllows adjustment of facial features, hair, clothing, and accessories to match personal or brand needs.\r\nReal-time animation\r\nGenerates natural head movement and facial expressions for videos or live presentations.\r\nText-to-speech voices\r\nConverts written text into spoken audio using multiple voices and supported languages.\r\nEmotion and expression control\r\nDetects emotional cues and applies matching facial expressions for more natural communication.\r\nExport and format support\r\nAvatars can be exported in formats suitable for social media, presentations, and web platforms.\r\nDeveloper API access\r\nEnables teams to integrate avatars into websites, apps, or customer service tools.\r\nPre-built avatar templates\r\nOffers ready-made styles designed for marketing, education, and business use cases.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.jogg.ai\r\nProduct type: AI avatar generation platform\r\nLikely founded: Between 2019 and 2021\r\nPricing model: Subscription-based with multiple plan levels\r\nIntended users: Content creators, marketers, educators, and support teams', '<p>JoggAI&rsquo;s main strength is the visual quality of its avatars, which look consistent and professional across different uses. A possible limitation is that more complex avatars may take longer to generate. Overall, it works well for teams that need reliable digital presenters without manual design work.</p>', 11, 13),
(106, 'Reface', 'tools/reface.jpg', '<p>Reface is an AI-based platform that focuses on swapping faces in videos, GIFs, and images. It allows users to place their own face onto existing visual content while keeping expressions and movements aligned with the original media. The tool is mainly designed for entertainment and casual content creation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform works through automated face analysis and mapping. Users upload a photo, select a template, and the system applies the face to the chosen content. Reface is commonly used for short videos and memes that are shared on social media platforms.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Real-time face swapping – Detects facial landmarks and replaces faces in videos while keeping movements consistent.\r\nTemplate library – Provides ready-made scenes and clips so users do not need to create content from scratch.\r\nPhoto animation – Converts still images into short animations by adding facial motion.\r\nSocial media sharing – Allows direct export to social platforms, reducing manual upload steps.\r\nMobile apps (iOS and Android) – Enables users to create content directly from their phones.\r\nAvatar filters and styles – Applies visual effects to adjust appearance without manual editing.\r\nSimple interface – Designed so users can complete tasks without technical knowledge.\r\nAdaptive rendering system – Improves face alignment based on repeated usage patterns.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.reface.ai\r\nProduct type: AI face-swapping and avatar tool\r\nPlatform availability: iOS and Android\r\nPricing model: Freemium with optional subscription\r\nPrimary use: Entertainment and social media content\r\nFull-body avatar support: Limited\r\nBusiness-focused avatars: Not the main focus', '<p>Reface performs well in face swapping and delivers consistent results with minimal effort from the user. Its main strength is the accuracy of facial alignment in short videos. A clear limitation is the lack of tools for creating original or full-body avatars, which reduces its usefulness for professional or business-focused content.</p>', 11, 14),
(107, 'Aleyda Solís', 'tools/aleyda-sol-s.jpg', '<p>Aleyda Sol&iacute;s&rsquo; website is a clear example of how an experienced SEO professional presents her work online. It focuses on practical information, structured content, and easy navigation. The site explains what she does, how she works, and the type of SEO problems she helps solve.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The website also works as a real-world demonstration of SEO principles. Pages are organized around topics, supported by internal links and technical best practices. This makes the site useful both for potential clients and for SEO professionals who want to study how advanced SEO concepts are applied in practice.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Case study library – Shows past SEO projects and explains the steps taken and the results achieved.\r\nStructured data usage – Helps search engines better understand page content and display richer search results.\r\nContent hub structure – Groups related articles together to improve topic clarity and internal linking.\r\nMobile-first design – Ensures the site loads quickly and works well on phones and tablets.\r\nInternational SEO setup – Uses hreflang to guide search engines to the correct language or country version.\r\nTechnical audit examples – Demonstrates how website issues are identified and fixed.\r\nRegular blog updates – Shares analysis of SEO changes and practical guidance based on real experience.\r\nSpeaking portfolio – Lists conferences and events to show industry involvement.\r\nClient testimonials – Provides feedback with clear outcomes rather than general praise.\r\nSEO resources section – Offers tools and templates that help others apply SEO methods correctly.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.aleydasolis.com\r\nHeadquarters: Madrid, Spain\r\nFounded: Around 2010\r\nPricing: Custom consulting rates\r\nBest use case: Enterprise SEO and international search projects', '<p>The main strength of the website is how clearly it explains complex SEO work using real examples. This makes the expertise easy to verify. A limitation is that the focus on large-scale and international projects may not fully match the needs of small businesses or beginners looking for simple SEO portfolio ideas.</p>', 10, 1),
(108, 'Neil Patel', 'tools/neil-patel.jpg', '<p>Neil Patel&rsquo;s website is an online platform focused on search engine optimization and digital marketing. It combines learning materials with practical tools that help users understand how search engines work and how websites can improve visibility using data rather than guesswork.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The site is often used as a reference because it shows real examples of SEO work. These examples explain what was changed, why it mattered, and what results followed. This makes the platform useful for people who want to study SEO methods that are already tested.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO audit tools – Scan a website and point out technical and content issues that may hurt search rankings.\r\nAI content writer – Helps create basic SEO-focused text by suggesting structure and keywords.\r\nKeyword research – Finds search terms and shows how hard they are to rank for.\r\nBacklink analysis – Lists websites linking to a domain and highlights missing link opportunities.\r\nCompetitor analysis – Shows what keywords and pages competitors rank for.\r\nRank tracking – Tracks how keyword positions change over time.\r\nTechnical SEO suggestions – Identifies crawl, speed, and indexing problems.\r\nCustom reports – Turns SEO data into simple reports for sharing or review.\r\nGoogle data integration – Pulls data from Analytics and Search Console into one place.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://neilpatel.com\r\nFounder: Neil Patel\r\nHeadquarters: California, United States\r\nFounded: Early 2010s\r\nPricing model: Freemium\r\nPaid plans: Roughly $12–$120 per month\r\nTarget users: Marketers, SEO specialists, small business owners', '<p>The main strength of the platform is its clear connection between SEO actions and results, which helps users learn from real examples. One limitation is that the amount of data can be difficult to manage for beginners who are not familiar with SEO terms and reports.</p>', 10, 2),
(109, 'Brian Dean', 'tools/brian-dean.jpg', '<p>Backlinko is an educational website focused on search engine optimization. It was created in 2013 by Brian Dean as a place to publish practical SEO guides, experiments, and case studies. The site is often used as an example of how strong SEO practices work in real situations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The website is known for explaining SEO concepts through data, screenshots, and clear steps. Many of its pages rank well in Google, which helps demonstrate the same techniques being taught. In 2022, Backlinko was acquired by Semrush and became part of a larger marketing platform.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO audit guides – Explain how to review a website step by step to find technical and content-related SEO problems.\r\nCase studies – Show real traffic and ranking changes to explain what worked and what did not.\r\nSkyscraper Technique – Describes how to improve existing top-ranking content so it earns more backlinks.\r\nGoogle ranking factor analysis – Breaks down known and tested factors that influence search rankings.\r\nSEO checklists – Provide structured task lists to avoid missing key optimization steps.\r\nE-E-A-T content guidance – Explains how to improve trust and credibility signals in content.\r\nInternal linking frameworks – Show how linking between pages helps search engines understand site structure.\r\nCompetitor analysis methods – Teach how to study competing pages to find ranking opportunities.\r\nKeyword research approach – Focuses on matching keywords with search intent, not just volume.\r\nPerformance tracking systems – Explain how to measure SEO results using traffic and ranking data.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://backlinko.com\r\nFounded: 2013\r\nFounder: Brian Dean\r\nHeadquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA\r\nOwnership: Acquired by Semrush in 2022\r\nPricing: Free educational content\r\nBest for: SEO professionals, marketers, and content writers', '<p>Backlinko is strong because it explains SEO using clear examples and real data instead of theory. This makes it useful for learning and reference. One limitation is that some strategies require significant time and resources, which may be difficult for individuals or small teams to apply fully.</p>', 10, 3),
(110, 'Steve Wiideman', 'tools/steve-wiideman.jpg', '<p>Steve Wiideman has worked in search engine optimization since 1998. He leads Wiideman Consulting Group and focuses on solving technical and structural SEO problems. His work often involves websites with many pages, locations, or business units that need consistent and accurate search visibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He also teaches SEO-related courses at <strong>University of California San Diego</strong> and <strong>California State University Fullerton</strong>. This teaching background supports a structured approach to SEO that combines theory with real-world testing and long-term search performance.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Franchise and multi-location SEO\r\nHelps businesses manage search visibility across many locations while keeping brand information consistent and accurate.\r\nTechnical SEO for large websites\r\nImproves crawling, indexing, and site structure so search engines can correctly access and understand complex sites.\r\nAI-supported content optimization\r\nUses data and language analysis to align content with search intent and topic relevance.\r\nLocal search optimization\r\nImproves visibility in local results through accurate business listings and location-specific signals.\r\nSEO measurement and reporting\r\nTracks rankings, traffic, and conversions to show how SEO work affects business results.\r\nCustom SEO training programs\r\nTeaches teams how SEO works so they can maintain and improve performance internally.\r\nAlgorithm-aware SEO strategy\r\nAdjusts SEO methods as search engines change how they rank and display results.\r\nSemantic search optimization\r\nStructures content so search engines better understand meaning, context, and relationships between topics.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.stevewiideman.com\r\nCompany: Wiideman Consulting Group\r\nHeadquarters: La Mirada, California, USA\r\nSEO experience since: 1998\r\nPricing model: Project-based or monthly retainer\r\nTypical clients: Franchises, multi-location businesses, and large organizations', '<p>Steve Wiideman&rsquo;s main strength is his long experience with technically complex and multi-location SEO projects. This makes his work useful for large or structured businesses. A limitation is that his services may not suit small companies with limited budgets, as the work is designed for larger and more demanding SEO needs.</p>', 10, 4),
(111, 'Dixon Jones', '', '<p>Dixon Jones&rsquo; website presents a clear record of SEO work based on real projects. It focuses on showing how search problems were identified, what actions were taken, and what changed afterward. The content is written for readers who want to understand practical SEO decisions rather than general advice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The portfolio is organized around case studies from different industries. Each example explains the starting situation, the technical or content issues involved, and the results achieved. This structure helps readers see how SEO methods are applied step by step and adjusted over time.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Detailed case studies\r\nEach case study explains the initial problem, the actions taken, and the final results, helping readers understand the full SEO process.\r\nBefore-and-after performance data\r\nTraffic, rankings, and other metrics are shown to make changes measurable and easy to compare.\r\nClear explanation of SEO methods\r\nTechniques are described in plain terms, reducing confusion around complex SEO concepts.\r\nMulti-industry examples\r\nProjects from different sectors show how strategies change depending on business type and competition level.\r\nUse of AI-based analysis\r\nData tools are used to analyze keywords and content patterns more efficiently than manual methods.\r\nStrong focus on technical SEO\r\nSite structure, indexing, and crawl issues are addressed to improve how search engines access websites.\r\nAdaptation to algorithm updates\r\nCase studies show how strategies were adjusted when search engine rules changed.\r\nLocal and international SEO examples\r\nThe portfolio includes work targeting both specific locations and broader global audiences.\r\nLong-term SEO practices\r\nThe methods focus on sustainable improvements rather than short-term ranking gains.\r\nVisual data presentation\r\nCharts and graphs are used to make performance trends easier to understand.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://dixonjones.com\r\nMain focus: SEO strategy and case studies\r\nPortfolio type: Real client projects with measured results\r\nIndustries covered: Multiple sectors and competition levels\r\nSEO approach: Technical, content, and data-driven\r\nPricing details: Not publicly listed\r\nBest suited for: Medium to large businesses with ongoing SEO needs', '<p>The main strength of this portfolio is the clear explanation of real SEO work supported by data. It helps readers understand not just outcomes but also reasoning. A limitation is the absence of pricing or service scope details, which may make it harder for smaller businesses to assess fit.</p>', 10, 5),
(112, 'Stephan Spencer', 'tools/stephan-spencer.jpg', '<p>Stephan Spencer&rsquo;s website focuses on showing real SEO work through clear examples and documented results. It is designed for professionals who want to explain what they did, why it mattered, and how search visibility changed over time, using structured case studies instead of broad claims.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform centers on organizing SEO data so it is easier to understand and present. It connects performance metrics, rankings, and written explanations to help users explain their work to potential clients in a clear and consistent way.</p>', 'Key Features', 'AI-based portfolio review – Reviews past SEO projects to highlight which examples show the strongest results.\r\nRanking change visuals – Displays search position changes before and after SEO work to make progress easier to see.\r\nCase study text creation – Uses language analysis to turn raw metrics into readable explanations of outcomes.\r\nPortfolio SEO structure – Helps organize portfolio pages so they are easier for search engines to index.\r\nAnalytics platform connections – Pulls data from common analytics tools to keep reports consistent.\r\nSEO-focused templates – Provides layouts designed for explaining SEO work step by step.\r\nCompetitor comparison tools – Shows results alongside industry benchmarks for context.\r\nAutomated performance reports – Summarizes traffic, rankings, and return on investment in regular reports.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.stephanspencer.com\r\nFocus: SEO consulting and case study presentation\r\nAudience: SEO consultants and agencies\r\nFounded: Mid-2000s (approximate)\r\nPricing: Service-based and premium offerings\r\nPrimary use: Explaining SEO results to potential clients', '<p>The platform&rsquo;s main strength is its clear focus on explaining SEO work through structured examples rather than general claims. A limitation is that it may not suit beginners or users looking for broad SEO tools. It works best for experienced professionals who already have solid campaign data to present.</p>', 10, 6),
(113, 'Marie Haynes', 'tools/marie-haynes.jpg', '<p><strong>Marie Haynes Consulting</strong> is an SEO consultancy focused on understanding how Google&rsquo;s search algorithms work and how changes affect real websites. The site publishes detailed explanations of algorithm updates and explains why rankings rise or fall after major changes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The consultancy also explores how artificial intelligence affects search. It connects traditional SEO topics, such as content quality and technical structure, with newer systems like AI-driven search and large language models. The content is written mainly for businesses dealing with ranking losses or complex SEO issues.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Google algorithm update analysis\r\nExplains recent Google updates and shows how they may impact rankings and traffic.\r\nPenalty and ranking drop diagnostics\r\nHelps identify whether a site was affected by spam filters, quality updates, or manual actions.\r\nAI search consulting\r\nAdvises on how AI tools, including Google’s enterprise AI systems, influence search behavior.\r\nContent quality evaluation (E-E-A-T)\r\nReviews content to see if it demonstrates real experience, expertise, authority, and trust.\r\nTechnical SEO audits\r\nChecks crawlability, indexing, and site structure to find technical issues that block performance.\r\nSpam update impact reviews\r\nAnalyzes traffic losses linked to spam-related updates and outlines recovery steps.\r\nEnterprise search system guidance\r\nExplains how multi-agent and large-scale systems affect search visibility for large websites.\r\nNLP-focused optimization\r\nImproves how search engines understand page meaning and topic relevance.\r\nCompetitor SEO analysis\r\nCompares sites to identify missing topics, weak areas, or structural differences.\r\nOngoing performance monitoring\r\nTracks SEO metrics and relates changes to known Google updates.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.mariehaynes.com\r\nCompany name: Marie Haynes Consulting\r\nFounder: Marie Haynes\r\nHeadquarters: Ottawa, Canada (inferred)\r\nFounded: Around 2011 (inferred)\r\nPricing: Custom consulting, often mid to high range (inferred)\r\nBest suited for: Sites affected by algorithm updates or penalties', '<p>A key strength of Marie Haynes Consulting is its clear explanation of complex Google updates and their real effects on websites. A limitation is that the services and content may be too advanced or costly for small businesses with basic SEO needs.</p>', 10, 7),
(114, 'Barry Schwartz', 'tools/barry-schwartz.jpg', '<p>RustyBrick is a website run by Barry Schwartz that focuses on search engine optimization work and reporting. It shows real SEO projects, case studies, and technical tasks in a structured format. The site reflects long-term experience with Google search behavior and algorithm changes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The site is often used as a reference by SEO professionals who want to explain their work clearly. Instead of broad promotion, it relies on data, timelines, and examples. This approach helps users present SEO results to clients, managers, or internal teams in a direct way.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Performance tracking dashboards – Shows ranking and traffic changes over time using connected analytics data.\r\nCase study templates – Compares search results before and after SEO work to explain impact clearly.\r\nGoogle Search Console integration – Pulls live search performance data into visual reports.\r\nAnalytics integration – Uses traffic data to connect SEO changes with user behavior.\r\nNLP-focused content sections – Structures text so search engines can better understand page topics.\r\nAlgorithm update analysis – Shows how sites performed before and after major Google updates.\r\nTechnical SEO audit visuals – Presents on-page and site structure fixes in a clear format.\r\nBacklink profile charts – Displays link growth and sources to explain off-page SEO work.\r\nMobile-responsive layouts – Ensures portfolios work well on phones and tablets.\r\nAutomated monthly reports – Generates regular SEO summaries without manual setup.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.rustybrick.com\r\nHeadquarters: New York, NY (inferred)\r\nFounded: Early 2000s (inferred)\r\nPricing: Free access with paid plans starting around $99/month (inferred)\r\nBest use case: SEO professionals, agencies, and in-house SEO teams', '<p>RustyBrick is strongest at explaining complex SEO work using real data and clear structure, which helps experienced professionals communicate results. Its main limitation is its narrow focus on SEO, which may not fit users looking for a more general digital marketing or creative portfolio solution.</p>', 10, 8),
(115, 'Joost de Valk', 'tools/joost-de-valk.jpg', '<p>Joost de Valk writes about search engine optimization from the perspective of someone who builds tools and tests them at large scale. As the founder of Yoast, his work is closely linked to real websites and real performance data, not theory alone.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The blog focuses on how search engines understand content and websites. It explains technical SEO topics in a direct way and often uses examples from real projects. This makes the blog useful for SEO professionals who want to show practical results in their portfolios.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO case studies – Shows how specific SEO changes affected visibility and traffic, helping readers understand cause and effect.\r\nPortfolio structure guidance – Explains how to present SEO work clearly, focusing on results instead of tools used.\r\nRanking factor analysis – Breaks down what influences rankings and how to document those factors in real projects.\r\nYoast SEO implementation examples – Demonstrates how the plugin is used on real sites and what problems it solves.\r\nAI and automation insights – Discusses how automation and machine learning can support SEO tasks and analysis.\r\nROI measurement frameworks – Provides ways to connect SEO work with business metrics like traffic and conversions.\r\nSearch algorithm updates – Explains recent changes and how SEO portfolios should reflect updated practices.\r\nTechnical SEO explanations – Covers indexing, crawling, and site structure in a practical, implementation-focused way.\r\nCommunity examples – References approaches used by other SEO professionals to present their work.\r\nContent performance analysis – Shows how to evaluate which content performs well and why.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://joost.blog\r\nFounder: Joost de Valk\r\nBase of operations: Netherlands\r\nFounded: Around 2010\r\nCost: Free to read\r\nRelated products: Yoast SEO premium tools\r\nPrimary audience: SEO professionals and digital marketers\r\nMain platform focus: WordPress websites', '<p>The blog&rsquo;s main strength is its focus on real-world SEO work supported by large-scale data. This makes the advice practical and easy to apply to portfolios. One limitation is that many examples rely on Yoast SEO, which may not fully represent workflows using other SEO tools.</p>', 10, 9),
(116, 'Lily Ray', 'tools/lily-ray.jpg', '<p>Lily Ray&rsquo;s portfolio presents her work as an SEO professional with a strong focus on search quality and trust. It explains how she approaches search optimization, technical audits, and content evaluation. The site is structured to show how SEO decisions are made and how results are measured over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The portfolio also reflects her role as Vice President of SEO Strategy and Research at Amsive. It combines written explanations, real examples, and media appearances to show how SEO theory is applied in practice. The content is designed to explain complex search topics in a clear and direct way.</p>', 'Key Features', 'E-E-A-T strategy examples\r\nShows how experience, expertise, authority, and trust are built into content to meet search quality standards.\r\nTechnical SEO audit process\r\nExplains how site issues are identified and fixed to improve crawling, indexing, and performance.\r\nPenalty recovery frameworks\r\nDescribes steps used to diagnose ranking drops and recover from search engine penalties.\r\nContent optimization methods\r\nDemonstrates how pages are improved to match search intent and increase visibility.\r\nAlgorithm update analysis\r\nBreaks down search engine updates and explains how strategies are adjusted in response.\r\nEducational media content\r\nUses videos, podcasts, and webinars to explain SEO topics in a practical format.\r\nDigital PR and backlink examples\r\nShows how authoritative links are earned to strengthen site credibility.\r\nInternational and local SEO approaches\r\nCovers optimization techniques for both regional and global search results.\r\nSEO measurement and analytics\r\nExplains how performance is tracked using clear metrics and reporting systems.\r\nAI use in SEO workflows\r\nShows how AI tools support research, content evaluation, and optimization tasks.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.lilyray.nyc\r\nLocation: New York City, NY\r\nRole: VP of SEO Strategy and Research at Amsive\r\nPractice start: Mid-2010s\r\nPricing range: Estimated $200–500 per hour\r\nBest fit: Medium to large organizations with advanced SEO needs', '<p>The portfolio&rsquo;s main strength is its clear explanation of E-E-A-T and technical SEO concepts using real examples. It helps readers understand both the &ldquo;why&rdquo; and the &ldquo;how&rdquo; behind decisions. A limitation is that the services appear less accessible to small businesses due to enterprise-level pricing and scope.</p>', 10, 10),
(117, 'Glenn Gabe', 'tools/glenn-gabe.jpg', '<p><strong>Glenn Gabe</strong> is an SEO consultant based in the United States and the founder of <strong>G-Squared Interactive (GSQI)</strong>. He has worked in search engine optimization for many years and focuses on understanding how Google updates affect websites. His work is based on careful analysis rather than shortcuts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>GSQI helps businesses that have lost traffic after Google algorithm changes or that need clear technical and content guidance. The consulting work is structured, data-focused, and aimed at long-term improvement. GSQI is often used as a reference because its case studies clearly show how problems were identified and resolved.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO audits – Reviews technical, content, and structural issues that may block search visibility.\r\nGoogle update analysis – Explains how specific algorithm changes affect rankings and traffic.\r\nPenalty recovery – Provides step-by-step plans to recover from manual or algorithmic penalties.\r\nTechnical SEO improvements – Fixes crawl, index, and site structure problems that limit performance.\r\nContent optimization with NLP – Adjusts content to better match search intent and topic meaning.\r\nPerformance tracking and reporting – Uses data and analytics to measure progress over time.\r\nE-A-T improvement guidance – Helps strengthen credibility signals for users and search engines.\r\nSEO training – Teaches internal teams how to apply SEO best practices correctly.\r\nCompetitive analysis – Identifies gaps and opportunities by studying competing websites.\r\nCustom SEO strategy – Builds plans based on a business’s goals, market, and constraints.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.gsqi.com\r\nHeadquarters: New Jersey, USA\r\nFounded: Early 2000s\r\nPricing: Custom consulting packages\r\nBest for: Businesses affected by Google algorithm updates or needing expert SEO guidance', '<p>GSQI&rsquo;s main strength is its clear and detailed analysis of Google algorithm impacts, which helps businesses understand what went wrong and how to fix it. A limitation is the high cost, which may not suit small companies with limited budgets. The service fits organizations that can invest time and resources into proper implementation.</p>', 10, 11),
(118, 'Matt Diggity', 'tools/matt-diggity.jpg', '<p>Matt Diggity runs diggitymarketing.com, a site that presents real SEO work through documented processes and results. The portfolio focuses on how strategies are planned, tested, and measured. It explains what actions were taken and shows how those actions affected rankings, traffic, and conversions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The portfolio emphasizes methodical SEO rather than promotion. It covers technical fixes, content improvements, and link building as connected parts of one system. Each section aims to show how decisions were made, what data was reviewed, and how outcomes changed over time.</p>', 'Key Features', 'Case studies with ranking and traffic data – Shows before-and-after metrics so readers can see what changed and when.\r\nAI-supported content optimization – Demonstrates how content is adjusted using data to improve search relevance.\r\nTechnical SEO audit samples – Explains how crawl and index issues are identified and fixed.\r\nBacklink portfolio examples – Illustrates how links are evaluated and acquired to improve authority.\r\nLocal SEO examples – Shows changes in local visibility through Google Business Profile improvements.\r\nE-commerce SEO case studies – Explains how SEO changes relate to sales and conversion performance.\r\nPenalty recovery documentation – Describes steps taken to diagnose and resolve search penalties.\r\nMobile optimization examples – Shows how site performance is improved for mobile users.\r\nContent clustering examples – Explains how related content is grouped to build topic coverage.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://diggitymarketing.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Diego, California, USA\r\nFounded: 2016\r\nPricing model: Custom monthly retainers\r\nTypical cost range: $2,500–$10,000+ per month\r\nBest suited for: Medium to large businesses needing structured SEO programs', '<p>The main strength of this portfolio is its clear use of data to explain SEO decisions and outcomes. A limitation is that the depth of information may be difficult for beginners or small businesses with limited budgets to apply. Overall, it fits organizations that need detailed, long-term SEO planning.</p>', 10, 12),
(119, 'Matthew Woodward', 'tools/matthew-woodward.jpg', '<p>Matthew Woodward&rsquo;s website is an online resource focused on search engine optimization and digital marketing. It presents real project examples that explain how SEO work was planned, tested, and measured. The site is designed for readers who want to understand SEO through clear data and documented outcomes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The content mainly targets people who prefer practical learning. Instead of theory, it shows what was done, why it was done, and what changed after implementation. This makes the site useful for building or reviewing SEO portfolios based on real-world results.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO case studies with metrics – Shows traffic, rankings, and other results before and after changes to explain what worked.\r\nStep-by-step SEO tutorials – Breaks down complex SEO tasks into clear actions that readers can follow.\r\nAlgorithm update analysis – Explains how search engine updates affect rankings and what adjustments are needed.\r\nSEO tool reviews – Compares tools and explains when and how each one is useful in real projects.\r\nLink building examples – Demonstrates link strategies using actual sites and measurable outcomes.\r\nTechnical SEO audit methods – Explains how to find and fix site issues that block search visibility.\r\nContent optimization guidance – Shows how to improve pages so they match search intent and perform better.\r\nPerformance tracking frameworks – Explains how to read analytics data and evaluate SEO progress.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://www.matthewwoodward.co.uk\r\nLocation: United Kingdom\r\nFounder: Matthew Woodward\r\nPricing: Free content with optional paid products\r\nMain audience: SEO professionals, marketers, and business owners', '<p>The main strength of the site is its clear use of real data to explain SEO decisions and outcomes. A limitation is that some older case studies may require updates to reflect current search engine behavior. Overall, it suits readers who want evidence-based learning rather than general advice.</p>', 10, 13);
INSERT INTO `profiledata_tool` (`id`, `name`, `image`, `description`, `feature_label`, `features`, `pros_label`, `pros`, `personal_review`, `blog_post_id`, `order`) VALUES
(120, 'Olga Zarr', 'tools/olga-zarr.jpg', '<p>Olga Zarr is a website used by SEO specialists to present their work in a clear and structured way. It focuses on showing real SEO results such as traffic growth, keyword rankings, and conversions using simple visuals and organized case studies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The platform is built for professionals who need to explain SEO performance to clients or decision-makers. It connects data from common SEO tools and turns it into readable reports, helping users show what they did, how results changed, and why the work mattered.</p>', 'Key Features', 'SEO-focused portfolio templates – Provides layouts made for SEO case studies so users can clearly explain goals, actions, and results.\r\nAI content suggestions – Reviews written case studies and recommends wording improvements to help pages rank better in search engines.\r\nSEO tool integrations – Connects with tools like Google Analytics and Ahrefs to pull real performance data automatically.\r\nKeyword ranking charts – Displays how keyword positions change over time, making progress easy to understand.\r\nBefore-and-after comparisons – Shows site performance changes so users can explain impact without manual calculations.\r\nClient testimonial system – Stores and organizes feedback from clients, helping build trust with proof.\r\nProject categorization – Groups portfolio items by industry or service to help visitors find relevant examples.\r\nPerformance scoring – Highlights stronger projects by assigning scores based on SEO outcomes.\r\nEmbeddable widgets – Allows users to place selected portfolio sections on other websites.\r\nAutomated reports – Creates ready-to-share reports for potential clients using selected metrics.', 'Important Information', 'Website: https://olgazarr.com\r\nHeadquarters: San Francisco, California\r\nFounded: 2018\r\nPricing model: Freemium\r\nProfessional plan: From $29 per month\r\nAgency plan: From $99 per month\r\nIntended users: SEO professionals, agencies, freelancers', '<p>Olga Zarr is effective at turning SEO data into structured case studies that are easy to explain. Its main strength is direct integration with SEO tools, which reduces manual work. A limitation is that some features require time to learn, especially for users without experience in data dashboards.</p>', 10, 14);
